FROM (VALUES
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Cosmetology is best defined as the science and art of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "manufacturing pharmaceutical drugs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "caring for and beautifying the skin, hair and nails"}, {"id": "c", "text": "treating internal diseases of the body"}, {"id": "d", "text": "designing and sewing fashion garments"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cosmetology is the study and application of beauty treatments for the skin, hair and nails."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','A cosmetologist who specialises in the care and styling of hair is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "manicurist"}, {"id": "b", "text": "esthetician"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hairdresser or hairstylist"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dermatologist"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A hairdresser or hairstylist specialises in cutting, styling and treating hair."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','The branch of cosmetology that deals mainly with the care of the skin and facial treatments is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "esthetics"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pedicure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "barbering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cosmetic surgery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Esthetics (skin care) focuses on facials, skin treatments and beautifying the skin."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','The care and beautification of the hands and fingernails is known as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "pedicure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "manicure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "massage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "waxing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A manicure is the cosmetic treatment of the hands and fingernails."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which of the following is NOT a branch of cosmetology?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hairdressing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nail technology"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Skin care (esthetics)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Automobile repair"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "Automobile repair is unrelated to the care of skin, hair or nails."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','One major economic importance of studying cosmetology in Nigeria is that it:','[{"id": "a", "text": "provides self-employment and job creation opportunities"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduces the need for personal hygiene"}, {"id": "c", "text": "guarantees admission into medical school"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eliminates the need for electricity in salons"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cosmetology equips learners with skills for self-employment and creates jobs."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','A place where beauty services such as hairdressing, manicure and facials are offered is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "pharmacy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "salon or spa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "clinic laboratory"}, {"id": "d", "text": "boutique"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Beauty salons and spas are the workplaces where cosmetology services are rendered."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Which of the following is a career opportunity available to a trained cosmetologist?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make-up artist"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bricklayer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Welder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Accountant"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A make-up artist is a direct career path in cosmetology."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Good personal grooming by a cosmetologist is important mainly because it:','[{"id": "a", "text": "makes chemicals unnecessary"}, {"id": "b", "text": "attracts and retains clients through a professional image"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increases the price of every service"}, {"id": "d", "text": "removes the need for a work licence"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A well-groomed cosmetologist projects professionalism that builds client confidence."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','A key personal quality that helps a cosmetologist succeed in business is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "rudeness to customers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poor time-keeping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "good communication and customer-care skills"}, {"id": "d", "text": "refusal to learn new styles"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Good communication and customer care build client loyalty and repeat business."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','The tool used to remove tangles and smooth the hair before styling is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "scissors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nail file"}, {"id": "d", "text": "spatula"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A comb is used to detangle and part hair before styling."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','Which tool is used to trim and shape the fingernails during a manicure?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hair clipper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nail cutter and emery board"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Curling tongs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Facial steamer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nail cutter trims the nail while the emery board files it to shape."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','A heated tool used to create curls or waves in the hair is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "a hair dryer hood"}, {"id": "b", "text": "curling tongs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a tweezer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a mixing bowl"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Curling tongs (curling iron) apply heat to form curls and waves."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','The instrument used to pluck or shape the eyebrows is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "tweezer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "scissors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rat-tail comb"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sponge"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tweezers grip and remove individual hairs to shape the eyebrows."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','During a facial, a small flat tool used to lift cream or mask from a container is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "spatula"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clipper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "roller"}, {"id": "d", "text": "curler"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A spatula is used to scoop cosmetic products hygienically from their containers."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','In a salon, which of the following is classified as equipment rather than a hand tool?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scissors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hooded hair dryer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Nail file"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A hooded hair dryer is a large, powered appliance, classifying it as equipment."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Which of the following is a consumable material used up during a service?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton wool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pair of scissors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Styling chair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hair dryer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cotton wool is a consumable that is used up and replaced regularly."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Shampoo, relaxer cream and nail polish are best described as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "equipment"}, {"id": "b", "text": "materials or supplies"}, {"id": "c", "text": "furniture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hand tools"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "These are consumable materials or supplies applied during services."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Which item is best classified as salon furniture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Shampoo bottle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Styling chair and mirror"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Emery board"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hair spray"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A styling chair and mirror are fixed furnishings of the salon."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Proper storage of cosmetology tools after use is important mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase their weight"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep them clean, safe and prolong their lifespan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change their colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make them heavier to lift"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Correct storage keeps tools hygienic, prevents damage and extends their useful life."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','The complete destruction of all microorganisms, including their spores, on an instrument is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "sanitation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sterilisation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ventilation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lubrication"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sterilisation destroys all microbial life, including bacterial spores."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','Washing the hands with soap and water before attending to a client is an example of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "sterilisation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "personal hygiene and sanitation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fumigation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "styling"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Handwashing is a basic personal-hygiene and sanitation practice."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','Which chemical is commonly used to disinfect combs and other salon tools?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vegetable oil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Methylated spirit or a disinfectant solution"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Table salt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sugar syrup"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Methylated spirit and disinfectant solutions kill germs on salon tools."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','The main reason for disinfecting tools between clients is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "make the tools sharper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent the spread of infection from one client to another"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add fragrance to the tools"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase the salon''s rent"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Disinfection prevents cross-infection between clients."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','A closed cabinet that uses ultraviolet light to keep sanitised tools germ-free is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "UV sterilising cabinet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "refrigerator"}, {"id": "c", "text": "microwave oven"}, {"id": "d", "text": "water heater"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A UV sterilising cabinet keeps cleaned tools sanitary until use."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O2','Before applying a chemical relaxer, a patch or skin test is done to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "check the client''s blood group"}, {"id": "b", "text": "detect possible allergic reaction to the product"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure the length of the hair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "count the strands of hair"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A patch test reveals whether the client is allergic to the chemical."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O2','If a chemical relaxer accidentally enters a client''s eye, the first action should be to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "rub the eye vigorously with a towel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rinse the eye immediately with plenty of clean water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "apply more relaxer to neutralise it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ignore it and continue working"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Immediate flushing with clean water dilutes and removes the chemical."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O2','To protect the hands when applying chemicals such as relaxers or dyes, a cosmetologist should wear:','[{"id": "a", "text": "woollen mittens"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rubber or latex gloves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cotton socks"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nothing at all"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rubber or latex gloves protect the skin from harsh chemicals."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O2','The safest way to handle electrical salon equipment is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "operate it with wet hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep hands dry and check cords for damage before use"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pull the plug out by the cord"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leave it switched on overnight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dry hands and undamaged cords prevent electric shock and fire."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O2','A first-aid box in the salon is important because it is used to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "store hair products for sale"}, {"id": "b", "text": "give immediate treatment for minor cuts and burns"}, {"id": "c", "text": "keep money safe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "display cosmetics to clients"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A first-aid box provides immediate care for minor injuries such as cuts and burns."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O1','The outermost layer of the human skin is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "dermis"}, {"id": "b", "text": "epidermis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "subcutaneous layer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "muscle layer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The epidermis is the visible, outermost layer of the skin."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O1','Which of the following is a major function of the skin?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pumping blood round the body"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Protecting the body against germs and injury"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Digesting food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Producing bile"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The skin forms a protective barrier against germs, injury and water loss."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O1','The skin type that produces excess oil and often appears shiny is described as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "dry skin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "oily skin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "normal skin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "chapped skin"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oily skin has overactive sebaceous glands, giving a shiny appearance."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O1','The pigment that gives the skin its colour and protects it from the sun is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "melanin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keratin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "insulin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "haemoglobin"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Melanin gives skin its colour and shields it from ultraviolet radiation."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O1','Sweat is released onto the skin surface through the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "sweat (sudoriferous) glands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tear ducts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "salivary glands"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kidneys"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sweat glands (sudoriferous glands) secrete sweat to cool the body."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O2','The visible part of the hair that projects above the skin is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "hair root"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hair shaft"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hair follicle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hair bulb"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The hair shaft is the portion of hair seen above the scalp."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O2','The main protein that makes up hair and nails is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "collagen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keratin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "albumin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "casein"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hair and nails are made largely of the tough protein keratin."}',0.6,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O2','The main purpose of shampooing the hair is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "add permanent colour to the hair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clean the hair and scalp of dirt and excess oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the hair grow taller instantly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "straighten the hair permanently"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Shampoo cleanses the hair and scalp of dirt, sweat and excess sebum."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O2','Applying conditioner after shampooing helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "remove the natural colour of the hair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "soften, moisturise and make the hair easier to comb"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dry out the scalp completely"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase dandruff"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Conditioner moisturises and detangles hair, improving manageability."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T4','BTC-T4-O2','A good practice for keeping the nails healthy is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "bite them regularly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep them clean, trimmed and well moisturised"}, {"id": "c", "text": "use them to open tins"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leave dirt under them"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clean, trimmed and moisturised nails stay healthy and resist breakage."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O1','A cosmetic product applied to the face to even out skin tone and provide a base for make-up is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "foundation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shampoo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nail hardener"}, {"id": "d", "text": "relaxer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Foundation creates an even base and smooths skin tone before other make-up."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O1','Which product is applied to the lips to add colour during make-up?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mascara"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lipstick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Eyeshadow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blusher"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Lipstick adds colour and definition to the lips."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O1','Mascara is a make-up product used mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "darken and lengthen the eyelashes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "colour the fingernails"}, {"id": "c", "text": "moisturise the hands"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wash the hair"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mascara coats the eyelashes to make them darker, longer and fuller."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O1','Before applying make-up, the face should first be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "cleansed and toned"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rubbed with hair relaxer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "left dirty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "covered with nail polish"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cleansing and toning prepare a clean surface for smooth make-up application."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O1','A product used to remove make-up from the face at the end of the day is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "cleanser or make-up remover"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hair spray"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nail polish"}, {"id": "d", "text": "perfume"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A cleanser or make-up remover dissolves and lifts make-up from the skin."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O2','Keeping a record of daily sales and expenses in a salon is important because it helps the owner to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "know the profit or loss of the business"}, {"id": "b", "text": "change the colour of the walls"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid buying any materials"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stop serving customers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Records of sales and expenses reveal whether the business is making profit or loss."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O2','The best way to attract and keep loyal customers in a salon is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "provide good service and treat clients politely"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep the salon dirty"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ignore clients'' complaints"}, {"id": "d", "text": "delay every appointment"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Quality service and courteous treatment build customer loyalty and referrals."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O2','Money set aside to start and run a salon business is known as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "capital"}, {"id": "b", "text": "profit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loss"}, {"id": "d", "text": "debt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Capital is the money invested to establish and operate a business."}',0.55,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O2','When a customer complains about a service, the professional response is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "listen calmly and try to resolve the problem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shout at the customer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "send the customer away"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ignore the complaint completely"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Listening calmly and resolving complaints protects the salon''s reputation."}',0.5,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','BTC','BTC-T5','BTC-T5-O2','Advertising a salon''s services on radio, posters or social media is done mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "attract more customers and increase sales"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduce the number of clients"}, {"id": "c", "text": "waste the owner''s money"}, {"id": "d", "text": "close down the business"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Advertising creates awareness that draws customers and boosts sales."}',0.45,'{SSS1,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O1','Which tool is most suitable for removing the tiny cross-head screws that hold a smartphone casing together?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Claw hammer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Precision Phillips screwdriver"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wire stripper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hacksaw"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Phone casings use very small cross-head screws that need a precision Phillips screwdriver."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O1','A GSM technician needs to gently pry open the glued back cover of a phone without cracking it. Which tool should be used?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flat metal spudger or plastic opening pick"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cold chisel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pipe wrench"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Soldering iron"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A spudger or plastic pick separates glued covers without scratching or cracking the housing."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O1','Which instrument is used to measure voltage, current and resistance on a phone or computer circuit board?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Multimeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vernier caliper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spirit level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Micrometer screw gauge"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A multimeter measures voltage, current and resistance for electronic fault-finding."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O1','The hot-air rework station is mainly used in GSM repair to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charge the phone battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Remove and refit surface-mount components and ICs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clean the phone screen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Test network signal strength"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hot-air rework stations blow controlled hot air to desolder and resolder SMD parts and ICs."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O1','Which tool is used to hold and steady a phone board firmly while a technician works on it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "PCB holder or bench vice"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tweezers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Torch light"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Anti-static bag"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A PCB holder (board clamp) grips the circuit board steady during repair."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','Why should a technician wear an anti-static wrist strap when handling computer components?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To prevent electrostatic discharge from damaging the components"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To make the hands warmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To increase the speed of the computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To measure the current in the board"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The wrist strap safely drains static charge, preventing ESD damage to sensitive chips."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','Before opening a desktop computer system unit for repair, the FIRST safety step is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Unplug it from the mains power supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Remove the hard disk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Format the operating system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Spray water on the motherboard"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Disconnecting mains power first protects the technician from electric shock."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','Which fire-fighting device is most appropriate for an electrical fire in a computer workshop?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bucket of water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Carbon dioxide (CO2) or dry-powder extinguisher"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sand only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wet cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "CO2 or dry-powder extinguishers put out electrical fires without conducting current."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','A soldering iron that is switched on but not in use should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Placed flat on the workbench"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Kept in its stand or holder"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dropped into a bowl of water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wrapped in paper"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Resting a hot iron in its stand prevents burns and fire hazards."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','When soldering on a phone board, adequate ventilation is important because:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Solder fumes can be harmful if inhaled"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It makes the solder melt faster"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It cools the phone battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It improves the network signal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flux and solder fumes are toxic, so good ventilation protects the technician''s lungs."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which component is regarded as the ''brain'' of the computer that carries out processing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Central Processing Unit (CPU)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Power supply unit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Optical drive"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cooling fan"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The CPU executes instructions and is considered the brain of the computer."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which type of memory temporarily holds data and programs while the computer is running and loses its content when power is off?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hard disk drive"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Random Access Memory (RAM)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ROM BIOS"}, {"id": "d", "text": "DVD-ROM"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "RAM is volatile memory that holds running data and clears when power is removed."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','The large printed circuit board that connects the CPU, RAM and other components together is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Motherboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Router"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The motherboard is the main board that interconnects all major components."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which unit converts AC mains electricity into the DC voltages used by a desktop computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Graphics card"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Power Supply Unit (PSU)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sound card"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Network card"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The PSU converts AC mains to the low DC voltages the computer needs."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which of these is an output device on a computer system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Scanner"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The monitor displays results, making it an output device."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A desktop computer powers on with fans spinning but shows nothing on the screen and gives repeated beep codes. This most likely indicates a problem with the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "RAM module not properly seated or faulty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mouse"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Printer cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Speaker volume"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Repeated beep codes with no display commonly point to a faulty or loose RAM module."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','When installing a CPU into its socket during assembly, the technician must:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Force it in any direction that fits"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Align pin 1 or the notch correctly before seating it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Apply water to the socket first"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Remove the motherboard battery"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The CPU has an alignment mark that must match the socket to avoid bending pins."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A computer keeps losing the correct date and time each time it is switched off. The most likely cause is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Faulty monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Weak or dead CMOS battery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Broken keyboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Disconnected mouse"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The CMOS battery keeps the clock and BIOS settings; when weak the time resets."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','Applying thermal paste between the CPU and its heat sink during assembly is done to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Improve heat transfer away from the CPU"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the RAM capacity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Speed up the internet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Store extra data"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Thermal paste fills air gaps so heat moves efficiently from CPU to heat sink."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A newly assembled computer does not power on at all and shows no lights or fan movement. The FIRST item to check is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Operating system version"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Power supply connection and switch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Web browser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Printer driver"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "No lights or fans means no power, so the PSU connection and switch are checked first."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','Which of the following is an operating system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Word"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Windows 10"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Google Chrome"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Adobe Photoshop"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Windows 10 is an operating system; the others are application programs."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','The main function of an operating system is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Manage the hardware and software resources of the computer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Print documents only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Send text messages"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Charge the battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The OS manages hardware, software and provides a platform for applications."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','Which utility program is used to remove or quarantine malicious software from a computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Antivirus software"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spreadsheet software"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Media player"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Web browser"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Antivirus utilities detect, remove or quarantine malware."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','Which of these is a popular mobile phone operating system used on many GSM smartphones in Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Android"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Excel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "CorelDRAW"}, {"id": "d", "text": "WinRAR"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Android is a widely used smartphone operating system."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','A disk defragmenter utility is used to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Reorganise fragmented files so the hard disk performs better"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Delete the operating system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the screen brightness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Connect to Wi-Fi"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Defragmentation rearranges scattered file pieces to speed up disk access."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','Before performing a clean installation of an operating system on a used computer, the technician should FIRST:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Back up the user''s important data"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Remove the CPU"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Break the monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Unsolder the RAM"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean install erases the disk, so data must be backed up first."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','A device driver is software that:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Allows the operating system to communicate with a hardware device"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drives the user''s car"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increases the phone''s battery size"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Is used only for playing games"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A driver lets the OS control and communicate with a specific hardware device."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','Which storage medium is commonly used to boot and install a modern Windows operating system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bootable USB flash drive"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Floppy diskette"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Audio cassette"}, {"id": "d", "text": "SIM card"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A bootable USB flash drive is the common medium for installing modern Windows."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','After installing Windows, a device shows a yellow exclamation mark in Device Manager. This usually means:','[{"id": "a", "text": "The correct driver is missing or not properly installed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The computer has too much RAM"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The monitor is off"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The keyboard is Nigerian"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A yellow exclamation mark indicates a missing or faulty device driver."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','To enter the BIOS/UEFI setup so a computer can boot from a USB installer, the user usually:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Presses a specific key such as Del or F2 during startup"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Waits until Windows fully loads"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Removes the hard disk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Types the password in Word"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "BIOS/UEFI is accessed by pressing a setup key like Del or F2 at startup."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','Which component of a GSM phone provides the electrical power to run the phone?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loudspeaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Camera lens"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Vibrator motor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The rechargeable battery supplies power to the phone."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','The section of a GSM phone that handles transmitting and receiving radio signals is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Radio Frequency (RF) section"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Display glass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charging port cover"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Back panel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The RF section transmits and receives the network radio signals."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','In a GSM handset, the small removable card that stores the subscriber''s network identity is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "SIM card"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Graphics card"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sound card"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Credit card"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The SIM (Subscriber Identity Module) stores subscriber and network identity data."}',0.45,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','Which component converts electrical signals into the sound you hear during a phone call held to the ear?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Earpiece speaker"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microphone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Antenna"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The earpiece speaker converts electrical signals into audible sound."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','The IC on a GSM phone board that stores the phone''s operating firmware and user data is broadly known as the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Memory (flash) IC"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Antenna switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Screen protector"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The flash/memory IC holds the phone firmware and stored data."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A phone shows ''No Service'' or cannot find any network even with a good SIM. The fault is most likely in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Network/RF and antenna section"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Earpiece speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Vibrator motor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Camera flash"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Network reception faults point to the RF/antenna section of the phone."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A phone does not respond at all and does not charge or power on. A good first diagnostic step is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Test the battery and charging voltage with a DC power supply/multimeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Replace the SIM card immediately"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change the ringtone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Update the wallpaper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Checking battery and charging voltage confirms whether power is reaching the board."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A customer complains that callers cannot hear them, though they hear the caller clearly. The likely faulty component is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microphone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Earpiece speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Display"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "If the caller cannot hear the user, the microphone is likely faulty."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A phone''s touch screen shows a normal display but does not respond to touch. The most likely faulty part is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Touch digitizer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loudspeaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "SIM tray"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Charging cable"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clear display with no touch response indicates a faulty touch digitizer."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','When a phone gets very hot and drains quickly while charging, a wise safety-first diagnostic action is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Suspect a faulty battery or charging IC and stop charging to inspect"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ignore it and keep charging overnight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pour water on the phone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the screen brightness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Overheating while charging suggests a bad battery or charging IC and charging should stop."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','In electronic soldering, flux is used mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clean the joint and help the solder flow and bond well"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the phone''s memory"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charge the battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cool the soldering iron"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flux removes oxides and improves solder wetting for a good joint."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A good soldered joint on a phone board should appear:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Shiny, smooth and cone-shaped"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Dull, cracked and lumpy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Black and burnt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wet with water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A quality solder joint is shiny, smooth and well-formed, not dull or cracked."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A phone does not charge and shows nothing when a known-good charger is connected. A logical first check is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charging port (connector) for dirt, damage or dry solder"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ringtone volume"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wallpaper setting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Camera resolution"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A dirty, loose or damaged charging port is a common cause of no-charging faults."}',0.6,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','Which material is applied to remove excess solder from a joint or pad?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Desoldering braid (solder wick)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Candle wax"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Groundnut oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sand paper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Desoldering braid soaks up molten solder to clear excess from pads."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','The IC on the phone board that controls and regulates the charging of the battery is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charging IC"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Audio IC"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Camera IC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Display IC"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The charging IC manages and regulates current flowing into the battery."}',0.55,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','When a customer brings in a faulty phone, the FIRST professional action a technician should take is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Record the phone details, fault complaint and give a job/receipt ticket"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Open the phone immediately without any note"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sell the phone to another customer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Delete all the customer''s data at once"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Logging the device, fault and issuing a receipt protects both technician and customer."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Keeping a proper repair job record (log book) in a workshop is important because it helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Track jobs, avoid disputes and manage warranties"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the phone''s signal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charge the battery faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Replace the need for tools"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Records track jobs, reduce disputes and support warranty claims."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Good customer-service practice before starting a paid repair is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Give the customer a clear cost estimate and agree on it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hide the price and charge anything later"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Refuse to talk to the customer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Damage the phone deliberately"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Agreeing a clear estimate upfront builds trust and avoids payment disputes."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','A customer''s personal data and contacts on a phone under repair should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Kept private and confidential by the technician"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Shared publicly on social media"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sold to advertisers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sent to the technician''s friends"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Respecting customer privacy and confidentiality is a professional and ethical duty."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Offering a reasonable warranty period after a repair mainly helps the technician to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Build customer confidence and encourage repeat business"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Avoid ever fixing phones again"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the phone''s RAM"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reduce the network coverage"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A warranty reassures customers and encourages loyalty and referrals."}',0.5,'{SSS1,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','Which of the following best defines data?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Processed facts ready for decision making"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Raw, unprocessed facts and figures"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A printed report from a computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A trained staff member''s opinion"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Data refers to raw, unprocessed facts and figures before they are given meaning."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','A shopkeeper records the daily sales figures and later uses them to produce a monthly profit summary. The monthly summary is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "data"}, {"id": "b", "text": "raw input"}, {"id": "c", "text": "information"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a data source"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The processed, meaningful summary used for decisions is information."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','Which of the following is an attribute of good information?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It is always expensive"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It is relevant, accurate and timely"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It is stored only on paper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It is never shared"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good information must be relevant, accurate, complete and timely to be useful."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','A student''s raw examination scores of 45, 60 and 72 are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "information"}, {"id": "b", "text": "data"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a report"}, {"id": "d", "text": "knowledge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Individual raw scores that have not yet been summarised are data."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','The main difference between data and information is that information','[{"id": "a", "text": "has been processed and given meaning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "is always numeric"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cannot be stored on a computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "is collected before data"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Information is data that has been processed to become meaningful and useful."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','The three main stages of the data processing cycle are','[{"id": "a", "text": "input, processing and output"}, {"id": "b", "text": "typing, saving and printing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "coding, testing and debugging"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reading, writing and storing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The data processing cycle consists of input, processing and output stages."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','In a computerised WAEC result system, entering candidates'' scores into the computer represents which stage of the data processing cycle?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Output"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Processing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Input"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Storage"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Entering data into the computer for processing is the input stage."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','Which activity is carried out during the processing stage of the data cycle?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Collecting forms from candidates"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Calculating, sorting and summarising the data"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Printing the final result slip"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Distributing results to schools"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Processing involves calculations, sorting, classifying and summarising the input data."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','The stage of the data processing cycle that produces a printed result slip for a candidate is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "input stage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "collection stage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "output stage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "verification stage"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The output stage delivers the processed information, such as a printed result slip."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','Storing processed results so they can be retrieved later is best described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "input"}, {"id": "b", "text": "storage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "processing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "collection"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Keeping data or information for future retrieval is the storage activity."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','Using an abacus or the fingers to count goods in a market is an example of which method of data processing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Electronic method"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Manual method"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mechanical method"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Automatic method"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Processing done by hand or simple aids like the abacus is the manual method."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','Which of the following is an advantage of electronic data processing over the manual method?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It is slower but cheaper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It is fast and highly accurate for large volumes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It never requires electricity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It cannot store data"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Electronic processing handles large data volumes quickly and accurately."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','A typewriter and a mechanical adding machine belong to which method of data processing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Manual method"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Electronic method"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mechanical method"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Digital method"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Machines with moving mechanical parts, like typewriters, use the mechanical method."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','A major disadvantage of the manual method of data processing is that it is','[{"id": "a", "text": "too fast for humans"}, {"id": "b", "text": "slow and prone to errors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "impossible without a computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "always more accurate"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Manual processing is slow and error-prone, especially with large volumes."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','A modern Nigerian bank that processes millions of transactions daily most likely uses which method of data processing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Manual method"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mechanical method"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Electronic method"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hand-tally method"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "High-volume banking relies on fast, accurate electronic data processing."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Which of these is regarded as the earliest counting device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Slide rule"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Abacus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Napier''s bones"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pascaline"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The abacus is widely regarded as the earliest known counting device."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','The mechanical adding machine invented by Blaise Pascal is known as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Analytical Engine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pascaline"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Abacus"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Difference Engine"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Blaise Pascal invented the Pascaline, an early mechanical calculator."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Charles Babbage is remembered in the history of computing as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "father of the computer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "inventor of the abacus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "father of the internet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "inventor of the transistor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Charles Babbage designed the Analytical Engine and is called the father of the computer."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','The main electronic component used in first-generation computers was the','[{"id": "a", "text": "transistor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "integrated circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vacuum tube"}, {"id": "d", "text": "microprocessor"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "First-generation computers used vacuum tubes as their main components."}',0.6,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','The technology that characterises fourth-generation computers is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "vacuum tube"}, {"id": "b", "text": "transistor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "microprocessor (VLSI)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mechanical gear"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Fourth-generation computers are built around the microprocessor using VLSI technology."}',0.65,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','Which of the following is an input device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keyboard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Printer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Speaker"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The keyboard sends data into the computer, making it an input device."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','A device used to produce a permanent copy of a document on paper is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "scanner"}, {"id": "b", "text": "printer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "monitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mouse"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A printer produces hard (permanent) copies on paper as an output device."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','Which device is used to capture a printed photograph and convert it into a digital image for the computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plotter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scanner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Projector"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Monitor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A scanner captures printed images and converts them into digital form, acting as input."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','The monitor, printer and speaker are grouped together because they are all','[{"id": "a", "text": "input devices"}, {"id": "b", "text": "storage devices"}, {"id": "c", "text": "output devices"}, {"id": "d", "text": "processing devices"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "These devices deliver results from the computer, so they are output devices."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','Which of the following is BOTH commonly classified as an input and an output device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Touch screen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Light pen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Joystick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Barcode reader"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A touch screen both displays output and accepts input, so it serves both roles."}',0.65,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The part of the computer often called the brain of the system is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "monitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Central Processing Unit (CPU)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hard disk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "keyboard"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The CPU carries out processing and control and is called the brain of the computer."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','Which unit of the CPU performs addition, subtraction and logical comparisons?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Control Unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Arithmetic and Logic Unit (ALU)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Main memory"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Register file"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The ALU handles arithmetic operations and logical comparisons."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','RAM is described as volatile memory because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "cannot be written to"}, {"id": "b", "text": "loses its contents when power is switched off"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stores data permanently"}, {"id": "d", "text": "is only found in printers"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "RAM is volatile because its contents are lost once power is removed."}',0.6,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','Which of the following is a secondary (backing) storage device?','[{"id": "a", "text": "RAM"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cache"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hard disk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Register"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The hard disk is a secondary storage device that holds data permanently."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The unit within the CPU that directs and coordinates the operations of the computer is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Arithmetic and Logic Unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Control Unit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Main memory"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Output unit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Control Unit directs and coordinates all activities within the computer."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Which of the following is an example of system software?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Word"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Windows operating system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "CorelDRAW"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Microsoft Excel"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The operating system is system software that manages the computer''s resources."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','A program written to perform a specific user task such as typing letters is classified as','[{"id": "a", "text": "system software"}, {"id": "b", "text": "application software"}, {"id": "c", "text": "firmware"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a device driver"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Software that performs specific user tasks is application software."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Which of the following is an application software package used for calculations and charts in a spreadsheet?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Linux"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Excel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "MS-DOS"}, {"id": "d", "text": "BIOS"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Microsoft Excel is a spreadsheet application used for calculations and charts."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','A utility program that scans a computer for and removes malicious programs is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "a word processor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "an antivirus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a compiler"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a spreadsheet"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An antivirus is a utility that detects and removes malicious software."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','The set of programs that controls and coordinates the overall operation of a computer is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "application software"}, {"id": "b", "text": "system software"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spreadsheet software"}, {"id": "d", "text": "presentation software"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "System software controls and coordinates overall computer operations."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Which of the following is a function of an operating system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Designing motherboards"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Managing computer memory and resources"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Manufacturing hard disks"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Generating electricity for the computer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The operating system manages memory, processes and other hardware resources."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Which of the following is an example of an operating system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "CorelDRAW"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Android"}, {"id": "c", "text": "PowerPoint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "PageMaker"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Android is a mobile operating system that manages a device''s resources."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','An operating system that allows more than one program to run at the same time is described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "single-tasking"}, {"id": "b", "text": "multitasking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "read-only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "offline"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A multitasking operating system runs several programs concurrently."}',0.6,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','The operating system provides a link between the user and the computer hardware; this role is known as providing a','[{"id": "a", "text": "power supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "user interface"}, {"id": "c", "text": "printout"}, {"id": "d", "text": "storage disk"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The operating system provides a user interface between the user and the hardware."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Organising files into folders, copying and deleting them is part of the operating system function called','[{"id": "a", "text": "file management"}, {"id": "b", "text": "electricity control"}, {"id": "c", "text": "web browsing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "photo editing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Creating, copying, deleting and organising files is the file management function."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','In file organisation, a single character such as the letter ''A'' is referred to as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "field"}, {"id": "b", "text": "record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "byte or character"}, {"id": "d", "text": "file"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A single character is the smallest unit and is stored as a byte or character."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','A collection of related fields about one student, such as name, class and age, forms a','[{"id": "a", "text": "record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "field"}, {"id": "c", "text": "character"}, {"id": "d", "text": "database"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Related fields describing one entity together form a record."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','The correct hierarchy of data organisation from smallest to largest is','[{"id": "a", "text": "field, character, record, file"}, {"id": "b", "text": "character, field, record, file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "record, field, file, character"}, {"id": "d", "text": "file, record, field, character"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Data is organised as character, then field, then record, then file."}',0.6,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','In a school database, the column that stores every student''s date of birth is best described as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "field"}, {"id": "d", "text": "folder"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A field holds one item of data, such as the date of birth, across records."}',0.55,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','A collection of related records kept together, such as all students'' records in a class, is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "field"}, {"id": "b", "text": "file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "character"}, {"id": "d", "text": "byte"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A file is a collection of related records stored together."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','Which of the following is the best way to protect a computer file from unauthorised access?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Leaving the computer switched on"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Using a strong password"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increasing the screen brightness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sharing the file with everyone"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A strong password restricts access to authorised users only."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','Keeping a duplicate copy of important data on another storage medium is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "backup"}, {"id": "b", "text": "formatting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "deleting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "encrypting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Backup keeps a duplicate copy so data can be recovered if lost."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','A program that can copy itself and damage files on a computer is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "compiler"}, {"id": "b", "text": "computer virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spreadsheet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "browser"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A computer virus replicates itself and can damage files and programs."}',0.5,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','Converting data into a coded form so that only authorised persons can read it is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "encryption"}, {"id": "b", "text": "printing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "scanning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "backup"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Encryption codes data so only authorised persons with the key can read it."}',0.6,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','To reduce the risk of electric shock in a computer laboratory, a student should','[{"id": "a", "text": "handle cables with wet hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "avoid touching bare or exposed wires"}, {"id": "c", "text": "overload the wall socket"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pour water near the system unit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Avoiding contact with bare or exposed wires helps prevent electric shock."}',0.45,'{SSS1,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Before working on a domestic circuit, the FIRST safety action an electrician should take is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "wear a wristwatch for timing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "switch off and isolate the supply at the main"}, {"id": "c", "text": "open all the windows"}, {"id": "d", "text": "connect a new lamp"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isolating the supply at the main removes the danger of electric shock before work begins."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','A notice hung on an isolated main switch reading ''MEN AT WORK — DO NOT SWITCH ON'' is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "danger label"}, {"id": "b", "text": "caution tag"}, {"id": "c", "text": "permit-to-work"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lock-out/warning notice"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "A warning/lock-out notice prevents anyone from re-energising the circuit while work is in progress."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','The correct first aid for a victim still in contact with a live conductor is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "pull the victim with your bare hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pour water on the victim"}, {"id": "c", "text": "switch off the supply before touching the victim"}, {"id": "d", "text": "give the victim food to eat"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The supply must be switched off first so the rescuer does not also become a shock victim."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Which of the following fires must NOT be put out with water?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A wood fire"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A paper fire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "An electrical (live equipment) fire"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A grass fire"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Water conducts electricity, so a live electrical fire is fought with CO2 or dry-powder extinguishers, not water."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Rubber-soled shoes and rubber mats are used in the electrical workshop mainly because rubber is a good','[{"id": "a", "text": "conductor of heat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "insulator of electricity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "conductor of electricity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "magnetic material"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rubber is an insulator, so it prevents current from passing through the worker to earth."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The main purpose of earthing metal casings of electrical appliances is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the current drawn by the appliance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "provide a safe path for fault current and protect users from shock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the appliance run faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the electricity bill"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Earthing gives fault current a low-resistance path to earth so the fuse blows and the casing stays safe to touch."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','A device that automatically disconnects a circuit when a small earth-leakage current is detected is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ELCB/RCD"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ammeter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "transformer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dimmer switch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An Earth-Leakage Circuit Breaker / Residual Current Device trips on small leakage currents to prevent shock."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','In a fuse, the element melts and breaks the circuit when the current','[{"id": "a", "text": "falls below normal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "exceeds its rated value"}, {"id": "c", "text": "equals the voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "becomes alternating"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A fuse is a weak link that melts when current rises above its rating, protecting the circuit from overload."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','Which colour of insulation is used for the earth (protective) conductor in modern harmonised wiring?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Brown"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Green-and-yellow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Red"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The green-and-yellow striped conductor is reserved for earthing in the harmonised colour code."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','A miniature circuit breaker (MCB) is preferred to a rewirable fuse because the MCB','[{"id": "a", "text": "cannot be reset after tripping"}, {"id": "b", "text": "can be reset and reused after clearing the fault"}, {"id": "c", "text": "must be replaced each time it operates"}, {"id": "d", "text": "works only on direct current"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An MCB simply trips and can be switched back on after the fault is cleared, unlike a fuse that must be rewired."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The tool used specifically to remove insulation from the end of a conductor without cutting the copper is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "hacksaw"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wire stripper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hammer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "file"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A wire stripper is designed to cut and remove insulation while leaving the conductor undamaged."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','A neon tester (line tester) is used by an electrician to','[{"id": "a", "text": "measure the exact voltage of a supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "check whether a conductor is live"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure resistance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cut cables"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The neon lamp in the tester glows when the probe touches a live point, indicating presence of voltage."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The instrument used to measure the insulation resistance of a wiring installation is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "megger (insulation tester)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "voltmeter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ammeter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wattmeter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A megger applies a high test voltage and measures the very high insulation resistance in megohms."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','To measure current in a circuit, an ammeter must be connected','[{"id": "a", "text": "in parallel with the load"}, {"id": "b", "text": "in series with the load"}, {"id": "c", "text": "across the supply only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "to the earth wire"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An ammeter is connected in series so the whole circuit current flows through it."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','A clamp (tong) meter is especially useful because it can measure current','[{"id": "a", "text": "only after switching off the supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "without breaking or disconnecting the conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only in direct-current circuits"}, {"id": "d", "text": "by melting a fuse element"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The clamp encircles a live conductor and reads current by magnetic induction, so no disconnection is needed."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','The most common material used as a conductor in domestic wiring cables is','[{"id": "a", "text": "copper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rubber"}, {"id": "c", "text": "PVC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wood"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Copper is used because it has low resistance, good conductivity and is ductile."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','In the type of cable labelled PVC/PVC, the PVC serves as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "insulation and sheath"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fuse element"}, {"id": "d", "text": "earth electrode"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Poly-vinyl-chloride forms both the inner insulation and outer sheath that protect the copper conductor."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A round PVC box fitted in the ceiling to hold the connection point for a lamp holder is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "consumer unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "conduit bender"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ceiling rose / round box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "distribution board"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The ceiling rose (round box) houses the terminals that connect the flex of the lamp holder to the fixed wiring."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','Conduit pipes are used in wiring installations mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the voltage of the supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect and carry the cables"}, {"id": "c", "text": "generate electricity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure current"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Conduits provide mechanical protection for cables and allow them to be drawn in or out easily."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','The cross-sectional area of a cable conductor is measured in','[{"id": "a", "text": "square millimetres (mm2)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "volts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "amperes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "watts"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Conductor size is given as its cross-sectional area in square millimetres, e.g. 1.5 mm2, 2.5 mm2."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','The relationship between voltage V, current I and resistance R stated by Ohm''s law is','[{"id": "a", "text": "V = I + R"}, {"id": "b", "text": "V = I x R"}, {"id": "c", "text": "V = I / R"}, {"id": "d", "text": "V = I - R"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ohm''s law states that voltage equals current multiplied by resistance."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','A current of 2 A flows through a resistor of 10 ohms. The voltage across the resistor is','[{"id": "a", "text": "5 V"}, {"id": "b", "text": "12 V"}, {"id": "c", "text": "20 V"}, {"id": "d", "text": "0.2 V"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Using V = I x R, V = 2 x 10 = 20 volts."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','The SI unit of electrical resistance is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ampere"}, {"id": "b", "text": "volt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ohm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "watt"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Resistance is measured in ohms, symbolised by the Greek letter omega."}',0.45,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','Electric current is best defined as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "opposition to the flow of charge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rate of flow of electric charge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "energy stored in a battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pressure that drives electrons"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Current is the rate of flow of charge, measured in amperes (coulombs per second)."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','A 240 V supply drives a current of 4 A through a heater. The resistance of the heater is','[{"id": "a", "text": "60 ohms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "960 ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "244 ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "0.017 ohms"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "R = V / I = 240 / 4 = 60 ohms."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','Two resistors of 3 ohms and 5 ohms connected in series give a total resistance of','[{"id": "a", "text": "1.875 ohms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "8 ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "2 ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "15 ohms"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In series, resistances simply add: 3 + 5 = 8 ohms."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','In a purely series circuit, the current flowing through each component is','[{"id": "a", "text": "different in every component"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the same throughout the circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "zero"}, {"id": "d", "text": "equal to the total voltage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A series circuit has only one path, so the same current flows through every component."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','Household lamps and sockets are wired in parallel mainly so that','[{"id": "a", "text": "each device gets the full supply voltage and can work independently"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the total resistance increases"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only one device can work at a time"}, {"id": "d", "text": "less copper is needed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In parallel each appliance receives the full voltage and can be switched on or off without affecting others."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','The electrical power consumed by a device is given by the formula','[{"id": "a", "text": "P = V / I"}, {"id": "b", "text": "P = V x I"}, {"id": "c", "text": "P = V + I"}, {"id": "d", "text": "P = I / V"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Power equals voltage multiplied by current, measured in watts."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','An electric iron rated 240 V draws a current of 5 A. Its power rating is','[{"id": "a", "text": "48 W"}, {"id": "b", "text": "245 W"}, {"id": "c", "text": "1200 W"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1200 A"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "P = V x I = 240 x 5 = 1200 watts."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','A joint suitable for cables that will be subjected to a heavy pull (mechanical strain) is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "married joint"}, {"id": "b", "text": "britannia joint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tee joint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "twist joint"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Britannia joint is bound and soldered to withstand strong mechanical tension along the cable run."}',0.65,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','In a one-way lighting circuit, the switch must be connected in the','[{"id": "a", "text": "neutral conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "earth conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "live (phase) conductor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "both live and neutral together"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The switch is placed in the live conductor so the lamp is fully isolated from the phase when off."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','A single lamp that must be controlled from two different positions, such as a staircase, requires','[{"id": "a", "text": "two one-way switches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "two two-way switches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "one one-way switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a dimmer switch only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Two two-way switches allow the same lamp to be turned on or off from either end of the stairs."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','Soldered joints are cleaned and coated with flux before soldering in order to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the resistance of the joint"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent oxidation and help the solder flow and stick"}, {"id": "c", "text": "colour the joint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make the joint heavier"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Flux removes and prevents oxide so molten solder wets the copper and forms a sound low-resistance joint."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','A joint used to connect a branch (tapping) cable to a continuous main run without cutting the main is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "tee (T) joint"}, {"id": "b", "text": "straight joint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "married joint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "britannia joint"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tee joint taps a branch conductor onto an unbroken main conductor."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','The board that receives the incoming supply and distributes it to the various final circuits through fuses or MCBs is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ceiling rose"}, {"id": "b", "text": "consumer unit / distribution board"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lamp holder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "junction box"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The consumer unit contains the main switch and the protective devices that feed each final circuit."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','A ring final circuit for socket outlets in a house begins and ends at','[{"id": "a", "text": "the same protective device in the consumer unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "two different houses"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the meter and the earth rod"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a lamp holder"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A ring circuit forms a loop that starts and returns to the same fuse/MCB, sharing current on both legs."}',0.65,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','Which wiring system uses cables drawn through metal or PVC tubes fixed to the wall or slab?','[{"id": "a", "text": "conduit wiring"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cleat wiring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "batten wiring"}, {"id": "d", "text": "casing and capping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Conduit wiring runs the cables inside protective tubes (conduits), giving good mechanical protection."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','In a lighting circuit protected by a 6 A device and socket circuits by a 13 A/16 A device, the different ratings are chosen according to the','[{"id": "a", "text": "colour of the wall"}, {"id": "b", "text": "expected load current of each circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "length of the house"}, {"id": "d", "text": "number of windows"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Protective devices are rated to match the load and cable size so they trip before the cable overheats."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','The energy meter (kilowatt-hour meter) installed by the distribution company measures the','[{"id": "a", "text": "resistance of the wiring"}, {"id": "b", "text": "electrical energy consumed by the consumer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "colour code of the cables"}, {"id": "d", "text": "earth resistance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The kWh meter records the electrical energy used, which is the basis for the consumer''s bill."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A transformer works on the principle of','[{"id": "a", "text": "electromagnetic induction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chemical reaction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "static friction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gravitational force"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A changing current in the primary induces a voltage in the secondary by mutual electromagnetic induction."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A transformer that raises the output voltage above the input voltage is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "step-down transformer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "step-up transformer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "isolation transformer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "current transformer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A step-up transformer has more secondary turns, so the output voltage is higher than the input."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A transformer will NOT operate on a steady direct-current (DC) supply because','[{"id": "a", "text": "DC is too weak"}, {"id": "b", "text": "there is no changing magnetic flux to induce a secondary voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "DC melts the windings instantly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "DC has no current"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Induction needs a changing flux; steady DC produces constant flux, so no voltage is induced in the secondary."}',0.65,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','The device that converts electrical energy into mechanical (rotational) energy is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "generator"}, {"id": "b", "text": "electric motor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "transformer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rectifier"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A motor uses current in a magnetic field to produce a turning force, converting electrical to mechanical energy."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A step-down transformer has 1000 primary turns and 100 secondary turns. If the primary voltage is 240 V, the secondary voltage is','[{"id": "a", "text": "24 V"}, {"id": "b", "text": "2400 V"}, {"id": "c", "text": "240 V"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1000 V"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Vs = Vp x (Ns/Np) = 240 x (100/1000) = 24 volts."}',0.65,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','If a single lamp in a house fails to light while all others work, the MOST likely cause is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "power failure from the utility"}, {"id": "b", "text": "blown lamp or faulty holder on that point"}, {"id": "c", "text": "faulty energy meter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tripped main switch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Since only one point is affected, the fault is local to that lamp or its holder, not the whole supply."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','A condition in which the live and neutral (or earth) conductors touch and cause a very large current to flow is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "short circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "open circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "high resistance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "balanced load"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A short circuit provides a very low-resistance path, causing excessive current that blows the fuse."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','A continuity test on a cable is carried out to find out whether the conductor','[{"id": "a", "text": "is broken (open) or unbroken"}, {"id": "b", "text": "is the right colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "is long enough"}, {"id": "d", "text": "is expensive"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A continuity test checks that current can pass end-to-end, revealing any break in the conductor."}',0.55,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','When a fuse repeatedly blows immediately after replacement, the correct action is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "fit a fuse of much higher rating to stop it blowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "trace and clear the fault before replacing the fuse"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wrap the fuse holder with foil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ignore it and leave the circuit off permanently"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Repeated blowing indicates a persistent fault that must be located and cleared, not bypassed with a bigger fuse."}',0.6,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','Routine preventive maintenance of an installation includes','[{"id": "a", "text": "tightening loose terminals and cleaning contacts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increasing the supply voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "removing all earthing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "painting the cables red"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Preventive maintenance keeps connections tight and clean to avoid overheating and intermittent faults."}',0.5,'{SSS1,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which tool is used to remove stitches wrongly sewn without damaging the fabric?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tracing wheel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Seam ripper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bodkin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Thimble"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A seam ripper (stitch unpicker) cuts and lifts unwanted stitches cleanly."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','The measuring tool best suited for taking the body measurements of a customer is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "metre rule"}, {"id": "b", "text": "set square"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tape measure"}, {"id": "d", "text": "French curve"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A flexible tape measure follows the body''s curves to give accurate girth measurements."}',0.45,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','A thimble is worn on the finger mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "hold pins in place"}, {"id": "b", "text": "push the needle through fabric and protect the finger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure seam allowance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark the fabric"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The thimble protects the finger while pushing the needle during hand sewing."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which of these tools is used to transfer pattern markings onto fabric together with dressmaker''s carbon paper?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tracing wheel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pinking shears"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stiletto"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Loop turner"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tracing wheel presses carbon lines onto fabric to transfer pattern marks."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Pinking shears are used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "cut buttonholes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "give a zigzag edge that reduces fraying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "trim thread ends only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cut thick leather"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pinking shears leave a saw-tooth edge that limits fraying on raw seam edges."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Before oiling a sewing machine, the operator should first','[{"id": "a", "text": "thread the machine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "switch off and unplug the machine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the stitch length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "raise the presser foot only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Disconnecting power prevents accidental starting and injury during maintenance."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Pins and needles in the workshop should be kept in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "loose pocket"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pin cushion or magnetic tray"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cutting table drawer with fabrics"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bundle of thread"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pin cushion or magnetic tray keeps sharps together and prevents pricks and loss."}',0.45,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','A common cause of a sewing machine breaking needles is','[{"id": "a", "text": "correct threading"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pulling the fabric while the machine sews"}, {"id": "c", "text": "using the right needle size"}, {"id": "d", "text": "oiling the machine regularly"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pulling fabric bends the needle against the throat plate, causing it to break."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Which practice best keeps a sewing workshop safe from fire?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Leaving the pressing iron on after use"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Storing oily rags in a corner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Switching off and unplugging the iron when not in use"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overloading a single socket with many machines"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Unplugging the iron after use removes a major heat source and fire risk."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','To keep cutting shears sharp and rust-free, they should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "used to cut paper regularly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kept clean, dry and used only for fabric"}, {"id": "c", "text": "left open on a wet table"}, {"id": "d", "text": "washed in water after each use"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Reserving shears for fabric and keeping them dry preserves the blade and prevents rust."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which of these is a natural fibre obtained from a plant?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Polyester"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Acrylic"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cotton is a cellulosic natural fibre from the cotton plant boll."}',0.45,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Silk and wool are classified as natural fibres of','[{"id": "a", "text": "vegetable origin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mineral origin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "animal origin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "synthetic origin"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Silk comes from the silkworm and wool from sheep, so both are animal fibres."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','A fabric that is comfortable in the hot Nigerian climate because it absorbs sweat well is','[{"id": "a", "text": "polyester"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nylon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cotton"}, {"id": "d", "text": "acetate"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cotton is highly absorbent, making it cool and comfortable in hot weather."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which fibre is a man-made (synthetic) fibre produced from chemicals?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Linen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Jute"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Polyester"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Silk"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Polyester is a synthetic fibre made from petroleum-based chemicals."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','The burning test in which a fibre burns with the smell of burning paper and leaves soft grey ash indicates','[{"id": "a", "text": "cotton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nylon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silk"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cellulosic cotton burns like paper and leaves a soft grey ash."}',0.65,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','The lengthwise grain of a woven fabric, which runs parallel to the selvedge, is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "weft"}, {"id": "b", "text": "bias"}, {"id": "c", "text": "warp"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nap"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Warp yarns run lengthwise, parallel to the selvedge, and are the strongest grain."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','The finished, firmly woven edge along the length of a fabric that does not fray is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "selvedge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hemline"}, {"id": "c", "text": "raw edge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "seam line"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The selvedge is the self-finished lengthwise edge that prevents fraying."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Cutting fabric on the true bias means cutting at what angle to the selvedge?','[{"id": "a", "text": "0 degrees"}, {"id": "b", "text": "45 degrees"}, {"id": "c", "text": "90 degrees"}, {"id": "d", "text": "180 degrees"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "True bias runs at 45 degrees to the selvedge, giving fabric maximum stretch."}',0.65,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','A delicate silk blouse should best be laundered by','[{"id": "a", "text": "boiling in hot water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gentle hand washing in cool water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "scrubbing with a hard brush"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bleaching with strong chlorine"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Silk is delicate and protein-based, so gentle hand washing in cool water avoids damage."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Which laundry symbol instruction protects a garment made from wool?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Machine wash hot and tumble dry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hand wash cool and dry flat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Boil and wring hard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Soak overnight in bleach"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Wool felts and shrinks with heat and agitation, so cool hand washing and flat drying are safest."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','When taking the bust measurement, the tape should be passed','[{"id": "a", "text": "around the fullest part of the bust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "around the natural waistline"}, {"id": "c", "text": "over the shoulder to the hem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "around the widest part of the hip"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bust girth is taken around the fullest part of the chest, level all round."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The measurement taken around the fullest part of the seat is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "waist"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hip"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bust"}, {"id": "d", "text": "neck"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The hip measurement is taken around the fullest part of the seat."}',0.45,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','Before taking measurements, a piece of narrow tape or string is tied round the client''s waist to','[{"id": "a", "text": "decorate the client"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mark the natural waistline as a reference point"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hold the garment together"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure the length of the arm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The waist string fixes the true waistline so vertical measurements are consistent."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','For accurate measurements, the client should','[{"id": "a", "text": "wear a thick winter coat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stand upright in well-fitting clothing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bend forward slightly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sit on a low stool"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Standing upright in close-fitting clothing gives natural, accurate girths and lengths."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The sleeve length for a long sleeve is measured from the','[{"id": "a", "text": "neck to the waist"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shoulder tip to the wrist over a slightly bent elbow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "underarm to the hem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "waist to the knee"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sleeve length runs from the shoulder tip over the bent elbow to the wrist for room to move."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','The extra fabric added beyond the stitching line to allow for joining pieces is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "hem allowance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "seam allowance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dart"}, {"id": "d", "text": "notch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Seam allowance is the margin between the cutting line and the stitching line."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','A dart is used in pattern making to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add decoration only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shape flat fabric to fit body curves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lengthen a garment"}, {"id": "d", "text": "finish a raw edge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Darts remove excess fabric to create shape that fits the body''s contours."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','Small marks on a pattern that show where pieces should be matched during joining are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "notches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pleats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gathers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "selvedges"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Notches are balance marks that align corresponding pattern pieces accurately."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','When laying pattern pieces on fabric, the grain line on the pattern should be placed','[{"id": "a", "text": "at random on the fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "parallel to the selvedge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "across the width only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "on the bias always"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Aligning the grain line parallel to the selvedge keeps the garment hanging correctly."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','An economical fabric layout during cutting is important mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase fabric waste"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduce fabric wastage and cost"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the garment heavier"}, {"id": "d", "text": "change the fabric colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A well-planned layout uses fabric efficiently, cutting cost and waste."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','A long, temporary stitch used to hold fabric together before permanent sewing is','[{"id": "a", "text": "the tacking (basting) stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the backstitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the hemming stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the blanket stitch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tacking (basting) is a long temporary stitch removed after permanent stitching."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Which hand stitch is strong and resembles machine stitching, used where firmness is needed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Running stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tacking stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Backstitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Gathering stitch"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The backstitch overlaps stitches to form a strong, secure line like machine sewing."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','The blanket stitch is mainly used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "gather fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "neaten and decorate raw edges"}, {"id": "c", "text": "attach a zip"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark darts"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The blanket stitch finishes and decorates edges while preventing fraying."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','A row of loose running stitches drawn up to reduce fabric width produces','[{"id": "a", "text": "gathers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "darts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "facings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "seams"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pulling up loose running stitches gathers the fabric into soft folds."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Which stitch is most suitable for turning up and securing a hem invisibly on the right side?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Chain stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Slip (hemming) stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cross stitch on the right side"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Machine top stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The slip or hemming stitch catches only a thread of the garment so it stays hidden."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','The simplest and most common seam, made by joining two pieces on the wrong side, is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "French seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "plain (open) seam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flat-fell seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "overlaid seam"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The plain seam is the basic seam pressed open, used on most garments."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A self-neatening seam that encloses all raw edges, suitable for sheer fabrics, is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "plain seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "French seam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "top-stitched seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "channel seam"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The French seam encloses raw edges within the seam, ideal for sheer or fraying fabric."}',0.65,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A strong, self-finished seam commonly used on jeans and children''s wear is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "flat-fell seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "plain seam pressed open"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lapped seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "piped seam"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The flat-fell seam encloses edges and is double-stitched, giving strength for hard-wear garments."}',0.65,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A shaped piece of fabric used to neaten a curved edge such as a neckline is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "facing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gusset"}, {"id": "c", "text": "yoke"}, {"id": "d", "text": "placket cover"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A facing is cut to the same shape as the edge and turned inside to finish it neatly."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Before top-stitching a curved seam such as an armhole, the seam allowance is often clipped to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make it fray faster"}, {"id": "b", "text": "allow the curve to lie flat and smooth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add decoration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase the seam allowance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clipping releases tension so a curved seam turns and lies flat without puckering."}',0.65,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Which of the following is an element of design used in clothing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Balance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Proportion"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Colour, line, shape and texture are elements of design; balance and rhythm are principles."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Vertical lines in a garment design generally make the wearer appear','[{"id": "a", "text": "shorter and wider"}, {"id": "b", "text": "taller and slimmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rounder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "unchanged"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Vertical lines lead the eye up and down, creating an illusion of height and slimness."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','On the colour wheel, the colours directly opposite each other, such as red and green, are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "primary colours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "analogous colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "complementary colours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "neutral colours"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Complementary colours sit opposite on the colour wheel and contrast strongly."}',0.6,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','The principle of design that gives a feeling of equal visual weight on both sides of a garment is','[{"id": "a", "text": "balance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "texture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "line"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Balance arranges design features so the garment looks visually stable and even."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Red, blue and yellow are referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "secondary colours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "primary colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tertiary colours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "warm colours only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Red, blue and yellow are primary colours from which other colours are mixed."}',0.45,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','A tailor buys 3 metres of fabric at N1,500 per metre. The total fabric cost is','[{"id": "a", "text": "N1,500"}, {"id": "b", "text": "N3,000"}, {"id": "c", "text": "N4,500"}, {"id": "d", "text": "N6,000"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "3 metres times N1,500 equals N4,500 in total fabric cost."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','In pricing a garment, the selling price should normally cover the cost of materials, labour and','[{"id": "a", "text": "loss only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a reasonable profit margin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the customer''s transport"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nothing extra"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A viable price covers costs plus a profit margin to keep the business running."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','If total cost of making a dress is N7,000 and it is sold for N10,000, the profit is','[{"id": "a", "text": "N2,000"}, {"id": "b", "text": "N3,000"}, {"id": "c", "text": "N7,000"}, {"id": "d", "text": "N17,000"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Profit equals selling price minus cost: N10,000 minus N7,000 is N3,000."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','Keeping a record book of daily sales and expenses in a tailoring business helps the owner to','[{"id": "a", "text": "waste more materials"}, {"id": "b", "text": "know whether the business is making profit or loss"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid paying customers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase fabric fraying"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Accurate records show income against expenses, revealing profit or loss."}',0.55,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','Which quality best builds customer loyalty for a garment-making enterprise?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Poor finishing to save time"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Delivering well-finished garments on the promised date"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ignoring the client''s measurements"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Frequently missing deadlines"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good workmanship delivered on time earns trust and repeat customers."}',0.5,'{SSS1,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Horticulture is best defined as the science and art of cultivating which group of plants?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cereal grains grown on large mechanised farms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fruits, vegetables, flowers and ornamental plants"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Timber trees grown for construction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Grasses grown solely for livestock grazing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Horticulture deals with intensive cultivation of fruits, vegetables, flowers and ornamental plants."}',0.45,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','The branch of horticulture that deals with the production of fruits is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Floriculture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Arboriculture"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Pomology is the branch of horticulture concerned with fruit production."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','A student growing tomatoes, okra and pepper for the market is practising which branch of horticulture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Floriculture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Landscaping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Olericulture is the branch dealing with the production of vegetables."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','The cultivation and arrangement of flowers and ornamental plants for beauty is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Floriculture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Agronomy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Floriculture is the branch concerned with growing flowers and ornamental plants."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Which branch of horticulture is chiefly concerned with the design and care of gardens, parks and outdoor spaces?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Landscape horticulture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Viticulture"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Landscape horticulture deals with designing, planting and maintaining outdoor spaces."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Which of the following is a major economic importance of horticulture to Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It provides employment and income to farmers and traders"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It reduces the need for rainfall in farming"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It removes the need for soil testing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It eliminates the use of hand tools on farms"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Horticulture creates jobs and generates income along its production and marketing chain."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Fruits and vegetables produced through horticulture are especially valued in the diet because they supply','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mainly fats and oils"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vitamins and mineral salts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only carbohydrates"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pure protein and nothing else"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fruits and vegetables are important dietary sources of vitamins and minerals."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','The planting of ornamental plants and lawns around a school compound mainly serves to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Increase soil erosion around buildings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Beautify the environment and improve aesthetics"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Attract pests to the buildings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reduce the supply of oxygen"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ornamental planting beautifies the environment and improves its appearance."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Horticulture contributes to Nigeria''s foreign exchange earnings mainly through','[{"id": "a", "text": "Export of fruits, vegetables and cut flowers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Importation of processed food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Abandoning farmland to bush fallow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reducing the number of markets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Exporting horticultural produce such as fruits and flowers earns foreign exchange."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Which environmental benefit is provided by trees and shrubs grown in horticulture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "They increase air pollution"}, {"id": "b", "text": "They provide shade and help purify the air"}, {"id": "c", "text": "They raise the temperature of surroundings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "They stop plants from photosynthesising"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Trees and shrubs provide shade and absorb carbon dioxide, helping to purify the air."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Which tool is most suitable for digging and turning the soil in a garden bed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Secateurs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spade"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A spade is used for digging, turning soil and making beds."}',0.45,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','A gardener wishing to prune the branches of an ornamental shrub should use','[{"id": "a", "text": "A hoe"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A secateurs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A trowel"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Secateurs (pruning shears) are used to cut small branches and stems cleanly."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','The garden tool used mainly for levelling soil and gathering leaves or debris is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dibber"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sprayer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rake is used to level soil surfaces and gather leaves and debris."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','A trowel is best described as a tool used for','[{"id": "a", "text": "Spraying chemicals on crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Transplanting seedlings and digging small holes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cutting large tree trunks"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Carrying manure across the farm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A hand trowel is used to dig small holes and transplant seedlings."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Which equipment is used to convey manure, soil or refuse from one part of the garden to another?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Secateurs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Dibber"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A wheelbarrow is used to carry soil, manure and refuse around the garden."}',0.45,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','After using cutting tools such as a cutlass, they should be cleaned and lightly oiled mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make them heavier to use"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prevent rusting and keep them sharp"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change their colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase their market price"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning and oiling tools prevents rust and preserves their cutting edge."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','The correct way to hand a sharp cutlass to another worker is to give it','[{"id": "a", "text": "Blade first, pointing at the receiver"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Handle first, with the blade pointing away"}, {"id": "c", "text": "By throwing it across to them"}, {"id": "d", "text": "While both people run"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Passing a cutting tool handle-first prevents injury to the receiver."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Which protective item should be worn when spraying pesticides in a nursery?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Open sandals only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hand gloves and a nose mask"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A short-sleeved singlet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "No protection is needed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Gloves and a nose mask protect the skin and lungs from harmful chemicals."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Garden tools should be stored after use in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "Dry, well-ventilated store or shed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Heap in the open under the rain"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bucket of water overnight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pile of fresh manure"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Storing tools in a dry, ventilated place prevents rust and damage."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','A blunt hoe or cutlass should be sharpened because a sharp tool','[{"id": "a", "text": "Requires more effort and is more dangerous"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Works more easily and safely"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cannot cut weeds at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Should never be used on a farm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A sharp tool cuts with less effort and slips less, making work safer and easier."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Propagation of plants by means of seeds is described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "Asexual propagation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sexual propagation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Vegetative propagation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Grafting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Seed propagation involves fertilisation, so it is sexual propagation."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Which of the following is an example of asexual (vegetative) propagation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sowing maize grains"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Raising tomato from seeds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Planting cassava stem cuttings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Planting pepper seeds in a nursery"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Planting cassava stem cuttings uses a plant part, making it vegetative propagation."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','The joining of a scion of one plant to the rootstock of another is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Layering"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sowing"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Grafting unites a scion with a rootstock so they grow as one plant."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','An advantage of vegetative propagation over seed propagation is that the new plants','[{"id": "a", "text": "Are always different from the parent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Retain the exact characteristics of the parent plant"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cannot bear fruit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Take much longer to mature"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Vegetatively propagated plants are genetically identical to the parent."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','In which method of propagation is a stem bent down and covered with soil until it produces roots?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Layering"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Seed sowing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In layering a stem is covered with soil while still attached until roots form."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','A nursery in horticulture is best described as a place where','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mature crops are stored after harvest"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Young seedlings are raised and cared for before transplanting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Farm animals are reared"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tools are repaired and sold"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nursery is where seedlings are raised and tended before transplanting to the field."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','A nursery site is best located','[{"id": "a", "text": "Far from any source of water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Near a reliable source of water and well drained"}, {"id": "c", "text": "On a steep, eroded hillside"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Under a heavily shaded thick forest floor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A good nursery site is well drained and close to a reliable water supply."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Young seedlings in a nursery are shaded mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Protect them from intense sunlight and drying out"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prevent them from ever receiving light"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Encourage pests to attack them"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stop them from being watered"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Shading protects tender seedlings from scorching sun and excessive water loss."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','The practice of removing excess crowded seedlings to give the rest more space is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pricking out"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thinning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Staking"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Thinning removes overcrowded seedlings so the remaining ones have space to grow."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Hardening off nursery seedlings before transplanting involves','[{"id": "a", "text": "Gradually exposing them to field conditions"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Keeping them permanently in deep shade"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Withholding all water until they wilt fully"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Burying them completely in soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hardening off gradually exposes seedlings to sun and drier conditions so they survive transplanting."}',0.65,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','The best type of soil for growing most horticultural crops is','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pure sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Heavy sticky clay"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rocky gravel"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Loamy soil holds moisture and nutrients well while draining freely, ideal for most crops."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','Adding well-rotted farmyard manure or compost to garden soil mainly helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Improve soil fertility and structure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the soil completely waterproof"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kill all soil organisms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase soil erosion"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Organic manure adds nutrients and improves soil structure and water retention."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','Covering the soil surface around plants with dry grass or leaves to conserve moisture is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ridging"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pruning"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mulching covers the soil to conserve moisture and suppress weeds."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','A soil that is too acidic for vegetables can be corrected by applying','[{"id": "a", "text": "Common salt"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lime"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kerosene"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sand"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Liming raises soil pH, reducing acidity for better crop growth."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','The main reason for ploughing or digging garden soil before planting is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Loosen the soil and improve aeration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the soil more compact and hard"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Remove all the topsoil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Prevent water from entering the soil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cultivating the soil loosens it, improving aeration and root penetration."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','The best time of day to water horticultural crops to reduce loss of water by evaporation is','[{"id": "a", "text": "Early morning or late evening"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mid-day under the hot sun"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only at exactly noon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Never during the dry season"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Watering in the cool early morning or evening reduces evaporation losses."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Weeds compete with horticultural crops mainly for','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nutrients, water, light and space"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Farm tools and equipment"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Storage barns"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Market prices"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weeds compete with crops for nutrients, water, sunlight and space."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Which of the following is a cultural method of controlling pests in a vegetable garden?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Crop rotation and regular weeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spraying only synthetic insecticides"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Introducing predatory insects"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Planting resistant varieties"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Crop rotation and sanitation through weeding are cultural control methods."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Overhead irrigation that applies water like artificial rainfall is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sprinkler irrigation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Furrow irrigation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Basin irrigation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sub-surface irrigation"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sprinkler irrigation sprays water over crops resembling rainfall."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Yellowing of leaves in a leafy vegetable crop is most likely a sign of','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nutrient deficiency such as nitrogen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Too many tools in the store"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The plant being fully mature and healthy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Correct spacing of the plants"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Yellowing (chlorosis) of leaves often indicates a nutrient deficiency such as nitrogen."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Landscaping can be defined as the art of','[{"id": "a", "text": "Improving and beautifying an area of land using plants and features"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Growing only cereal crops for food"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rearing fish in ponds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Building houses and roads only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Landscaping is the art of improving and beautifying land with plants and features."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','A lawn in a landscape design refers to','[{"id": "a", "text": "An area covered with cut, well-maintained grass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A pile of building sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A pond of ornamental fish"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A row of fruit trees only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A lawn is an area covered with mown, well-kept grass."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Which of the following is a softscape element in landscaping?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flowering shrubs and trees"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Concrete walkways"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stone walls"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paved parking area"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Softscape refers to the living plant elements such as shrubs and trees."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Paved paths, walls and fountains in a garden are together referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hardscape features"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Softscape features"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nursery beds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Compost heaps"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Non-living constructed features such as paths and walls are hardscape elements."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','A hedge in a landscape is best described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "A row of closely planted shrubs forming a boundary or screen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A single tall ornamental tree"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A pool of water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A heap of dry leaves"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hedge is a line of closely planted shrubs used as a boundary or screen."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','A common method of establishing a lawn quickly using pieces of grass with soil attached is','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sprigging or sodding (turfing)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Layering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Lawns can be established by sodding/turfing or sprigging using grass pieces."}',0.6,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Regular mowing of a lawn is carried out mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Keep the grass short, neat and dense"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Kill all the grass permanently"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Encourage weeds to dominate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Remove all the topsoil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mowing keeps a lawn short, even, neat and encourages dense growth."}',0.5,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','The trimming of shrubs and hedges to a desired shape and size is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pruning or trimming"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Irrigating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Harvesting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Pruning or trimming shapes shrubs and hedges and encourages healthy growth."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Edging of a lawn along walkways and beds is done mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Give a neat, well-defined boundary"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the height of the grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Destroy the ornamental plants"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Block drainage from the garden"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Edging creates a neat, clearly defined boundary between the lawn and other areas."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Applying fertiliser to a lawn during maintenance is done to','[{"id": "a", "text": "Supply nutrients for healthy green growth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the grass turn brown and die"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Attract pests to the lawn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Harden the soil into rock"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Fertilising supplies nutrients that keep lawn grass green and healthy."}',0.55,'{SSS1,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which of the following best defines livestock farming?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The cultivation of crops for food and cash"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The rearing of domestic animals for food and other products"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The catching of fish from rivers and lakes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The planting of trees for timber production"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Livestock farming is the rearing of domesticated animals for meat, milk, eggs and other useful products."}',0.45,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','A farmer in Kano who keeps cattle, sheep and goats is practising which branch of agriculture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Arable farming"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Forestry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Animal husbandry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Horticulture"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Rearing of farm animals such as cattle, sheep and goats is called animal husbandry."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which group of farm animals is classified as poultry?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cattle and buffalo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Fowls, turkeys and ducks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sheep and goats"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pigs and rabbits"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Poultry refers to domesticated birds such as fowls, turkeys, ducks and guinea fowls reared for meat and eggs."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Cattle, sheep and goats are grouped together as ruminants because they all','[{"id": "a", "text": "have a single-chambered stomach"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lay eggs for reproduction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chew the cud and have a four-chambered stomach"}, {"id": "d", "text": "feed only on animal protein"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Ruminants have a four-chambered stomach and chew the cud to digest fibrous plant material."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which of the following farm animals is a monogastric (non-ruminant) animal?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pig"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sheep"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The pig has a simple single-chambered stomach, making it a monogastric or non-ruminant animal."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','The main livestock product obtained from a dairy cow is','[{"id": "a", "text": "wool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "milk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "eggs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "honey"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dairy cattle are reared mainly for the production of milk."}',0.45,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Which livestock product is the main source of animal fibre used for making textiles?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hide"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Milk"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Wool obtained from sheep is the animal fibre spun into yarn for textiles."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Animal skin processed into leather for shoes and bags is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "hide"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cud"}, {"id": "c", "text": "silage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "offal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hide is the skin of large animals such as cattle, tanned into leather for shoes and bags."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','How does livestock farming contribute to crop production on a mixed farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It supplies pesticides for spraying crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It supplies animal dung used as organic manure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It removes weeds from the farmland"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It provides irrigation water for crops"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Animal dung is a valuable organic manure that improves soil fertility for crops."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','One important economic benefit of livestock farming to Nigeria is that it','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduces the supply of animal protein"}, {"id": "b", "text": "provides employment and income to farmers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "causes desertification of the land"}, {"id": "d", "text": "discourages the growth of agro-based industries"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Livestock farming provides jobs and steady income, supporting rural livelihoods and the economy."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','The White Fulani (Bunaji) is a common Nigerian breed of','[{"id": "a", "text": "goat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cattle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sheep"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pig"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The White Fulani (Bunaji) is a widely reared indigenous zebu cattle breed in Nigeria."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Which of the following is an exotic breed of poultry kept mainly for egg production?','[{"id": "a", "text": "White Leghorn"}, {"id": "b", "text": "West African Dwarf"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Red Sokoto"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Yankasa"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The White Leghorn is an exotic layer breed noted for high egg production."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','The Red Sokoto (Maradi) is a well-known Nigerian breed of','[{"id": "a", "text": "cattle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "goat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rabbit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The Red Sokoto (Maradi) is a popular Nigerian goat breed valued for meat and quality skin."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','A poultry breed reared for both meat and eggs is best described as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "layer breed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "broiler breed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dual-purpose breed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ornamental breed"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Dual-purpose breeds are reared for both meat and egg production."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Broilers are strains of chicken raised specifically for','[{"id": "a", "text": "rapid meat production"}, {"id": "b", "text": "long-term egg laying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "feather and wool production"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ornamental purposes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Broilers are fast-growing chickens reared mainly for their meat within a short period."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','In the extensive system of rearing, animals are','[{"id": "a", "text": "kept permanently in confined houses"}, {"id": "b", "text": "allowed to roam freely and feed on natural pasture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "kept in cages and fed only concentrates"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reared entirely on hydroponic feed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In the extensive system animals graze freely over a wide area of natural pasture."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The system in which birds are kept permanently in cages or houses and fully provided with feed and water is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "extensive system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "semi-intensive system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "intensive system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "nomadic system"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In the intensive system animals are confined and all their needs are supplied by the farmer."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','An advantage of the intensive system of poultry keeping over the extensive system is','[{"id": "a", "text": "lower cost of housing and feeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "easier control of diseases and predators"}, {"id": "c", "text": "animals search for their own food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "no need for record keeping"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Confinement in the intensive system makes disease control and protection from predators easier."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The semi-intensive system of rearing combines','[{"id": "a", "text": "confinement with limited access to an outdoor run"}, {"id": "b", "text": "total confinement with no outdoor movement"}, {"id": "c", "text": "free range with no shelter at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "water rearing with cage rearing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The semi-intensive system provides housing plus a fenced outdoor run for the animals."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The movement of Fulani herdsmen with their cattle in search of pasture and water is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "intensive rearing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "battery cage rearing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nomadic (pastoral) rearing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "deep litter rearing"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Nomadic or pastoral rearing involves moving herds from place to place seeking pasture and water."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Maize and guinea corn are added to livestock feed mainly to supply','[{"id": "a", "text": "protein"}, {"id": "b", "text": "energy (carbohydrate)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vitamins"}, {"id": "d", "text": "minerals"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cereal grains such as maize and guinea corn are energy feeds rich in carbohydrate."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Groundnut cake and soybean meal are included in animal rations chiefly as sources of','[{"id": "a", "text": "carbohydrate"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "protein"}, {"id": "d", "text": "water"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Oilseed cakes like groundnut cake and soybean meal are protein concentrates."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Bone meal and oyster shell are added to poultry feed mainly to provide','[{"id": "a", "text": "energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "minerals such as calcium and phosphorus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "roughage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "protein"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bone meal and oyster shell supply calcium and phosphorus for strong bones and egg shells."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','A ration that supplies all the nutrients an animal needs in the correct proportion is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "maintenance ration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "balanced ration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "supplementary ration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "production ration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A balanced ration contains all required nutrients in the right proportions for the animal."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Which feedstuff is a good source of roughage for ruminants?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fish meal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Elephant grass and hay"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Palm oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Common salt"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Grasses such as elephant grass and hay provide the fibre (roughage) needed by ruminants."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','A good livestock house should be sited on a','[{"id": "a", "text": "waterlogged low-lying ground"}, {"id": "b", "text": "well-drained land with good ventilation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dusty area beside a busy road"}, {"id": "d", "text": "swampy river bank"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Animal houses should be on well-drained, well-ventilated sites to keep animals healthy."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','In the deep litter system of poultry keeping, the floor is covered with','[{"id": "a", "text": "wire mesh only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wood shavings or dry litter material"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wet mud"}, {"id": "d", "text": "polythene sheets"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The deep litter floor is spread with absorbent litter such as wood shavings or dry grass."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','The building used to house pigs on the farm is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "sty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "byre"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hutch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "coop"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pig house is called a sty (piggery)."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','A rabbit is normally housed in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "byre"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hutch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "kraal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sty"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rabbits are kept in a hutch, a raised wooden cage-like house."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','Adequate ventilation in a livestock house is important because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "increases the humidity and heat inside"}, {"id": "b", "text": "removes stale air and reduces build-up of harmful gases"}, {"id": "c", "text": "encourages the growth of parasites"}, {"id": "d", "text": "prevents animals from feeding"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good ventilation supplies fresh air and removes ammonia and moisture, keeping animals healthy."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Newcastle disease is a serious viral disease that affects','[{"id": "a", "text": "cattle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pigs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "goats"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Newcastle disease is a highly contagious viral disease of poultry causing heavy losses."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','The most effective way to prevent Newcastle disease in a poultry flock is by','[{"id": "a", "text": "giving antibiotics after the outbreak"}, {"id": "b", "text": "regular vaccination of the birds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increasing the feed given daily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reducing the water supply"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Newcastle disease is a viral infection best prevented by routine vaccination, since antibiotics do not cure viruses."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Foot-and-mouth disease is a viral disease commonly associated with','[{"id": "a", "text": "fowls and ducks"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cattle and other cloven-hoofed animals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rabbits only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fish"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Foot-and-mouth disease affects cloven-hoofed animals such as cattle, sheep, goats and pigs."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','A general sign that a farm animal is sick is','[{"id": "a", "text": "bright eyes and active movement"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dullness, loss of appetite and isolation from the herd"}, {"id": "c", "text": "smooth shiny coat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "steady weight gain"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sick animals often appear dull, refuse feed, and separate themselves from the rest of the herd."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','To prevent the spread of a contagious disease among farm animals, a sick animal should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "mixed with healthy ones for warmth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "isolated (quarantined) and treated"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sold immediately to the market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "given more grazing space"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isolating (quarantining) and treating the sick animal prevents it from infecting healthy stock."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Which of the following is an external parasite of livestock?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tapeworm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Liver fluke"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tick"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Roundworm"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Ticks live on the skin of animals sucking blood, making them external parasites."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Tapeworms and roundworms found in the intestine of animals are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "external parasites"}, {"id": "b", "text": "internal parasites"}, {"id": "c", "text": "predators"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vectors"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tapeworms and roundworms live inside the body, so they are internal (endo) parasites."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Ticks are harmful to cattle mainly because they','[{"id": "a", "text": "improve the animal''s appetite"}, {"id": "b", "text": "suck blood and transmit diseases"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase milk production"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clean the animal''s skin"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ticks suck blood, weaken the animal and can transmit diseases from one animal to another."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Internal worms in ruminants are best controlled by','[{"id": "a", "text": "spraying the skin with acaricide"}, {"id": "b", "text": "regular deworming with anthelmintics"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increasing salt in the feed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trimming the hooves"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Anthelmintic (deworming) drugs are used to remove internal worms from ruminants."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Dipping or spraying cattle with acaricide is carried out mainly to control','[{"id": "a", "text": "tapeworms in the gut"}, {"id": "b", "text": "external parasites such as ticks and mites"}, {"id": "c", "text": "viral infections of the lung"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mineral deficiency"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Acaricides applied by dipping or spraying kill external parasites like ticks and mites on the skin."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The period during which a female animal is ready and willing to mate is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "gestation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "oestrus (heat)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lactation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "weaning"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oestrus, or heat, is the period when a female is sexually receptive and can be mated."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The introduction of semen from a male into a female animal without natural mating is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "crossbreeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "artificial insemination"}, {"id": "c", "text": "castration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "culling"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Artificial insemination is the artificial placement of semen into the female reproductive tract."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The period of pregnancy from fertilisation to birth in an animal is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "incubation period"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gestation period"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weaning period"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brooding period"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The gestation period is the length of pregnancy from conception to the birth of the young."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','Castration of male animals not needed for breeding is carried out to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make them more aggressive"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduce aggression and improve meat quality"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase their fertility"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make them produce milk"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Castration reduces aggressiveness and improves the quality of meat in fattening animals."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The removal of poor or unproductive animals from a herd or flock is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "c", "text": "docking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dipping"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Culling is the removal of unproductive, sick or old animals to keep the herd efficient."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','A record that shows the parents and ancestry of a breeding animal is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "sales record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pedigree (breeding) record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "feeding record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "health record"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pedigree or breeding record traces the ancestry and parentage of breeding animals."}',0.6,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','Why is it important for a livestock farmer to keep proper farm records?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To make the work more difficult"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To assess profit or loss and plan production"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To hide information from buyers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To waste the farmer''s time"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Farm records help the farmer track income and expenses, measure performance and plan ahead."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','Which record would a poultry farmer use to track the number of eggs collected daily?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vaccination record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Egg production record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pedigree record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wages record"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An egg production record documents the daily number of eggs laid by the flock."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','A good safety practice when handling drugs and disinfectants on a livestock farm is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "wear protective gloves and follow the instructions"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mix all chemicals together in one container"}, {"id": "c", "text": "store them with the animal feed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "taste them to test their strength"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Wearing gloves and following label instructions protects the handler from harm when using farm chemicals."}',0.5,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','When approaching a large animal such as a bull for handling, the worker should','[{"id": "a", "text": "startle it suddenly from behind"}, {"id": "b", "text": "approach calmly and let the animal notice him first"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shout loudly to frighten it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "run quickly towards it"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Approaching calmly and letting the animal see you first prevents it from panicking and injuring the handler."}',0.55,'{SSS1,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The direct conversion of sunlight into electricity by a solar cell is known as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "thermoelectric effect"}, {"id": "b", "text": "photovoltaic effect"}, {"id": "c", "text": "piezoelectric effect"}, {"id": "d", "text": "electromagnetic effect"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The photovoltaic effect is the generation of voltage and current when a material is exposed to light."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The semiconductor material most commonly used to manufacture solar PV cells is','[{"id": "a", "text": "copper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "aluminium"}, {"id": "c", "text": "silicon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "carbon"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Silicon is the dominant semiconductor used in most solar cells worldwide."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The intensity of solar radiation reaching a surface is measured in','[{"id": "a", "text": "watts per square metre"}, {"id": "b", "text": "amperes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "farads"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Solar irradiance is measured in watts per square metre (W/m2)."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','A single crystalline silicon solar cell produces an open-circuit voltage of about','[{"id": "a", "text": "0.5 to 0.6 volts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "1.5 volts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "12 volts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "24 volts"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A typical silicon solar cell generates roughly 0.5 to 0.6 V regardless of its size."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','For a solar panel in Nigeria to capture the most energy over the day, its surface should ideally face','[{"id": "a", "text": "north"}, {"id": "b", "text": "south"}, {"id": "c", "text": "east"}, {"id": "d", "text": "west"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Nigeria is in the northern hemisphere, so panels tilted toward the south receive the most sunlight."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Which type of solar cell is made from a single continuous crystal structure and is usually most efficient?','[{"id": "a", "text": "polycrystalline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "amorphous thin-film"}, {"id": "c", "text": "monocrystalline"}, {"id": "d", "text": "organic"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Monocrystalline cells are cut from a single silicon crystal and offer the highest efficiency among common types."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','As the temperature of a silicon solar panel rises well above 25 degrees Celsius, its power output generally','[{"id": "a", "text": "increases sharply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "decreases"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stays exactly the same"}, {"id": "d", "text": "becomes zero"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "High cell temperature lowers output voltage, so power output falls as panels get hotter."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','The output current of a solar module increases mainly when there is an increase in','[{"id": "a", "text": "wind speed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "solar irradiance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cable length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "air humidity"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Current produced by a PV module is directly proportional to the intensity of sunlight (irradiance)."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','A polycrystalline solar panel can be recognised by its','[{"id": "a", "text": "uniform black colour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "bluish colour with visible crystal grains"}, {"id": "c", "text": "transparent glass with no cells"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brown wooden frame"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Polycrystalline panels have a speckled blue appearance from many silicon crystals fused together."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Partial shading of even one cell in a series-connected module is a problem because it can','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the whole module output"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduce the output of the entire module"}, {"id": "c", "text": "have no effect at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "permanently reverse the polarity"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In a series string, the shaded cell limits current and can sharply reduce the whole module''s output."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','The device that converts direct current (DC) from solar panels into alternating current (AC) for home appliances is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "charge controller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "inverter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "combiner box"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An inverter changes DC electricity into the AC used by most household appliances."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','The main function of a charge controller in a solar system is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "convert DC to AC"}, {"id": "b", "text": "regulate charging and prevent battery overcharge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase panel wattage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cool the inverter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A charge controller regulates current from the panels to protect the battery from overcharging and deep discharge."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','In an off-grid solar home system, energy for use at night is stored in the','[{"id": "a", "text": "inverter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "solar panel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "battery bank"}, {"id": "d", "text": "charge controller"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Batteries store the energy generated during the day for use when there is no sunlight."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','Which charge controller technology extracts the most power from the panels by tracking their maximum power point?','[{"id": "a", "text": "PWM"}, {"id": "b", "text": "MPPT"}, {"id": "c", "text": "RCD"}, {"id": "d", "text": "MCB"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "MPPT (Maximum Power Point Tracking) controllers are more efficient than simple PWM types."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','A combiner box in a PV array is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "join the outputs of several strings into one circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "store electrical energy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "convert DC to AC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure sunlight intensity"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A combiner box brings together the outputs of multiple PV strings, often with fuses, into a single feed."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','Connecting two 12 V solar panels in series gives an output voltage of','[{"id": "a", "text": "6 V"}, {"id": "b", "text": "12 V"}, {"id": "c", "text": "24 V"}, {"id": "d", "text": "48 V"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In series, voltages add up, so two 12 V panels give 24 V."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','Connecting two identical solar panels in parallel will increase the total','[{"id": "a", "text": "voltage only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "current output"}, {"id": "c", "text": "resistance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frequency"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Parallel connection keeps voltage the same while the currents add together."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','A solar system that works together with the public electricity grid and has no batteries is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "grid-tied system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stand-alone system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hybrid system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "portable system"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A grid-tied (on-grid) system feeds power to and draws from the utility grid without battery storage."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','A solar system that uses both batteries and the grid or a generator as backup is described as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "grid-tied system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hybrid system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pure off-grid system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "series system"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A hybrid system combines solar, battery storage and another source such as the grid or a generator."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','When panels are wired in series to raise voltage, the cable carrying the array current is best sized to','[{"id": "a", "text": "carry the rated current safely with low voltage drop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "be as thin as possible to save cost"}, {"id": "c", "text": "match the colour of the roof"}, {"id": "d", "text": "be made only of iron"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cables must be sized to carry the current without overheating and to keep voltage drop low."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','The special connector commonly used to join solar panel cables outdoors is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "RJ45 connector"}, {"id": "b", "text": "MC4 connector"}, {"id": "c", "text": "BNC connector"}, {"id": "d", "text": "USB connector"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "MC4 connectors are the weather-resistant standard for connecting PV module cables."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Which instrument is used to measure the voltage, current and resistance during solar installation testing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "hydrometer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "multimeter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "barometer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "thermometer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A multimeter measures voltage, current and resistance, essential for PV testing."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','The correct tool for making a firm, gas-tight connection of a lug or ferrule onto a cable is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "crimping tool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hacksaw"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spirit level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trowel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A crimping tool presses a lug or connector tightly onto a conductor."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','The instrument used to check whether a mounting rail is horizontal or a pole is vertical is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "clamp meter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "spirit level"}, {"id": "c", "text": "soldering iron"}, {"id": "d", "text": "megger"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A spirit level shows whether a surface is level (horizontal) or plumb (vertical)."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Solar panel mounting frames and structures are usually made of aluminium or galvanised steel mainly because these materials are','[{"id": "a", "text": "very cheap and heavy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "corrosion resistant and durable outdoors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "good electrical insulators"}, {"id": "d", "text": "transparent to light"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Aluminium and galvanised steel resist rust and last long when exposed to weather."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','Before working on the DC side of a solar array in bright sunlight, the installer should remember that the panels are','[{"id": "a", "text": "completely safe and produce no voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "still generating dangerous voltage whenever light falls on them"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only live at night"}, {"id": "d", "text": "live only when connected to a battery"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "PV modules produce voltage whenever exposed to light and cannot simply be switched off like a mains circuit."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','The personal protective equipment that protects an installer''s hands from cuts and electric shock is','[{"id": "a", "text": "safety goggles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "insulated gloves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ear muffs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reflective vest"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Insulated gloves protect the hands from cuts and reduce the risk of electric shock."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','When installing panels on a high rooftop, the most important safety measure to prevent falls is to use a','[{"id": "a", "text": "safety harness with a secure anchor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pair of sunglasses"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wooden ladder laid flat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "raincoat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A properly anchored safety harness is essential to prevent falls when working at height."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','To reduce shock risk while connecting a battery bank, the installer should','[{"id": "a", "text": "wear metal rings and a wristwatch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "use insulated tools and remove metal jewellery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pour water on the terminals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "work with wet hands"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Insulated tools and the removal of metal jewellery prevent accidental short circuits and shock."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','The safest first action if a fire starts at a live solar DC circuit is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "throw water directly on the panels"}, {"id": "b", "text": "isolate the circuit and use a CO2 or dry-powder extinguisher"}, {"id": "c", "text": "touch the wires to check if they are hot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cover the fire with a metal sheet"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Electrical fires are fought by isolating the supply and using CO2 or dry-powder extinguishers, never water."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','A 100 W bulb that runs for 5 hours per day consumes energy of','[{"id": "a", "text": "20 watt-hours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "105 watt-hours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "500 watt-hours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "5000 watt-hours"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Energy equals power times time: 100 W x 5 h = 500 Wh."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','The first step in correctly sizing a solar home system is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "buy the largest inverter available"}, {"id": "b", "text": "estimate the total daily energy demand of the loads"}, {"id": "c", "text": "paint the roof white"}, {"id": "d", "text": "install the batteries first"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sizing begins with an energy audit of the loads to know how much energy must be supplied each day."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','Battery capacity used in solar systems is commonly rated in','[{"id": "a", "text": "ampere-hours (Ah)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "watts (W)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hertz (Hz)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ohms"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Battery storage capacity is expressed in ampere-hours (Ah) at a given voltage."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','If a load needs 1200 Wh per day and one panel produces 300 Wh per day, the minimum number of such panels needed is','[{"id": "a", "text": "2"}, {"id": "b", "text": "3"}, {"id": "c", "text": "4"}, {"id": "d", "text": "6"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "1200 Wh divided by 300 Wh per panel equals 4 panels."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','When sizing an inverter, its continuous power rating should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "less than the total connected load"}, {"id": "b", "text": "at least equal to the total peak load it must run"}, {"id": "c", "text": "exactly zero"}, {"id": "d", "text": "based only on the battery colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An inverter must be rated to handle at least the peak power of the appliances it will run."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','The angle at which a solar panel is fixed relative to the horizontal is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "tilt angle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "phase angle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "power factor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frequency"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The tilt angle is the inclination of the panel from the horizontal plane."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','A general guide for fixed panel tilt at a location is to set the tilt angle roughly equal to the site''s','[{"id": "a", "text": "longitude"}, {"id": "b", "text": "latitude"}, {"id": "c", "text": "altitude in metres"}, {"id": "d", "text": "annual rainfall"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A common rule of thumb sets the fixed tilt angle close to the location''s latitude."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','Solar panels should be mounted in a location that is','[{"id": "a", "text": "shaded by tall trees all day"}, {"id": "b", "text": "free from shading for most of the day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "inside a closed room"}, {"id": "d", "text": "behind a high wall facing north"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Panels must be sited where they receive unobstructed sunlight for most of the day."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','A small air gap is usually left between a roof surface and the back of a solar panel to','[{"id": "a", "text": "allow cooling airflow and reduce heat build-up"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the panel heavier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "store rain water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "block sunlight"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The gap lets air circulate to cool the panel, keeping output higher."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','Panel mounting bolts and clamps must be tightened firmly mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the panel voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent the panels from being blown off by wind"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change the panel colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the tilt angle to zero"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Secure fixing keeps panels from loosening or being lifted by strong winds."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','The most common routine maintenance task that keeps panel output high is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "repaint the panels black"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clean dust and dirt off the panel surface"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add more water to the panels daily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cover the panels with cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dust and dirt block sunlight, so regular cleaning maintains panel output."}',0.45,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','For a flooded lead-acid battery, a routine check is to measure and top up the','[{"id": "a", "text": "electrolyte (distilled water) level"}, {"id": "b", "text": "engine oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "petrol level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brake fluid"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flooded lead-acid batteries need their electrolyte level topped up with distilled water."}',0.55,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','The best time of day to clean solar panels safely is','[{"id": "a", "text": "at midday when panels are very hot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "early morning or evening when panels are cool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "only during rainfall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "at midnight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning cool panels in the early morning or evening avoids thermal shock to hot glass."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','Loose or corroded terminals in a solar system should be inspected during maintenance because they can cause','[{"id": "a", "text": "higher efficiency"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poor connection, heating and power loss"}, {"id": "c", "text": "faster charging"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cooler cables"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Loose or corroded terminals raise resistance, causing overheating and loss of power."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','A device used to record how much energy a solar system produces and how the battery charges over time is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "system monitor or energy meter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hammer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hacksaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "paint brush"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A monitor or energy meter tracks generation and battery state to confirm healthy operation."}',0.5,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','If a solar system suddenly stops working, the first sensible step in fault-finding is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "replace all the panels immediately"}, {"id": "b", "text": "carry out a systematic visual and voltage check of each part"}, {"id": "c", "text": "throw away the batteries"}, {"id": "d", "text": "repaint the inverter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Systematic checking of connections and voltages locates the fault before replacing parts."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A battery that no longer holds charge and discharges very quickly is most likely','[{"id": "a", "text": "brand new"}, {"id": "b", "text": "worn out (sulphated or aged)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "overcharged with sunlight only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "too cold to test"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A battery that will not hold charge is usually worn out or sulphated and needs replacement."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','If a charge controller shows no charging current at midday under clear sky, a likely cause is','[{"id": "a", "text": "a broken or disconnected panel cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "too much sunlight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the panel being too clean"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the battery being new"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "No charging current in good sunlight often points to a broken or loose panel connection."}',0.65,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','An inverter that keeps switching off under normal load and shows a low-battery alarm indicates that the','[{"id": "a", "text": "battery voltage has dropped too low"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sunlight is too strong"}, {"id": "c", "text": "panels are over-cleaned"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cables are too thick"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A low-battery alarm and shutdown mean the battery voltage has fallen below the inverter''s safe limit."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS1','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A blown fuse in the DC combiner box will usually cause','[{"id": "a", "text": "that string to stop delivering power"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the panels to produce more current"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the battery to charge faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "no change at all in the system"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A blown fuse breaks the circuit, so the protected string stops feeding power until replaced."}',0.6,'{SSS1,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which tool is used to section and part the hair before styling?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tail comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blusher brush"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cuticle nipper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Depilatory strip"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tail comb has a long pointed end that is used to make clean partings and sections."}',0.5,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','In a Nigerian salon, the hood dryer is mainly used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "cut split ends"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dry the hair after washing or setting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sterilise metal tools"}, {"id": "d", "text": "remove nail polish"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A hood dryer supplies heat to dry wet or set hair evenly."}',0.5,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','The tool used for trimming and shaping the free edge of the nails is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "orange stick"}, {"id": "b", "text": "buffer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nail clipper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "spatula"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A nail clipper cuts and shortens the free edge of the nail."}',0.5,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which piece of equipment applies controlled heat to press and straighten kinky hair?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hot comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cotton wool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sponge roller"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Emery board"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hot comb is heated and passed through the hair to press and straighten it."}',0.55,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','An orange stick is chiefly used during a manicure to','[{"id": "a", "text": "file the nail plate"}, {"id": "b", "text": "push back the cuticle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "curl the eyelashes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure hair length"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The orange stick is used to gently push back the softened cuticle."}',0.6,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Which material is most suitable for applying toner or removing make-up gently?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton wool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Steel wool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sandpaper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Aluminium foil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cotton wool is soft, absorbent and gentle on the skin for cleansing."}',0.45,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','A neutralising shampoo is used after a relaxer service to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add permanent colour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stop chemical action and restore the hair''s pH"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bleach the scalp"}, {"id": "d", "text": "curl the hair tightly"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Neutralising shampoo halts the relaxer''s action and returns hair to a normal acidic pH."}',0.65,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Which of these is a consumable that must be replaced for each client?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hood dryer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Disposable razor blade"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Styling chair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wash basin"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A disposable blade is single-use and discarded after one client for hygiene."}',0.5,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Base cream (protective cream) is applied to the scalp before relaxing mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "colour the hair black"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect the scalp from chemical burns"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add fragrance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "speed up drying"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Base cream forms a barrier that shields the scalp from the caustic relaxer."}',0.6,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','An emery board is a material used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "file and smooth the nails"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wash the hair"}, {"id": "c", "text": "apply eyeshadow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sterilise combs"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An emery board is an abrasive strip used to file and shape the nail edge."}',0.45,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','The best method of sterilising metal salon tools such as scissors is by using','[{"id": "a", "text": "an autoclave or approved disinfectant"}, {"id": "b", "text": "plain tap water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vegetable oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dry sand"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An autoclave or chemical disinfectant destroys micro-organisms on metal tools."}',0.55,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','Sanitising a workstation between clients is important because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "increases the salon rent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevents cross-infection between clients"}, {"id": "c", "text": "makes the hair grow faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "changes the client''s hair colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sanitising removes germs and stops infections passing from one client to another."}',0.5,'{SSS2,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
