  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','Before opening a desktop computer''s power supply unit, the safest first step is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "unplug it from the mains and allow capacitors to discharge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "switch it on to test the fan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pour water on it to cool it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "connect it to a higher voltage"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Unplugging and waiting lets stored charge in capacitors bleed off, preventing shock."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','In a Nigerian repair workshop with unstable NEPA supply, the best device to protect equipment from voltage surges is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "voltage stabiliser with surge protection"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wooden extension board"}, {"id": "c", "text": "candle lamp"}, {"id": "d", "text": "plastic bucket"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stabiliser regulates voltage and guards equipment against surges and sags."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','A fire caused by an electrical fault in the workshop should be put out using a','[{"id": "a", "text": "CO2 or dry-powder fire extinguisher"}, {"id": "b", "text": "bucket of water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wet cloth soaked in petrol"}, {"id": "d", "text": "handful of sand mixed with fuel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "CO2 or dry-powder extinguishers are safe on live electrical fires; water conducts and worsens them."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T1','CGR-T1-O2','Good workshop practice requires that solder fumes be handled by','[{"id": "a", "text": "using a fume extractor or working in a ventilated area"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sealing all windows tightly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increasing the soldering temperature"}, {"id": "d", "text": "inhaling deeply to test the flux"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Extraction or ventilation removes harmful solder fumes from the breathing zone."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','The component often described as the ''brain'' of the computer that executes instructions is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Central Processing Unit (CPU)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hard disk drive"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Power supply unit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Optical drive"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The CPU processes and executes program instructions, acting as the computer''s brain."}',0.45,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which component provides temporary storage that is lost when the computer is switched off?','[{"id": "a", "text": "RAM"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hard disk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ROM BIOS chip"}, {"id": "d", "text": "CMOS battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "RAM is volatile memory whose contents are lost once power is removed."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','The main board that connects the CPU, RAM, and other components together is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "motherboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "daughter card"}, {"id": "c", "text": "heat sink"}, {"id": "d", "text": "expansion slot cover"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The motherboard is the main printed circuit board linking all core components."}',0.45,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','A small round battery on the motherboard that keeps the system clock and BIOS settings is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "CMOS battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lithium laptop battery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "UPS battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "torch battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The CMOS coin cell powers the real-time clock and stores BIOS configuration."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O1','Which storage device generally gives the fastest boot and data access in a modern computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Solid State Drive (SSD)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Floppy disk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Magnetic tape"}, {"id": "d", "text": "CD-ROM"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An SSD has no moving parts and offers much faster access than mechanical media."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A desktop powers on, fans spin, but there is no display and it gives repeated beep codes. This most likely indicates a fault with the','[{"id": "a", "text": "RAM module or its slot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keyboard cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "printer driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "internet connection"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "POST beep codes with no display commonly point to a faulty or unseated RAM module."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','When installing a CPU, thermal paste is applied between the processor and heat sink in order to','[{"id": "a", "text": "improve heat transfer away from the CPU"}, {"id": "b", "text": "glue the CPU permanently to the socket"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the clock speed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "insulate the CPU from the heat sink"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Thermal paste fills air gaps so heat conducts efficiently to the heat sink."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A computer fails to boot and shows ''No bootable device''. The technician should first check the','[{"id": "a", "text": "hard disk/SSD connection and boot order in BIOS"}, {"id": "b", "text": "brightness of the monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "colour of the casing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "speaker volume"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The message means no OS drive was found, so check drive connection and boot order."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','Before touching the internal components of a computer for repair, a technician should','[{"id": "a", "text": "shut down, unplug the system and discharge static"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase the room humidity to maximum"}, {"id": "c", "text": "run the system at full load"}, {"id": "d", "text": "remove all screws with a magnetised knife"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Powering down, unplugging and discharging static protects both technician and components."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A laptop keeps overheating and shutting down after some minutes of use. The most likely cause is','[{"id": "a", "text": "a dust-clogged fan or dried thermal paste"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a full recycle bin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "too many desktop icons"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a bright wallpaper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Blocked cooling airflow or dried paste causes heat build-up and thermal shutdown."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','In a GSM handset, the section that manages charging, power distribution and voltage regulation is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "power management IC (PMIC) section"}, {"id": "b", "text": "camera module"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loudspeaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vibrator motor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The PMIC handles charging and supplies regulated voltages to the phone''s sections."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','The component in a phone that converts electrical signals into sound during a call is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "earpiece speaker"}, {"id": "b", "text": "microphone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "antenna"}, {"id": "d", "text": "SIM connector"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The earpiece speaker turns electrical audio signals into sound the user hears."}',0.45,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','The unique 15-digit number that identifies a GSM handset on the network is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "IMEI number"}, {"id": "b", "text": "PIN code"}, {"id": "c", "text": "IP address"}, {"id": "d", "text": "MAC serial"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The IMEI is the unique 15-digit identity of the handset on GSM networks."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','In the radio section of a phone, the component responsible for transmitting and receiving RF signals through the antenna is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "RF power amplifier"}, {"id": "b", "text": "display connector"}, {"id": "c", "text": "battery gauge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "touch controller"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The RF power amplifier boosts signals for transmission and works with the antenna."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','The small chip that stores subscriber identity and network details in a GSM phone is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "SIM card"}, {"id": "b", "text": "CPU"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flash memory"}, {"id": "d", "text": "crystal oscillator"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The SIM (Subscriber Identity Module) stores the subscriber and network identity."}',0.45,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','A small two-terminal SMD component marked ''R'' on a phone schematic that limits current is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "resistor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "transistor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "crystal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "connector"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Components labelled ''R'' on schematics are resistors, which limit current."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','On a phone board a component that stores charge and is often used for filtering and decoupling is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "capacitor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fuse"}, {"id": "c", "text": "inductor coil only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "diode bridge"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Capacitors store charge and are used for filtering and decoupling supply lines."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','A diode allows current to flow mainly in','[{"id": "a", "text": "one direction only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "both directions equally"}, {"id": "c", "text": "no direction at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a circular loop only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A diode conducts in one direction and blocks current in the reverse direction."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','When a schematic shows a component labelled ''L'', it usually represents an','[{"id": "a", "text": "inductor (coil)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "LED indicator only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "logic switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "loudspeaker only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The letter ''L'' denotes an inductor or coil on electronic schematics."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','The main advantage of surface-mount (SMD) components over through-hole components in modern phones is that they','[{"id": "a", "text": "are smaller and allow more compact circuit boards"}, {"id": "b", "text": "can only be soldered by hand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "carry much higher household voltages"}, {"id": "d", "text": "never need any soldering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "SMD parts are smaller and let manufacturers pack circuits into compact phone boards."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','A phone shows ''Not charging'' even with a good charger and cable. The first hardware part to inspect is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "charging port (connector) and its solder joints"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rear glass panel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ringtone settings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wallpaper file"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A loose or damaged charging port commonly stops charging even with a good charger."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','A handset displays ''No Service'' in an area with strong network. A likely hardware cause is a fault in the','[{"id": "a", "text": "network/RF section or antenna switch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "camera flash"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vibration motor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "screen brightness sensor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "No Service where signal is strong points to a fault in the RF/network section."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','A phone that is completely dead (no display, no charging indication) should first be tested by','[{"id": "a", "text": "measuring current draw on a DC power supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reinstalling social media apps"}, {"id": "c", "text": "changing the ringtone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "updating the wallpaper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A bench DC supply shows current draw, revealing shorts or an open power path."}',0.65,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','The caller cannot hear the phone owner during calls though the earpiece works. The faulty component is most likely the','[{"id": "a", "text": "microphone (mic)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "earpiece speaker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "SIM card"}, {"id": "d", "text": "battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "If the caller cannot hear the user, the transmitting microphone is the likely fault."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','A phone battery drains very fast and the phone gets hot even while idle. The most likely cause is','[{"id": "a", "text": "a swollen/faulty battery or a shorted component drawing current"}, {"id": "b", "text": "too many contacts saved"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a bright ringtone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a long phone name"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rapid drain with heat at idle points to a bad battery or a component drawing excess current."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','The process of reattaching a BGA chip by reflowing new solder balls under it is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "reballing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "formatting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flashing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "jailbreaking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Reballing places fresh solder balls under a BGA chip before reflowing it onto the board."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','When using a hot-air rework station to remove an SMD component, setting the temperature far too high can','[{"id": "a", "text": "burn the board and lift copper pads"}, {"id": "b", "text": "improve the phone''s battery life"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the network signal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make the solder permanently liquid"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Excess heat damages the PCB and can lift or burn the copper pads and tracks."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A good solder joint on a phone board should appear','[{"id": "a", "text": "shiny, smooth and cone-shaped"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dull, cracked and grainy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "black and burnt"}, {"id": "d", "text": "loose and ball-like on one side"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A well-made joint is shiny, smooth and well-formed, showing good solder wetting."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','Before soldering a new component, the tip of the soldering iron should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "cleaned and tinned with a little solder"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dipped in cold water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rubbed with sandpaper while hot"}, {"id": "d", "text": "coated with engine oil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clean, tinned tip transfers heat well and produces reliable joints."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','A jumper wire is used in board-level repair to','[{"id": "a", "text": "bridge a broken track and restore a connection"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase the phone''s screen size"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add extra RAM to the phone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "replace the battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A jumper wire reconnects a broken PCB track so current can flow again."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','Loading fresh firmware onto a phone to fix software problems is commonly called','[{"id": "a", "text": "flashing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reballing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "soldering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "defragmenting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flashing writes new firmware to the phone to correct software faults."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','Before flashing a customer''s smartphone, the most important precaution is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "back up the customer''s data where possible"}, {"id": "b", "text": "remove the phone''s camera"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the screen brightness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "change the phone casing colour"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flashing can erase data, so backing up first protects the customer''s information."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A software tool used to write a fresh Windows operating system onto a computer is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "bootable installation USB/DVD"}, {"id": "b", "text": "soldering iron"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hot-air gun"}, {"id": "d", "text": "multimeter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A bootable USB or DVD carries the OS installer used to set up Windows."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A smartphone is stuck on the manufacturer''s logo and will not boot fully. This is best classified as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "software (firmware) fault often fixed by flashing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cracked screen glass fault"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dead battery only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "broken charging port only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A logo boot-loop is typically a firmware issue that flashing can resolve."}',0.6,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','Installing genuine, licensed software and drivers on a repaired computer is important because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "ensures stability, updates and avoids malware from cracked copies"}, {"id": "b", "text": "makes the screen physically larger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increases the RAM chip size"}, {"id": "d", "text": "removes the need for a power supply"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Genuine software receives updates and avoids malware bundled in cracked copies."}',0.55,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','A customer brings a phone for screen replacement. Good ethics require the technician to','[{"id": "a", "text": "give a clear quotation and get consent before starting work"}, {"id": "b", "text": "swap out other good parts secretly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "keep the customer''s SIM card"}, {"id": "d", "text": "start repair without telling the price"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honest practice means quoting the cost and getting the customer''s consent first."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Keeping a record book of jobs received, faults and charges in a repair business mainly helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "track work, avoid disputes and manage income"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase the phone''s signal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cool the soldering iron"}, {"id": "d", "text": "charge the batteries faster"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A job record helps trace work done, settle disputes and monitor business income."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Offering a warranty on a repair job to a customer means the technician agrees to','[{"id": "a", "text": "fix the same fault free within an agreed period if it recurs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "never repair that phone again"}, {"id": "c", "text": "keep the phone permanently"}, {"id": "d", "text": "charge double for the same fault"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A warranty commits the technician to re-fix the same fault free within the agreed time."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','When a fault is beyond a technician''s tools or skill, the most professional action is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "refer the customer to a better-equipped technician honestly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "damage the board further to hide it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "keep the phone without explanation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "deny that the phone was ever brought"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Honest referral protects the customer and the technician''s reputation."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','A technician who buys spare parts in bulk and marks up a fair price before reselling is applying the business idea of','[{"id": "a", "text": "making profit through buying and selling"}, {"id": "b", "text": "giving all parts away free"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoiding record keeping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "refusing to serve customers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Buying at lower cost and selling at a fair margin is the basic way a business earns profit."}',0.5,'{SSS2,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','In a spreadsheet, the intersection of a row and a column is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "range"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cell"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sheet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "field"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A cell is the box formed where a single row and a single column meet."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','The cell reference formed by the third column and fifth row of a worksheet is','[{"id": "a", "text": "5C"}, {"id": "b", "text": "3E"}, {"id": "c", "text": "C5"}, {"id": "d", "text": "E3"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The third column is C and the fifth row is 5, giving C5."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','A group of adjacent cells selected together, such as B2 to B10, is known as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "range"}, {"id": "b", "text": "label"}, {"id": "c", "text": "macro"}, {"id": "d", "text": "query"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A block of neighbouring cells like B2:B10 is called a range."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','When a formula in C1 uses $A$1 and is copied to C2, the reference remains A1 because $A$1 is a(n)','[{"id": "a", "text": "relative reference"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mixed reference"}, {"id": "c", "text": "absolute reference"}, {"id": "d", "text": "circular reference"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The dollar signs lock both column and row, making it an absolute reference that does not change when copied."}',0.65,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','The document produced by a spreadsheet package such as Microsoft Excel is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "presentation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "workbook"}, {"id": "c", "text": "database"}, {"id": "d", "text": "publication"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An Excel file, which contains one or more worksheets, is called a workbook."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','Every formula entered into a spreadsheet cell must begin with the sign','[{"id": "a", "text": "#"}, {"id": "b", "text": "="}, {"id": "c", "text": "@"}, {"id": "d", "text": "&"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The equals sign tells the spreadsheet that the entry is a formula to be calculated."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','To add the values in cells A1 through A5, the correct function is','[{"id": "a", "text": "=ADD(A1:A5)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "=TOTAL(A1:A5)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "=SUM(A1:A5)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "=PLUS(A1:A5)"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "SUM is the standard function that totals a range of values."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','A shop owner uses =AVERAGE(B2:B6) to find the mean daily sales. The AVERAGE function returns the','[{"id": "a", "text": "highest value in the range"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sum of the values"}, {"id": "c", "text": "arithmetic mean of the values"}, {"id": "d", "text": "count of the cells"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "AVERAGE divides the sum of the values by how many there are to give the mean."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','The function =IF(C2>=50,"PASS","FAIL") will display FAIL when the value in C2 is','[{"id": "a", "text": "exactly 50"}, {"id": "b", "text": "less than 50"}, {"id": "c", "text": "greater than 50"}, {"id": "d", "text": "50 or more"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The condition C2>=50 is false only when the value is below 50, so FAIL is shown."}',0.65,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','To count how many cells in the range D2:D20 contain numbers, a student should use','[{"id": "a", "text": "=SUM(D2:D20)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "=COUNT(D2:D20)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "=MAX(D2:D20)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "=ROUND(D2:D20)"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "COUNT returns the number of cells that hold numeric values within a range."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','In a database table, a single row that holds all the details of one item is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "field"}, {"id": "b", "text": "record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "query"}, {"id": "d", "text": "form"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A record is one complete row containing all the fields describing a single entity."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','A single column such as Surname or Phone Number in a database table is known as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "field"}, {"id": "d", "text": "report"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A field is a single column that holds one category of data for every record."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','The field that uniquely identifies each record in a table, such as a student''s registration number, is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "foreign key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "primary key"}, {"id": "c", "text": "composite field"}, {"id": "d", "text": "index field"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A primary key uniquely identifies every record and cannot be duplicated."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','Examples of Database Management System software include Microsoft Access and','[{"id": "a", "text": "CorelDraw"}, {"id": "b", "text": "MySQL"}, {"id": "c", "text": "PowerPoint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Photoshop"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "MySQL, like Microsoft Access, is software used to create and manage databases."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','An organised collection of related data stored so that it can be easily accessed and managed is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "spreadsheet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "database"}, {"id": "c", "text": "webpage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "folder"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A database is a structured, organised store of related data for easy retrieval and management."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','In Microsoft Access, the object used to retrieve specific records that meet a stated condition is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "form"}, {"id": "b", "text": "report"}, {"id": "c", "text": "query"}, {"id": "d", "text": "macro"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A query extracts records that match given criteria from one or more tables."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Arranging student records from A to Z by surname is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "filtering"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sorting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "indexing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "merging"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sorting arranges records in a defined order such as alphabetical order."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','The database object best suited for entering and editing data one record at a time on screen is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "form"}, {"id": "b", "text": "query"}, {"id": "c", "text": "report"}, {"id": "d", "text": "table"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A form provides a user-friendly interface for entering and editing one record at a time."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','A clerk wants a neatly formatted, printable summary of all customers for management. The best object to use is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "form"}, {"id": "b", "text": "query"}, {"id": "c", "text": "report"}, {"id": "d", "text": "table"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A report presents data in a formatted layout designed for printing and presentation."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Displaying only records where State = "Lagos" while temporarily hiding the others is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "sorting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "filtering"}, {"id": "c", "text": "formatting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "validating"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Filtering shows only the records matching a condition and hides the rest."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','A network that connects computers within a single building or school is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "WAN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "LAN"}, {"id": "c", "text": "MAN"}, {"id": "d", "text": "PAN"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A Local Area Network (LAN) covers a small area such as one building or school."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','A network that spans a very large geographical area, such as connecting offices across Nigeria, is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "LAN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "PAN"}, {"id": "c", "text": "WAN"}, {"id": "d", "text": "VPN"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A Wide Area Network (WAN) links computers over large distances, even across the country."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','Which of the following is a wireless transmission medium?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Coaxial cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Twisted pair"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fibre optic cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Radio waves"}]','{"correct": ["d"], "explanation": "Radio waves carry data through the air without cables, making them a wireless medium."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','The transmission medium that uses light signals through glass strands and offers very high speed is','[{"id": "a", "text": "twisted pair cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fibre optic cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "coaxial cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "telephone wire"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fibre optic cable transmits data as pulses of light, giving very high speed and bandwidth."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','The device that connects two or more different networks and directs data along the best path is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "router"}, {"id": "b", "text": "monitor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "scanner"}, {"id": "d", "text": "plotter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A router connects networks together and chooses the best path to forward data."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The global network of interconnected computers that allows worldwide communication is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "intranet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "internet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "extranet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ethernet"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The internet is the worldwide network linking millions of computers for communication."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','A software program used to access and view websites, such as Google Chrome, is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "search engine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "web browser"}, {"id": "c", "text": "web server"}, {"id": "d", "text": "protocol"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A web browser like Chrome retrieves and displays web pages for the user."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','Google and Bing are examples of tools used to find information on the web, called','[{"id": "a", "text": "web browsers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "search engines"}, {"id": "c", "text": "email clients"}, {"id": "d", "text": "firewalls"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A search engine such as Google helps locate information across websites on the internet."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','In the email address ojo@gmail.com, the part that identifies the mail service provider is','[{"id": "a", "text": "ojo"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the @ sign"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gmail.com"}, {"id": "d", "text": ".com only"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The portion after the @ sign, gmail.com, identifies the mail host or domain."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The unique address that locates a specific web page, such as www.waec.org, is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "URL"}, {"id": "b", "text": "HTML"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ISP"}, {"id": "d", "text": "FTP"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A URL (Uniform Resource Locator) is the unique address of a resource on the web."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','A secret word or string of characters used to restrict access to a computer system is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "username"}, {"id": "b", "text": "password"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hyperlink"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cookie"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A password is a secret code that controls who may access a system or account."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Keeping an extra copy of important data on another storage device in case the original is lost is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "formatting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "backup"}, {"id": "c", "text": "encryption"}, {"id": "d", "text": "defragmenting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A backup is a spare copy of data kept safe so it can be restored if the original is lost."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Converting data into a coded form so that only authorised people can read it is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "compression"}, {"id": "b", "text": "encryption"}, {"id": "c", "text": "validation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sorting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Encryption scrambles data into a coded form readable only by those with the key."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','A hardware or software system that monitors and controls incoming and outgoing network traffic to block threats is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "firewall"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gateway"}, {"id": "c", "text": "modem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "server"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A firewall filters network traffic to protect a system from unauthorised access."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Which of the following is the strongest password?','[{"id": "a", "text": "12345"}, {"id": "b", "text": "password"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ng#7pXq2!"}, {"id": "d", "text": "myname"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Ng#7pXq2! mixes upper and lower case, digits and symbols, making it hard to guess."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','A program written to damage files or disrupt the normal working of a computer is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "utility"}, {"id": "b", "text": "virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "compiler"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A computer virus is malicious software designed to harm or disrupt a computer."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Software specifically designed to detect and remove viruses from a computer is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "antivirus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "spreadsheet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "browser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "spyware"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Antivirus software scans for, detects and removes viruses and other malware."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Which of the following is a common way a computer virus can spread?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Shutting down the system correctly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Opening infected email attachments"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cleaning the keyboard regularly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increasing screen brightness"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Viruses often spread through infected email attachments and shared storage devices."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','To keep an antivirus program effective against new threats, a user must regularly','[{"id": "a", "text": "delete the antivirus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "update its virus definitions"}, {"id": "c", "text": "disable the firewall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the RAM"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Regularly updating virus definitions lets the antivirus recognise newly created viruses."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Scanning a friend''s flash drive before opening its files is a good practice because flash drives can','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase internet speed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "carry and transfer viruses"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cool the computer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "improve the monitor display"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Removable drives commonly carry viruses, so scanning them first prevents infection."}',0.55,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','Which of the following is a word processing package?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Excel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Word"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Access"}, {"id": "d", "text": "CorelDraw"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Microsoft Word is a word processing package used to create and edit text documents."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','Making a selected heading appear thick and darker for emphasis is done using the','[{"id": "a", "text": "italics tool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "underline tool"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bold tool"}, {"id": "d", "text": "highlight tool"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The bold tool makes text appear thicker and darker to give it emphasis."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','The word processing feature that automatically checks a document for spelling mistakes is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "mail merge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "spell check"}, {"id": "c", "text": "word wrap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "thesaurus"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The spell check feature scans the document and flags misspelled words."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','A secretary must send the same letter to 200 customers, each with a different name and address. The best feature to use is','[{"id": "a", "text": "word wrap"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mail merge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spell check"}, {"id": "d", "text": "drop cap"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Mail merge combines one main document with a list of names and addresses to produce many personalised letters."}',0.65,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','The feature that automatically moves text to the next line when the current line is full, without pressing Enter, is','[{"id": "a", "text": "word wrap"}, {"id": "b", "text": "line spacing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "indentation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "justification"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Word wrap automatically continues text on the next line when a line becomes full."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','The application package commonly used to create slide presentations is Microsoft','[{"id": "a", "text": "Word"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Excel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "PowerPoint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Access"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Microsoft PowerPoint is used to design and deliver slide presentations."}',0.45,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','A single page in a presentation on which text and images are placed is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "sheet"}, {"id": "b", "text": "slide"}, {"id": "c", "text": "record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frame"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Each page of a PowerPoint presentation is called a slide."}',0.5,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','The visual effect controlling how one slide changes to the next during a show is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "transition"}, {"id": "b", "text": "template"}, {"id": "c", "text": "footer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hyperlink"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A slide transition is the visual effect used when moving from one slide to another."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','Motion effects applied to text or objects within a single slide are known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "animations"}, {"id": "b", "text": "transitions"}, {"id": "c", "text": "themes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bullets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Animations control the movement or appearance of items on an individual slide."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','To run a PowerPoint presentation in full screen from the first slide, a presenter can press','[{"id": "a", "text": "F1"}, {"id": "b", "text": "F5"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Esc"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tab"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pressing F5 starts the slide show from the beginning in full screen."}',0.6,'{SSS2,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Which hand tool is used to strip the insulation from a copper conductor before making a joint?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wire stripper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ball-pein hammer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bradawl"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Try square"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A wire stripper removes insulation cleanly without cutting the conductor strands."}',0.45,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','An electrician needs to make a hole in a wooden board to mount a wooden conduit saddle. Which tool is most appropriate?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hacksaw"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bradawl"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pliers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Screwdriver"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A bradawl makes a small starting hole in wood for screws."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','The tool used mainly for cutting conduit pipe and metal in electrical work is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "chisel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hacksaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mallet"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A hacksaw fitted with a metal-cutting blade is used to cut conduit and metal parts."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Which pair of pliers is best suited for gripping and cutting wires in confined spaces such as a conduit box?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Combination pliers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Long-nose pliers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Slip-joint pliers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Water-pump pliers"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Long-nose pliers reach into tight spaces to grip and bend small wires."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','The correct tool for tightening a terminal screw on a 13 A socket outlet is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "spanner"}, {"id": "b", "text": "screwdriver"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chisel"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hammer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A screwdriver matches the slotted or cross terminal screws used on socket outlets."}',0.45,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','Which instrument is used to measure the insulation resistance of a completed wiring installation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ammeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Megger (insulation resistance tester)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Voltmeter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wattmeter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A megger applies a high test voltage to measure insulation resistance in megohms."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','A multimeter set to the ohms range is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "measure electrical power"}, {"id": "b", "text": "test continuity and measure resistance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure light intensity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure the speed of a motor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "On the ohms range a multimeter checks continuity and reads resistance values."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The conductor material most commonly used for domestic wiring cables in Nigeria because of its good conductivity and low cost is','[{"id": "a", "text": "iron"}, {"id": "b", "text": "aluminium foil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "copper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silver"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Copper is widely used for wiring because it conducts well and is affordable compared with silver."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','PVC is used as the covering of a cable mainly because it is a good','[{"id": "a", "text": "conductor of heat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "insulator"}, {"id": "c", "text": "conductor of electricity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "magnetic material"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "PVC is a good insulator, so it prevents contact with the live conductor."}',0.45,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The cross-sectional area of a cable conductor is normally expressed in','[{"id": "a", "text": "amperes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "square millimetres"}, {"id": "c", "text": "volts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "watts"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cable size is given by conductor cross-sectional area in square millimetres."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','Before working on a circuit, the first safety action an electrician must take is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "wear sunglasses"}, {"id": "b", "text": "isolate (switch off) the supply and prove it is dead"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the supply voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "remove the earth wire"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isolating the supply and confirming it is dead prevents electric shock."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The main purpose of earthing the metal casing of an electrical appliance is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the current drawn"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect the user from electric shock if a fault occurs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "improve the appearance of the appliance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the cost of wiring"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Earthing gives fault current a safe path and blows the fuse, protecting the user."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The correct first-aid response when a person is in contact with a live conductor is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "pull the victim with your bare hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pour water on the victim"}, {"id": "c", "text": "switch off the supply before touching the victim"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leave the victim and run for help"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Switching off the supply first prevents the rescuer from also being shocked."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The type of fire extinguisher recommended for an electrical fire is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "water type"}, {"id": "b", "text": "carbon dioxide (CO2) type"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sand bucket only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "foam type"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A CO2 extinguisher is non-conductive and safe for live electrical fires."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','Rubber-soled shoes are worn by electricians during work because rubber is','[{"id": "a", "text": "a good conductor of electricity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "an insulator that reduces the risk of shock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "magnetic"}, {"id": "d", "text": "heavier than leather"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rubber insulates the wearer from the ground, lowering the chance of electric shock."}',0.45,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A fuse in a circuit is designed to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the current flow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "melt and break the circuit when excess current flows"}, {"id": "c", "text": "store electrical charge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "convert AC to DC"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A fuse element melts under excessive current, breaking the circuit for protection."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','Which protective device automatically disconnects the supply when a small earth-leakage current is detected?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Residual current device (RCD/ELCB)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Isolator switch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dimmer switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Capacitor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An RCD trips on earth-leakage current, protecting against shock."}',0.65,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A miniature circuit breaker (MCB) is preferred to a rewireable fuse because the MCB','[{"id": "a", "text": "cannot be reset once tripped"}, {"id": "b", "text": "can be reset after clearing the fault"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increases the fault current"}, {"id": "d", "text": "needs no enclosure"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An MCB can simply be switched back on after the fault is cleared, unlike a fuse wire."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A yellow triangle sign showing a black lightning arrow in the workshop warns of','[{"id": "a", "text": "a first-aid box"}, {"id": "b", "text": "risk of electric shock / danger of electricity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a fire exit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "drinking water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The lightning-arrow triangle is the standard warning for electrical shock hazard."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','The fuse should always be connected in the','[{"id": "a", "text": "neutral conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "earth conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "live (phase) conductor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "middle of the appliance"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Placing the fuse in the live conductor isolates the appliance from the supply when it blows."}',0.65,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','Ohm''s law states that the current in a conductor is directly proportional to the applied voltage and inversely proportional to the','[{"id": "a", "text": "power"}, {"id": "b", "text": "resistance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "charge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frequency"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ohm''s law gives I = V/R, so current is inversely proportional to resistance."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','A 240 V supply is connected across a heater of resistance 60 ohms. The current flowing is','[{"id": "a", "text": "2 A"}, {"id": "b", "text": "4 A"}, {"id": "c", "text": "6 A"}, {"id": "d", "text": "14 400 A"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "I = V/R = 240/60 = 4 A."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','An electric iron rated 1000 W is used on a 250 V supply. The current it draws is','[{"id": "a", "text": "0.25 A"}, {"id": "b", "text": "4 A"}, {"id": "c", "text": "40 A"}, {"id": "d", "text": "250 000 A"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "I = P/V = 1000/250 = 4 A."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','The SI unit of electrical resistance is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ampere"}, {"id": "b", "text": "volt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ohm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "watt"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Resistance is measured in ohms (symbol capital omega)."}',0.45,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','Electrical power in a resistive circuit is correctly given by the expression','[{"id": "a", "text": "P = V/I"}, {"id": "b", "text": "P = V x I"}, {"id": "c", "text": "P = I/V"}, {"id": "d", "text": "P = V + I"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Power equals voltage multiplied by current, P = VI."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','Two resistors of 3 ohms and 6 ohms are connected in series. Their total resistance is','[{"id": "a", "text": "2 ohms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "9 ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "18 ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "0.5 ohm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In series, resistances add: 3 + 6 = 9 ohms."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','Two lamps of 6 ohms each are connected in parallel. Their combined resistance is','[{"id": "a", "text": "12 ohms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "6 ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "3 ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "36 ohms"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "For two equal parallel resistors, total = R/2 = 6/2 = 3 ohms."}',0.65,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','Lamps in a house are usually connected in parallel so that','[{"id": "a", "text": "one blown lamp turns off all the others"}, {"id": "b", "text": "each lamp gets the full supply voltage and works independently"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the total current is reduced to zero"}, {"id": "d", "text": "less copper is used than any other method"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In parallel each lamp receives full voltage and one can fail without affecting the rest."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','In a series circuit, the current flowing through each component is','[{"id": "a", "text": "different at every point"}, {"id": "b", "text": "the same at every point"}, {"id": "c", "text": "always zero"}, {"id": "d", "text": "equal to the voltage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A series circuit has one path, so the same current flows through every component."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','The total voltage across resistors connected in series is equal to the','[{"id": "a", "text": "voltage across the largest resistor only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sum of the voltages across each resistor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "product of the individual voltages"}, {"id": "d", "text": "difference between the two smallest voltages"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In series the applied voltage is shared, so it equals the sum of the individual voltage drops."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','A wiring system in which cables are drawn through metal or PVC tubes fixed to the wall is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "conduit wiring"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cleat wiring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "batten wiring"}, {"id": "d", "text": "casing and capping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Conduit wiring runs cables inside protective tubes (conduits)."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','In a standard three-core flexible cable to Nigerian/IEE colour code, the green-and-yellow conductor is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "live conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "neutral conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "earth conductor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "control conductor"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Green-and-yellow is the standard colour for the earth (protective) conductor."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','The accessory used to join and protect the ends of cables where they meet inside a conduit system is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "junction (conduit) box"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ceiling rose"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lamp holder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dimmer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A junction/conduit box encloses and protects cable joints."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','The device fixed on the ceiling to which the flexible cable of a pendant lamp is connected is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "consumer unit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ceiling rose"}, {"id": "c", "text": "socket outlet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "isolator"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A ceiling rose provides the fixing and connection point for a pendant lamp flex."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','Casing and capping wiring uses which material to enclose the cables?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Grooved plastic or wooden channels with a cover"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Glass tubes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rubber hoses"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Iron rods"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Casing and capping uses a grooved channel (casing) closed by a cover strip (capping)."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','A switch that controls a single lamp from one position is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "one-way switch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "two-way switch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "intermediate switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dimmer switch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A one-way switch turns a lamp on or off from a single point."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','To control one lamp from two different positions, for example at the top and bottom of a staircase, the electrician uses','[{"id": "a", "text": "two one-way switches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "two two-way switches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "one dimmer switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a push-button bell"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Two two-way switches allow the same lamp to be operated from either position."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','A switch must always be connected in the live conductor so that when it is off, the appliance is','[{"id": "a", "text": "still connected to the live supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "disconnected from the live supply and safe"}, {"id": "c", "text": "connected only to earth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "supplied with double voltage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Switching the live conductor makes the appliance dead and safe to touch when off."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','A ring final circuit for 13 A socket outlets in a Nigerian home is commonly protected by a fuse or MCB rated','[{"id": "a", "text": "5 A"}, {"id": "b", "text": "15 A"}, {"id": "c", "text": "30 A (or 32 A)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "100 A"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A ring final circuit is normally protected by a 30 A fuse or 32 A MCB."}',0.7,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','In a correctly wired 13 A plug, the brown conductor should be connected to the','[{"id": "a", "text": "earth terminal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "live terminal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "neutral terminal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fuse holder cover"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Brown is the live conductor colour and goes to the live (fused) terminal."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','An electric motor is a machine that converts','[{"id": "a", "text": "electrical energy into mechanical energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mechanical energy into electrical energy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "heat energy into light energy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "chemical energy into sound energy"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A motor changes electrical energy into rotational mechanical energy."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A machine that converts mechanical energy into electrical energy is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "transformer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "generator"}, {"id": "c", "text": "battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rectifier"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A generator converts mechanical (rotational) energy into electrical energy."}',0.5,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A transformer that increases the voltage from primary to secondary is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "step-down transformer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "step-up transformer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "isolation transformer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "current transformer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A step-up transformer has more secondary turns and raises the output voltage."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A transformer operates on the principle of','[{"id": "a", "text": "electromagnetic induction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chemical reaction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "static friction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gravitational force"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A transformer transfers energy between windings by mutual electromagnetic induction."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','Compared with an incandescent filament lamp, a fluorescent tube of the same brightness is preferred because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "uses more electrical energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "is more energy-efficient and lasts longer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "produces no light"}, {"id": "d", "text": "needs no electrical supply"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A fluorescent tube gives the same light for less power and has a longer life."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','A lamp fails to light and testing shows no continuity through its filament. The most likely fault is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "short circuit in the lamp"}, {"id": "b", "text": "blown (open-circuit) filament"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reversed polarity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "overloaded neutral"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "No continuity means the filament is broken, giving an open circuit."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','When a live conductor accidentally touches a neutral conductor with negligible resistance between them, the fault is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "open circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "short circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "high-resistance joint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "power factor fault"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A direct low-resistance contact between live and neutral is a short circuit."}',0.6,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','If a fuse blows again immediately each time it is replaced, the electrician should first','[{"id": "a", "text": "fit a much larger fuse to stop it blowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "find and clear the fault before replacing the fuse"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bridge the fuse with a nail"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ignore it and switch on"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Repeated blowing indicates a fault that must be located and cleared, not bypassed."}',0.65,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','A high-resistance joint in a circuit is undesirable mainly because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "produces excessive heat at the joint"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increases the supply voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "improves conductivity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cools the conductor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A loose or high-resistance joint dissipates power as heat and can cause a fire."}',0.65,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','Routine preventive maintenance of an installation should include','[{"id": "a", "text": "tightening loose connections and cleaning contacts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "removing all earth wires"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increasing every fuse rating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "disconnecting the main switch permanently"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Preventive maintenance tightens connections and cleans contacts to avoid faults."}',0.55,'{SSS2,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which tool is used specifically for cutting fabric in a garment-making workshop?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pinking shears"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tailor''s shears"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Paper scissors"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Seam ripper"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tailor''s shears have long blades and a bent handle designed for cutting fabric flat on a table."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','A seam ripper is used mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "cut out pattern pieces"}, {"id": "b", "text": "remove wrongly sewn stitches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "press open seams"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark buttonholes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A seam ripper unpicks and removes stitches that have been sewn incorrectly."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','The tool used to transfer pattern markings onto fabric using a tracing wheel is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "tailor''s chalk"}, {"id": "b", "text": "bodkin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dressmaker''s carbon paper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "thimble"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Dressmaker''s carbon paper is used with a tracing wheel to transfer markings onto fabric."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','A thimble is worn on the finger during hand sewing to','[{"id": "a", "text": "measure the seam allowance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect the finger and push the needle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hold pins temporarily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "thread the needle easily"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The thimble protects the finger and helps push the needle through thick fabric."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which measuring tool is flexible and most suitable for taking body measurements?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Metre rule"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Set square"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tape measure"}, {"id": "d", "text": "L-square"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A flexible tape measure follows body curves, making it ideal for taking body measurements."}',0.45,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Before threading or oiling a sewing machine, the safest first step is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "raise the presser foot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "switch off or unplug the machine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lower the needle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wind the bobbin"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Switching off or unplugging prevents accidental starting and injury during maintenance."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Pins and needles should be kept in a pin cushion mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "keep them sharp forever"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent injury and loss"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make them rust faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "colour-code the sizes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pin cushion keeps sharp pins and needles together, reducing the risk of injury and loss."}',0.45,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','A common cause of a sewing machine skipping stitches is','[{"id": "a", "text": "using a well-oiled machine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a blunt or wrongly fitted needle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a full bobbin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "correct thread tension"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A blunt, bent or wrongly inserted needle commonly causes skipped stitches."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Routine oiling of the moving parts of a sewing machine is done to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the thread tension"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reduce friction and wear"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change the stitch length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "clean the fabric"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oiling reduces friction between moving parts, preventing wear and keeping the machine running smoothly."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','To keep the workshop safe, electrical iron cords and machine cables should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "left across the walkway"}, {"id": "b", "text": "checked and kept free of cuts or fraying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wrapped in wet cloth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "tied to the ceiling fan"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cords must be inspected and free of damage to prevent electric shock and fire hazards."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which of the following is a natural fibre obtained from a plant?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Silk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Polyester"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cotton is a natural cellulose fibre obtained from the cotton plant."}',0.45,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Silk and wool are both classified as','[{"id": "a", "text": "synthetic fibres"}, {"id": "b", "text": "natural animal fibres"}, {"id": "c", "text": "natural plant fibres"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mineral fibres"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Silk comes from the silkworm and wool from sheep, so both are natural animal fibres."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which fibre is fully man-made (synthetic)?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Linen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Jute"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Polyester"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wool"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Polyester is a synthetic fibre manufactured from petrochemicals."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','A major advantage of cotton fabric for tropical Nigerian wear is that it','[{"id": "a", "text": "melts under heat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "absorbs moisture and is comfortable in heat"}, {"id": "c", "text": "never creases"}, {"id": "d", "text": "is fully waterproof"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cotton is absorbent and breathable, making it comfortable in a hot climate."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','The simple test in which a fibre burns with the smell of burning paper and leaves soft grey ash indicates a','[{"id": "a", "text": "cellulose (cotton/linen) fibre"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protein (wool/silk) fibre"}, {"id": "c", "text": "nylon fibre"}, {"id": "d", "text": "polyester fibre"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cellulose fibres like cotton burn like paper and leave a soft grey ash."}',0.65,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Delicate fabrics such as silk are best washed by','[{"id": "a", "text": "hard scrubbing with a brush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gentle hand washing in mild soap"}, {"id": "c", "text": "boiling in hot water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "soaking in bleach overnight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Silk is delicate and should be gently hand washed in mild soap to avoid damage."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','A hot iron setting is most suitable for which fabric?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Polyester"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Acetate"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cotton withstands high heat, so a hot iron gives the best pressing results."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Synthetic fabrics like nylon should be ironed with a','[{"id": "a", "text": "very hot iron"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cool or warm iron"}, {"id": "c", "text": "iron dipped in water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "red-hot charcoal iron"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Nylon is heat-sensitive and can melt, so a cool or warm iron is used."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','The main purpose of a care label sewn into a garment is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "show the price of the garment"}, {"id": "b", "text": "guide washing, drying and ironing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "identify the tailor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure the wearer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Care labels give instructions on how to wash, dry and iron the garment safely."}',0.45,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','White cotton fabric that has become dull and grey is best brightened by','[{"id": "a", "text": "adding a suitable bleach or blue during laundering"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ironing it at a low temperature"}, {"id": "c", "text": "drying it indoors only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "washing in cold water without soap"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bleaching or adding blue (whitening agent) restores brightness to dulled white cotton."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','When taking the bust measurement, the tape measure should be passed','[{"id": "a", "text": "around the fullest part of the bust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "around the narrowest part of the waist"}, {"id": "c", "text": "around the widest part of the hip"}, {"id": "d", "text": "across the shoulder blades only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The bust measurement is taken around the fullest part of the bust, kept level."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The waist measurement is taken around the','[{"id": "a", "text": "fullest part of the hip"}, {"id": "b", "text": "smallest part of the trunk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "base of the neck"}, {"id": "d", "text": "middle of the thigh"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The waist is measured around the smallest part of the trunk, usually tied with a string as a guide."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','For a correct fit, body measurements should be taken','[{"id": "a", "text": "over heavy outer garments"}, {"id": "b", "text": "over light clothing with the tape held snug, not tight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "with the tape pulled very tight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "with the tape hanging loosely"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Measurements are taken over light clothing with the tape snug but not tight for accuracy."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','Which measurement is needed to determine the length of a full-length skirt?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Neck to bust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Waist to desired hem length"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shoulder to shoulder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wrist to elbow"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Skirt length is measured from the waist down to the desired hem level."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The measurement taken around the fullest part of the seat is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "waist measurement"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hip measurement"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bust measurement"}, {"id": "d", "text": "back width"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The hip measurement is taken around the fullest part of the hips/seat."}',0.45,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','The straight grain line on a fabric runs','[{"id": "a", "text": "across the width, from selvedge to selvedge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "parallel to the selvedge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "diagonally at 45 degrees"}, {"id": "d", "text": "in a circular direction"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The lengthwise straight grain runs parallel to the selvedge and gives the strongest hang."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','The bias of a fabric is the direction that runs at','[{"id": "a", "text": "90 degrees to the selvedge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "0 degrees along the selvedge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "45 degrees to the selvedge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "parallel to the hem"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The true bias runs at 45 degrees to the selvedge and has the most stretch."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','Seam allowance added to a pattern piece before cutting is the extra fabric that allows for','[{"id": "a", "text": "decoration only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "joining the pieces together with stitches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shrinking the pattern"}, {"id": "d", "text": "colour fastness"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Seam allowance is the margin beyond the seam line used to stitch pieces together."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','Before cutting out, pattern pieces are pinned to the fabric mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add colour to the fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hold them firmly in place so they do not shift"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the seam allowance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "press the fabric"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pinning holds the pattern securely so it does not move while cutting."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','Notches marked on a pattern edge are used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "show the ironing temperature"}, {"id": "b", "text": "match corresponding pieces when joining"}, {"id": "c", "text": "indicate the fabric colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark the buttonhole size"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Notches help align and correctly match seams when joining pattern pieces."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Which temporary stitch is used to hold fabric layers together before permanent stitching?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Back stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tacking (basting) stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hemming stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overcasting stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tacking (basting) is a temporary long stitch that holds layers before final sewing."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','The hand stitch that most closely resembles machine stitching in strength is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "running stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "back stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tacking stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "gathering stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The back stitch is strong and firm, resembling machine stitching."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Overcasting or overlocking a raw edge is done mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add decoration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent the edge from fraying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gather the fabric"}, {"id": "d", "text": "shorten the garment"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Overcasting neatens and prevents raw edges from fraying."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','A stitch used to attach a folded hem to the garment almost invisibly on the right side is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "top stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "slip (hemming) stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chain stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "saddle stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The slip or hemming stitch secures a hem while remaining nearly invisible on the right side."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','To gather fabric so it can be eased into a smaller edge, you use a','[{"id": "a", "text": "back stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "long running/gathering stitch that is then drawn up"}, {"id": "c", "text": "buttonhole stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "blanket stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Long running stitches are drawn up along the thread to gather the fabric."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','The plain (open) seam is finished by','[{"id": "a", "text": "leaving the raw edges as they are"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pressing the allowances open and neatening the raw edges"}, {"id": "c", "text": "folding the whole seam to one side and gathering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cutting off the seam allowance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A plain seam is pressed open and its raw edges neatened to prevent fraying."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A French seam is most suitable for','[{"id": "a", "text": "heavy denim jeans"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sheer or lightweight fabrics"}, {"id": "c", "text": "thick woollen coats"}, {"id": "d", "text": "leather bags"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The French seam encloses raw edges neatly, making it ideal for sheer, light fabrics."}',0.65,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Which seam is commonly used on jeans and work-wear because it is strong and encloses the edges?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plain seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Run and fell (flat fell) seam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "French seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overlaid seam"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The flat fell (run and fell) seam is strong and self-neatening, ideal for jeans and work-wear."}',0.65,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A facing is used at a neckline or armhole mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "decorate the outside of the garment"}, {"id": "b", "text": "neaten and finish the raw edge on the inside"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add extra length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make the garment heavier"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A facing is stitched to and turned inside the edge to neaten and finish it."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Interfacing is applied to collars and cuffs to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make them softer and floppy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "give them firmness and shape"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change their colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce their size"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Interfacing adds firmness and body so collars and cuffs keep their shape."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Which of the following is an element of design?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Balance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Proportion"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Colour is an element of design, while balance, rhythm and proportion are principles."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Vertical lines used in a garment design tend to make the wearer appear','[{"id": "a", "text": "shorter and wider"}, {"id": "b", "text": "taller and slimmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rounder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "unchanged"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Vertical lines lead the eye up and down, creating an impression of height and slimness."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','In colour theory, red, yellow and blue are known as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "secondary colours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "primary colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tertiary colours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "neutral colours"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Red, yellow and blue are the primary colours from which others are mixed."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','The final pressing of a completed garment is important because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "adds seam allowance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gives a neat, professional finished appearance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increases the size"}, {"id": "d", "text": "removes the interfacing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Final pressing smooths seams and gives the garment a neat professional look."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','A trimming such as lace or piping is added to a garment mainly for','[{"id": "a", "text": "strength of the seams"}, {"id": "b", "text": "decoration and attractiveness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "taking measurements"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reducing fabric cost"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Trimmings like lace and piping are decorative additions that enhance appearance."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','When costing a sewn garment, the tailor must add together the cost of materials, labour and','[{"id": "a", "text": "the customer''s salary"}, {"id": "b", "text": "overheads plus a profit margin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the price of the shop next door"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the fabric shop''s rent only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A selling price covers materials, labour, overheads and a reasonable profit margin."}',0.6,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','Keeping accurate records of income and expenses in a fashion business helps the owner to','[{"id": "a", "text": "avoid paying any tax at all"}, {"id": "b", "text": "know whether the business is making profit or loss"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase fabric fraying"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure customers faster"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good records show income against expenses, revealing profit or loss."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','A key quality that helps a fashion entrepreneur attract and keep customers is','[{"id": "a", "text": "delivering poor finishing quickly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "good customer service and timely delivery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ignoring customer complaints"}, {"id": "d", "text": "raising prices without value"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good service and reliable, timely delivery build customer loyalty and referrals."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','If materials cost N3,000, labour N1,500 and the tailor wants a N1,000 profit, the minimum selling price should be at least','[{"id": "a", "text": "N4,500"}, {"id": "b", "text": "N5,500"}, {"id": "c", "text": "N3,000"}, {"id": "d", "text": "N1,000"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Adding N3,000 + N1,500 + N1,000 gives a minimum selling price of N5,500."}',0.55,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','One major benefit of self-employment in garment making is that the fashion designer can','[{"id": "a", "text": "avoid learning new skills"}, {"id": "b", "text": "create jobs and earn income independently"}, {"id": "c", "text": "depend fully on government salary"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stop keeping records"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Self-employment lets the designer earn independent income and create jobs for others."}',0.5,'{SSS2,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Horticulture is best defined as the science and art of cultivating which category of plants?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cereal grains grown on large mechanized farms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Garden crops such as fruits, vegetables and ornamentals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Forest timber trees for construction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wild grasses used only for grazing cattle"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Horticulture deals with intensively cultivated garden crops: fruits, vegetables, flowers and ornamental plants."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','The branch of horticulture that deals with the production of fruits is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Floriculture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Arboriculture"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Pomology is the branch of horticulture concerned with fruit and fruit tree cultivation."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','A Nigerian farmer specialising in growing tomatoes, okra and peppers for the market is practising which branch of horticulture?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Floriculture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Landscaping"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Olericulture is the branch dealing with the production of vegetables such as tomatoes and peppers."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Floriculture is the branch of horticulture that focuses mainly on the cultivation of?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Root and tuber crops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Flowering and ornamental plants"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fruit-bearing trees"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Medicinal herbs for drugs"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Floriculture deals with the growing of flowers and ornamental plants for beauty and trade."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Which branch of horticulture is directly concerned with designing and beautifying gardens, parks and surroundings?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pomology"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Olericulture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Landscape horticulture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Vegeculture"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Landscape horticulture deals with the design, establishment and maintenance of gardens and outdoor spaces."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Which of the following is a direct economic benefit of horticulture to a Nigerian community?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It reduces the need for any labour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It provides employment and income through sale of produce"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It eliminates the use of all farm tools"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It prevents rainfall in the region"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Horticulture creates jobs and generates income from selling fruits, vegetables and ornamentals."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Horticultural crops such as citrus, mango and vegetables contribute to human health mainly by supplying?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Carbohydrates only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vitamins and minerals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Crude oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Building cement"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fruits and vegetables are rich sources of vitamins and mineral nutrients for a balanced diet."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','The planting of ornamental trees and flowers around public buildings in Nigeria primarily serves to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beautify the environment and improve aesthetics"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the price of fuel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Replace the need for electricity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stop vehicles from moving"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Ornamental horticulture enhances the beauty and aesthetic value of the environment."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Which horticultural activity earns Nigeria foreign exchange when its produce is exported?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Growing weeds for compost only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Export of fresh fruits and vegetables"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Burning refuse in gardens"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaving farmland fallow permanently"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Exporting horticultural produce such as fruits and vegetables earns foreign exchange for the country."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Apart from food and income, horticultural plants also benefit the environment by?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Absorbing carbon dioxide and reducing soil erosion"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increasing air pollution"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Blocking all sunlight from the soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Destroying wildlife habitats"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Plants absorb carbon dioxide, release oxygen and their roots help control soil erosion."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Which tool is most appropriate for digging planting holes and turning the soil in a nursery bed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Secateurs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spade"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A spade is used for digging, lifting soil and preparing planting holes."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Secateurs are hand tools used chiefly for?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering seedlings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pruning and cutting small branches or stems"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Levelling seed beds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Measuring plant spacing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Secateurs (hand pruners) are used to prune and cut small woody stems and branches cleanly."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','A gardener wants to gather dry leaves and level a fine seedbed. The best tool is a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hand trowel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rake is used to collect debris, break clods and level the surface of a seedbed."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','The hand trowel is most useful in the nursery for?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Transplanting seedlings and digging small holes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cutting large tree trunks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spraying insecticides"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Carrying large loads of manure"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hand trowel is a small tool for lifting and transplanting seedlings and digging small holes."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Which tool would a landscaper use to trim and shape an ornamental hedge to an even level?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering can"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hedge shears"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Garden fork"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hedge shears are designed for clipping and shaping hedges to a neat, even form."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','The main reason for wearing hand gloves while pruning thorny ornamental plants is to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make the work slower"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Protect the hands from cuts and injury"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Improve the taste of the fruit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the plant''s growth rate"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Gloves protect the hands from thorns, cuts and blisters during garden work."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','After using a cutlass and spade, the correct way to maintain them is to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Leave them wet and buried in the soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clean, dry and store them properly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Throw them into a water drum"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Burn the handles in fire"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tools should be cleaned, dried and stored properly to prevent rusting and prolong their life."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Which safety practice should be observed when applying chemical pesticides in the garden?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Spray against the direction of the wind"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wear protective clothing, nose mask and gloves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Eat and drink while spraying"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Use bare hands to mix the chemical"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Protective clothing, nose mask and gloves prevent poisoning and skin contact with pesticides."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','To reduce rusting of metal garden tools during storage, a gardener should?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Oil the metal parts before storing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Soak them in salty water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leave them exposed to rain"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wrap them in wet cloth"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Applying oil to metal parts forms a protective film that prevents moisture and rusting."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Sharp cutting tools such as cutlasses and knives should be carried by?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pointing the sharp edge towards other people"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Holding the blade with bare hands"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Keeping the sharp edge down and away from the body"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Swinging them carelessly while walking"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Carrying sharp tools with the edge down and away from the body prevents accidental injury."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Sexual propagation of horticultural crops is achieved through the use of?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Seeds produced from fertilization"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stem cuttings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Layering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sexual propagation uses seeds formed after fertilization of flowers."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Which of the following is an example of asexual (vegetative) propagation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sowing tomato seeds"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Planting cassava stem cuttings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Broadcasting maize grains"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Raising pepper from seeds"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Planting stem cuttings, as in cassava, is a form of asexual or vegetative propagation."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','A major advantage of vegetative propagation over seed propagation is that the offspring?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Are always genetically different from the parent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Retain the exact characteristics of the parent plant"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Take much longer to mature"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cannot bear fruit at all"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Vegetatively propagated plants are genetically identical to the parent, retaining its desirable traits."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','The method of propagation in which a stem is bent and partly buried to develop roots before separation is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Layering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sowing"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In layering, a stem is bent to the ground and covered so it forms roots before being detached."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Joining a scion of a desired variety onto the rootstock of another plant is known as?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pricking out"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Thinning"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Grafting unites a scion of the desired variety with a rootstock so they grow as one plant."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','The main reason for raising many horticultural crops in a nursery before transplanting is to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Give seedlings special care until they are strong enough"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the seeds germinate more slowly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Prevent the plants from ever being moved"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase weed growth on the field"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A nursery allows young seedlings to receive close care and protection until strong enough to transplant."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Providing shade over a nursery bed in the dry season is important because it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Reduces excessive heat and water loss from seedlings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stops the seedlings from photosynthesising forever"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Encourages pests to attack the seedlings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Prevents the seeds from being watered"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Shade protects tender seedlings from intense heat and reduces excessive transpiration and drying out."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','The nursery practice of removing excess or weak seedlings to give the remaining ones more space is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pricking out"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thinning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hardening off"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mulching"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Thinning removes surplus or weak seedlings so the remaining ones have adequate space and nutrients."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Gradually exposing nursery seedlings to full sunlight and less watering before transplanting is known as?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hardening off"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Layering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pruning"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hardening off toughens seedlings by gradual exposure to field conditions, reducing transplanting shock."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','To reduce transplanting shock, seedlings are best transplanted?','[{"id": "a", "text": "At noon under the hot sun"}, {"id": "b", "text": "In the cool of evening or on a cloudy day"}, {"id": "c", "text": "With all their roots washed clean and bare"}, {"id": "d", "text": "After the soil has been left completely dry"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Transplanting in the cool evening or on cloudy days reduces moisture stress and transplanting shock."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','The main purpose of adding organic manure to a vegetable garden soil is to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Improve soil fertility and structure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the soil completely waterproof"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Kill all the earthworms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase soil temperature to boiling point"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Organic manure supplies nutrients and improves soil structure, aeration and water retention."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','Which soil type is generally most suitable for growing most vegetables because it is well-drained and fertile?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pure sandy soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loamy soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Heavy clay soil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Gravelly soil"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Loamy soil holds moisture and nutrients well while draining freely, making it ideal for vegetables."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','Mulching the surface of a horticultural bed with dry grass helps mainly to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Conserve soil moisture and suppress weeds"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase evaporation from the soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Attract more pests to the crop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Make the soil more acidic instantly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mulch conserves soil moisture, controls weeds and moderates soil temperature."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','A soil found to be too acidic for good vegetable growth can be corrected by applying?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Common salt"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Agricultural lime"}, {"id": "c", "text": "More acid"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Kerosene"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Liming raises soil pH, reducing acidity to a level suitable for crop growth."}',0.65,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','The main nutrient element that promotes healthy green leafy growth in vegetables is?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nitrogen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Chlorine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sodium"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Aluminium"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Nitrogen promotes vigorous vegetative growth and the green colour of leaves."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','The best time to water horticultural crops to reduce water loss by evaporation is?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Early morning or late evening"}, {"id": "b", "text": "At midday when the sun is hottest"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Only during heavy rainfall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "At exactly 12 noon daily"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Watering in the cool of morning or evening reduces evaporation loss and stress on plants."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Which irrigation method delivers water slowly and directly to the base of each plant, conserving water?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Drip irrigation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Flood irrigation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Broadcasting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overhead flooding of the whole field"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Drip irrigation applies water slowly at the plant base, minimising wastage and conserving water."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Removing unwanted plants that compete with vegetables for nutrients, water and light is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Weeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Staking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Grafting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weeding removes competing weeds so crops obtain more nutrients, water and sunlight."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Providing stakes for climbing crops such as tomatoes and yam is done in order to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Support the plant and keep fruit off the ground"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prevent the plant from ever flowering"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop the roots from absorbing water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase pest attack on the crop"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Staking supports weak or climbing stems and keeps fruits off the soil, reducing rot."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Over-watering horticultural crops in a poorly drained soil is harmful mainly because it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Deprives roots of oxygen and causes root rot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Makes the plant grow too fast and healthy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increases the sweetness of every fruit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Has no effect at all on the plant"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Waterlogging fills soil pores, starving roots of oxygen and encouraging root rot diseases."}',0.65,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Landscaping can best be described as the art of?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Beautifying and improving an area of land using plants and features"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Growing cereals for export only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Constructing tarred highways"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Refining crude oil into petrol"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Landscaping is the art of beautifying and improving land using plants and other design features."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','A lawn in landscaping refers to?','[{"id": "a", "text": "An area covered with closely mown grass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A pond stocked with fish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A row of tall timber trees"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A heap of compost manure"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A lawn is an area of ground covered with regularly mown, closely-set grass for beauty."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Which of these is an example of a hard landscape feature?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A flower bed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A paved walkway"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A hedge"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A lawn of grass"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hard landscape features are non-living structures such as paved walkways, walls and paths."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','In landscape design, arranging plants and features so that both sides of a garden appear equal creates?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Balance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Erosion"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Disease"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wilting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Balance is a design principle where visual weight is evenly distributed across the landscape."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','A shrub planted in a row and trimmed to form a living boundary or screen is called a?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hedge"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Lawn"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pond"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hedge is a row of closely planted shrubs trimmed to form a boundary, screen or fence."}',0.5,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','A lawn can be established quickly by laying pieces of already-growing grass and soil called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Turfs (sods)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scions"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tubers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bulbs"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Turfing establishes a lawn rapidly by laying sods of grass with soil onto prepared ground."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','The routine operation of cutting a lawn to keep the grass short and neat is called?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Mowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Layering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mowing is the regular cutting of lawn grass to maintain a short, even and attractive surface."}',0.45,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Trimming an ornamental shrub into a decorative shape such as a ball or cone is a practice known as?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Topiary"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thinning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mulching"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weeding"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Topiary is the art of clipping shrubs or trees into ornamental decorative shapes."}',0.65,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Regular maintenance of a landscape lawn should include mowing, watering and?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fertilizing and edging"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pouring petrol on the grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Covering it with concrete"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leaving weeds to overgrow"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A healthy lawn is maintained by mowing, watering, fertilizing and edging the borders neatly."}',0.55,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Which factor should be considered FIRST before selecting plants for a particular landscape site?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The climate and soil conditions of the site"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The colour of the owner''s car"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The price of petrol that day"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The name of the nearest bank"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Plants must suit the site''s climate and soil conditions to survive and thrive in the landscape."}',0.6,'{SSS2,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Cattle, sheep and goats are grouped together as ruminants mainly because they possess a','[{"id": "a", "text": "simple single stomach"}, {"id": "b", "text": "four-chambered stomach"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gizzard for grinding food"}, {"id": "d", "text": "crop for storing food"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ruminants have a four-chambered stomach (rumen, reticulum, omasum, abomasum) for digesting fibrous feed."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which of the following farm animals is classified as a monogastric animal?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sheep"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pig"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Goat"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The pig has a single simple stomach, making it a monogastric (non-ruminant) animal."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','A farmer who keeps birds such as chickens, turkeys and ducks is engaged in','[{"id": "a", "text": "piggery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poultry farming"}, {"id": "c", "text": "apiculture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pisciculture"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rearing of domestic birds for meat and eggs is called poultry farming."}',0.45,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','The main economic product obtained from keeping honeybees in apiculture is','[{"id": "a", "text": "wool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "milk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "honey"}, {"id": "d", "text": "eggs"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Apiculture (bee-keeping) is practised mainly to obtain honey and beeswax."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','In Nigeria, animals such as rabbits and grasscutters kept for meat production are generally referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "micro-livestock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "draught animals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "aquatic animals"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Small animals like rabbits and grasscutters are called micro-livestock (mini-livestock)."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','The White Fulani (Bunaji) is a well-known Nigerian breed of','[{"id": "a", "text": "cattle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sheep"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pig"}, {"id": "d", "text": "goat"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The White Fulani (Bunaji) is a popular indigenous zebu cattle breed reared for milk and beef in Nigeria."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Which of the following is an indigenous Nigerian breed of goat noted for its small size and high prolificacy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Holstein-Friesian"}, {"id": "b", "text": "West African Dwarf"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rhode Island Red"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Large White"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The West African Dwarf goat is a small, hardy, prolific indigenous breed common in southern Nigeria."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','A poultry farmer who wants a breed that is an excellent layer of eggs should choose the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Broiler"}, {"id": "b", "text": "White Leghorn"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Muscovy duck"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Turkey"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The White Leghorn is a light breed specially developed for high egg production."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','The N''Dama breed of cattle is valued in the humid zones of West Africa mainly because it is','[{"id": "a", "text": "the fastest-growing beef breed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tolerant to trypanosomiasis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the highest milk producer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "resistant to all diseases"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The N''Dama is trypanotolerant, allowing it to survive in tsetse-fly infested humid zones."}',0.65,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Which breed of chicken is reared primarily for rapid meat production?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Layer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Broiler"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cockerel only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Local frizzled fowl"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Broilers are meat-type chickens bred to reach market weight quickly."}',0.45,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','The system of poultry management in which birds are confined in cages placed in tiers is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "free-range system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "deep litter system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "battery cage system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fold unit system"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In the battery cage system birds are housed in wire cages arranged in tiers."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','In the deep litter system of poultry keeping, materials such as wood shavings or groundnut husks are spread on the floor to','[{"id": "a", "text": "feed the birds"}, {"id": "b", "text": "absorb moisture from droppings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "provide light"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase egg size"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Litter absorbs moisture from droppings, keeping the floor dry and reducing disease."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','A structure used to hold and restrain cattle during operations such as spraying, dehorning or treatment is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "crush"}, {"id": "b", "text": "silo"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hatchery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brooder"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A crush is a narrow cage-like structure that restrains cattle for safe handling and treatment."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','The building or house in which pigs are reared is commonly called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "sty"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hutch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "coop"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kraal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pig house is called a sty (piggery)."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','A rabbit is best housed in a','[{"id": "a", "text": "kraal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "hutch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sty"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silo"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rabbits are kept in raised wooden or wire cages called hutches."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','An important factor to consider when siting a poultry house is that it should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "close to a noisy market"}, {"id": "b", "text": "well-ventilated and away from residential areas"}, {"id": "c", "text": "in a water-logged valley"}, {"id": "d", "text": "without any access road"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A poultry house should be well-ventilated, well-drained and sited away from dwellings to control odour and disease."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The equipment used to supply warmth to newly hatched chicks is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "incubator"}, {"id": "b", "text": "brooder"}, {"id": "c", "text": "debeaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "candler"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A brooder provides supplementary heat to keep young chicks warm."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','A shallow disinfectant-filled trough placed at the entrance of a poultry house to disinfect the feet of visitors is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "feeder"}, {"id": "b", "text": "drinker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "foot bath"}, {"id": "d", "text": "waterer"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A foot bath (foot dip) disinfects footwear to prevent disease being carried into the pen."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The practice of raising the floor of a poultry or rabbit house above the ground on a wire mesh is mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make cleaning easier and reduce parasite build-up"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase egg production directly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "provide extra feed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "attract wild birds"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Raised wire floors allow droppings to fall through, easing cleaning and reducing parasites."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','Regular cleaning and disinfection of animal houses is important because it helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the market price of feed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "break the life cycle of disease-causing organisms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "change the breed of the animals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the need for water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sanitation reduces the population of pathogens and parasites, preventing disease outbreaks."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Maize and guinea corn are added to livestock rations mainly as a source of','[{"id": "a", "text": "protein"}, {"id": "b", "text": "energy (carbohydrate)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "minerals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vitamins"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cereal grains like maize and guinea corn are rich in carbohydrate and serve as energy feeds."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Which of the following feedstuffs is the best plant source of protein in poultry feed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cassava peel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Soya bean meal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wheat offal"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Soya bean meal is a high-quality plant protein concentrate used in poultry rations."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Bone meal and oyster shell are commonly added to poultry feed to supply','[{"id": "a", "text": "energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "calcium and phosphorus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fibre"}, {"id": "d", "text": "fat"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bone meal and oyster shell are mineral sources rich in calcium and phosphorus for bones and eggshells."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','A feed ingredient added in small quantities to supply a specific nutrient such as vitamins or minerals is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "roughage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "concentrate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "feed additive/supplement"}, {"id": "d", "text": "silage"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A supplement (additive) is a small-quantity ingredient that supplies a particular nutrient like vitamins or minerals."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','Fresh grasses and legumes fed to ruminants are classified as','[{"id": "a", "text": "concentrates"}, {"id": "b", "text": "roughages"}, {"id": "c", "text": "mineral licks"}, {"id": "d", "text": "additives"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bulky, high-fibre feeds such as grasses and legumes are roughages."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','A ration that supplies all the nutrients an animal needs in the correct proportion is described as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "maintenance ration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "balanced ration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "starter ration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "single feed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A balanced ration contains all required nutrients in the right proportion for the animal''s needs."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','The amount of feed required by an animal just to keep its body functioning without gaining or losing weight is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "production ration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "maintenance ration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "finishing ration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "balanced ration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The maintenance ration meets only the animal''s basic body needs, with no growth or production."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','The method commonly used to formulate a simple ration from two feedstuffs to obtain a required crude protein level is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pearson square method"}, {"id": "b", "text": "candling method"}, {"id": "c", "text": "culling method"}, {"id": "d", "text": "flushing method"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Pearson square is a simple tool for mixing two feeds to reach a desired protein percentage."}',0.65,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','Giving extra feed to breeding females shortly before mating to improve ovulation and conception is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "creep feeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "steaming up"}, {"id": "d", "text": "culling"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Flushing is improved feeding of females before service to raise the number of eggs shed and conception rate."}',0.7,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','Providing young suckling animals with special feed in an area their mothers cannot reach is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "creep feeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dry feeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "force feeding"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Creep feeding supplies extra feed to the young through a small opening that excludes adults."}',0.65,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Newcastle disease, a highly contagious disease of poultry, is caused by a','[{"id": "a", "text": "bacterium"}, {"id": "b", "text": "virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fungus"}, {"id": "d", "text": "protozoan"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Newcastle disease is a viral disease of poultry controlled mainly by vaccination."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Coccidiosis, a disease that causes bloody droppings in chickens, is caused by a','[{"id": "a", "text": "virus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protozoan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tapeworm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mite"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Coccidiosis is caused by protozoa of the genus Eimeria affecting the intestine of birds."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Which of the following diseases of cattle is transmitted by the tsetse fly?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Foot-and-mouth disease"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Trypanosomiasis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Anthrax"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rinderpest"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Trypanosomiasis (nagana) is a protozoan disease of cattle spread by the tsetse fly."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','A parasite that lives inside the body of a farm animal, such as a tapeworm in the intestine, is called an','[{"id": "a", "text": "ectoparasite"}, {"id": "b", "text": "endoparasite"}, {"id": "c", "text": "predator"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vector"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Internal parasites such as tapeworms and roundworms are endoparasites."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Ticks and lice found on the skin of cattle are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "endoparasites"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ectoparasites"}, {"id": "c", "text": "protozoa"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bacteria"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ticks and lice live on the outside of the body and are external parasites (ectoparasites)."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','The most effective way of protecting poultry against Newcastle disease is by','[{"id": "a", "text": "deworming"}, {"id": "b", "text": "vaccination"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dipping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "debeaking"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Since Newcastle is viral, regular vaccination is the main preventive measure."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Passing cattle through a tank containing acaricide solution to control ticks is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "drenching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dipping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "castration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dipping immerses animals in acaricide to kill ticks and other ectoparasites."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','The isolation of newly bought or sick animals from the herd for a period of observation is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "vaccination"}, {"id": "b", "text": "quarantine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "weaning"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Quarantine keeps new or sick animals separate to prevent introducing disease to the herd."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Giving liquid medicine to an animal by pouring it directly into the mouth using a bottle or drenching gun is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "drenching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dipping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spraying"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vaccination"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Drenching is the oral administration of liquid medicine, often to control internal parasites."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Which of the following is a good sanitary practice for preventing disease on a livestock farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Overcrowding animals in the pen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prompt removal and proper disposal of dead animals and waste"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Allowing sick and healthy animals to mix freely"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Feeding animals with mouldy feed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Removing and properly disposing of carcasses and waste prevents the spread of disease organisms."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The period during which a female farm animal is on heat and ready to accept the male for mating is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "gestation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "oestrus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lactation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "parturition"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oestrus (heat) is the period when the female is sexually receptive and can conceive."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The length of time between fertilisation and the birth of the young in a mammal is known as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "incubation period"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gestation period"}, {"id": "c", "text": "brooding period"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lactation period"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The gestation period is the duration of pregnancy from conception to birth."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The introduction of semen into the reproductive tract of a female animal by mechanical means instead of natural mating is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "cross breeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "artificial insemination"}, {"id": "c", "text": "inbreeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "flushing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Artificial insemination (AI) places semen into the female''s tract mechanically, without the male."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The act of giving birth in cattle is technically referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "farrowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lambing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "calving"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kidding"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Parturition in cattle is called calving; farrowing (pigs), lambing (sheep), kidding (goats)."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The mating of animals that are closely related, such as a sire to its own daughter, is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "outbreeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "inbreeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cross breeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "upgrading"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Inbreeding is the mating of closely related animals within the same breed line."}',0.6,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','The removal of the testes of a male animal to make it more docile and improve meat quality is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "castration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "debeaking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "docking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Castration removes the testes, reducing aggression and improving the quality of meat."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','Trimming the upper beak of chickens to prevent cannibalism and egg eating is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "debeaking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "drenching"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Debeaking removes part of the beak to stop feather pecking, cannibalism and egg eating."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','The removal of unproductive or inferior animals from a herd or flock is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dipping"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Culling removes poor-performing, sick or old animals to keep only productive stock."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','The gradual separation of young animals from their mother so that they stop suckling milk is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "b", "text": "castration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brooding"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Weaning is stopping the young from feeding on the mother''s milk so they eat solid feed."}',0.5,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','Placing an identification mark such as a number on the ear of cattle for record keeping is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "ear tagging"}, {"id": "b", "text": "docking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "flushing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Ear tagging attaches a numbered tag to the ear so individual animals can be identified and recorded."}',0.55,'{SSS2,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The photovoltaic effect refers to the direct conversion of sunlight into which form of energy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Thermal energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Electrical energy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chemical energy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mechanical energy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The photovoltaic effect converts light directly into electricity in a solar cell."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The most common semiconductor material used to manufacture solar cells is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Copper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Silicon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Aluminium"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Carbon"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Silicon is the dominant semiconductor material used in most PV cells."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','In a silicon solar cell, the region formed between the n-type and p-type layers is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Busbar"}, {"id": "b", "text": "P-N junction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Anti-reflective coating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Encapsulant"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The P-N junction creates the internal electric field that separates charge carriers."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','Adding phosphorus to pure silicon to create free electrons produces which type of semiconductor?','[{"id": "a", "text": "P-type"}, {"id": "b", "text": "N-type"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Intrinsic"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Insulating"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Phosphorus donates extra electrons, producing an n-type semiconductor."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The thin coating applied to the top surface of a solar cell to reduce loss of incoming sunlight is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Anti-reflective coating"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Back sheet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Junction box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bypass diode"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The anti-reflective coating minimises reflection so more light is absorbed."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','A solar module made from a single continuous silicon crystal, giving uniform dark colour and higher efficiency, is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Polycrystalline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monocrystalline"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Amorphous thin-film"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cadmium telluride"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Monocrystalline cells are cut from a single crystal and are the most efficient common type."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Polycrystalline panels can be visually distinguished from monocrystalline panels because they usually appear:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Uniform black"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bluish with a speckled grain pattern"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Transparent"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bright red"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Polycrystalline cells show a bluish, multi-crystal grain appearance."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Individual solar cells are connected in series inside a module mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Reduce the module weight"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the output voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Decrease the total current"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Change AC to DC"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Series connection adds cell voltages to reach a usable module voltage."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','The tough transparent front layer that protects PV cells from rain, dust and impact is made of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tempered glass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Plywood"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rubber"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Copper sheet"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tempered glass front protects the cells while transmitting sunlight."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Bypass diodes are fitted inside a PV module junction box mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Store energy for the night"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Allow current to pass around shaded or faulty cells"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Convert DC to AC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the module voltage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bypass diodes route current around shaded cells to prevent hot spots and power loss."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','The device that converts DC electricity from the panels into AC electricity for household appliances is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charge controller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Inverter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Combiner box"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An inverter changes DC from panels or batteries into AC for appliances."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','In an off-grid solar system, energy is stored for use at night mainly in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Inverter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Battery bank"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Array frame"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Junction box"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Batteries store the energy generated during the day for use when there is no sun."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','The component that regulates charging current and prevents batteries from over-charging is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charge controller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Busbar"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Surge arrester"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Earth rod"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The charge controller manages charging and protects batteries from overcharge and deep discharge."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','A charge controller type that harvests more energy by operating panels at their optimum point is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "PWM controller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "MPPT controller"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Shunt controller"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Relay controller"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "MPPT controllers track the maximum power point, harvesting more energy than PWM types."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','In a system feeding both the utility grid and local loads without batteries, the correct inverter type is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Grid-tie (on-grid) inverter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Standalone battery charger"}, {"id": "c", "text": "DC-DC converter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rectifier"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A grid-tie inverter synchronises with the grid and needs no battery to supply loads."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','The correct tool for making a proper watertight connection between solar cables is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "MC4 crimping tool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wood chisel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hacksaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paint brush"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An MC4 crimping tool makes secure, weatherproof PV cable connectors."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','A multimeter set to the DC volts range is used during installation to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Measure panel open-circuit voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tighten roof bolts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cut cables to length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bend the mounting rails"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A multimeter on DC volts reads the open-circuit voltage of panels and strings."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','The cable used to connect solar panels outdoors should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "UV-resistant double-insulated DC solar cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ordinary telephone wire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bare uninsulated copper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Flat television coaxial cable"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Solar DC cable is UV-resistant and double-insulated for outdoor rooftop use."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','When selecting cable size for a PV array, the main factor that must be considered to avoid overheating and voltage drop is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Colour of the cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Current-carrying capacity and length"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Brand name printed on it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Weight of the reel"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cable is sized by the current it must carry and the run length to limit voltage drop."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','A clamp meter is preferred over a standard multimeter when the installer needs to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Measure current without breaking the circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Drill holes in the roof"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cut the mounting rail"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Seal the junction box"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A clamp meter reads current by clamping around a conductor, without disconnecting it."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','A 100 W bulb operating for 5 hours consumes an energy of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "0.5 kWh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "20 kWh"}, {"id": "c", "text": "500 kWh"}, {"id": "d", "text": "5 kWh"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Energy = 100 W x 5 h = 500 Wh = 0.5 kWh."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','The unit of electrical energy used to size a solar system''s daily consumption is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Volt"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Watt-hour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ampere"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ohm"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Daily energy demand is expressed in watt-hours (or kilowatt-hours)."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','If a home uses a fan (60 W) for 8 hours and three bulbs (15 W each) for 6 hours, the total daily energy is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "480 Wh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "750 Wh"}, {"id": "c", "text": "270 Wh"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1080 Wh"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fan 60x8=480 Wh; bulbs 45x6=270 Wh; total 480+270=750 Wh."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Peak sun hours for a location are used mainly to estimate the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Daily energy a panel can generate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cable colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Inverter weight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Peak sun hours estimate how much energy an array produces per day."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','In most parts of Nigeria, the average daily peak sun hours used for basic PV sizing is approximately:','[{"id": "a", "text": "1 hour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "5 hours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "12 hours"}, {"id": "d", "text": "24 hours"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Nigeria typically averages about 5 peak sun hours per day for design purposes."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','The capacity of a battery is measured in:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ampere-hours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Volts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ohms"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Battery storage capacity is rated in ampere-hours (Ah)."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','The energy stored in a 12 V, 200 Ah battery is approximately:','[{"id": "a", "text": "24 Wh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "2400 Wh"}, {"id": "c", "text": "240 Wh"}, {"id": "d", "text": "16.7 Wh"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Energy = 12 V x 200 Ah = 2400 Wh."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','To reduce damage and lengthen the life of a lead-acid battery, the recommended depth of discharge is usually kept at about:','[{"id": "a", "text": "50 percent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "95 percent"}, {"id": "c", "text": "100 percent"}, {"id": "d", "text": "5 percent"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Limiting discharge to about 50 percent extends lead-acid battery life."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','Connecting two 12 V batteries in series produces a bank voltage of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "6 V"}, {"id": "b", "text": "24 V"}, {"id": "c", "text": "12 V"}, {"id": "d", "text": "144 V"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Series connection adds voltages: 12 V + 12 V = 24 V."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','An inverter should be selected so that its continuous power rating is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Less than the total connected load"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Equal to or greater than the total connected load"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Exactly half the load"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Unrelated to the load"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The inverter must handle at least the total load, with margin for surge."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','Before working on the DC side of a live PV array, the installer should first:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cover or isolate the panels and open the DC isolator"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pour water on the panels"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the load"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Remove the earth connection"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Isolating the array and opening the DC switch removes the shock hazard before work."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','Personal protective equipment appropriate for rooftop solar installation includes:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Safety harness, helmet and insulated gloves"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Slippers and sunglasses only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "No equipment at all"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A raincoat only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A harness, helmet and insulated gloves protect against falls and electric shock."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','Solar panels on a mounting frame should be tilted and oriented so that in Nigeria they generally face:','[{"id": "a", "text": "North"}, {"id": "b", "text": "South"}, {"id": "c", "text": "West"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Straight up only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Being north of the equator, Nigerian arrays are tilted facing south for best yearly output."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','A small tilt is given to roof-mounted panels mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Allow rainwater and dust to run off and self-clean"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Make the roof heavier"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reduce the panel voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hide the panels from view"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tilting lets rain wash off dust, keeping the panel surface clean."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','When mounting an array, panels should be positioned to avoid shading because even partial shade can:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Increase total output"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sharply reduce the output of the whole string"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change DC to AC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cool the inverter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Shading one cell can drag down the current of the whole series string."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','The metal frames of solar modules and mounting rails are earthed mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Increase panel output"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Protect people from electric shock and lightning surges"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Store energy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Change the tilt angle"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Earthing frames safely conducts fault and surge currents to ground, protecting users."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','A device fitted to protect the system from voltage spikes caused by lightning is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Surge protection device"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Charge controller"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Busbar"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cable tie"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A surge protection device diverts lightning-induced voltage spikes to earth."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','A DC circuit breaker or fuse is installed between the panels and the charge controller to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Provide over-current and short-circuit protection"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the sunlight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tilt the panels"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clean the modules"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The DC breaker/fuse protects wiring from over-current and short-circuit faults."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','When connecting battery terminals, the correct practice is to connect:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Positive to positive and negative to negative for series/parallel as designed, observing polarity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Any terminal to any terminal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Both leads to the positive terminal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Terminals with wet bare hands to test current"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Correct polarity must be observed to avoid short circuits and damage."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','The correct sequence when commissioning a battery-based system is to connect the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery to the controller first, then the panels, then the load"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Panels to the controller first, then the battery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Load before any source"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Inverter directly to the panels"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Most controllers require the battery connected first so the controller senses system voltage."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','The most common routine maintenance task that restores lost output on dusty Nigerian rooftops is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cleaning the panel surface"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Repainting the roof"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Replacing the inverter monthly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Removing the earth wire"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dust reduces output, so regular cleaning of the glass restores performance."}',0.45,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','Solar panels are best cleaned:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Early morning or evening with clean water and a soft cloth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "At midday with a wire brush"}, {"id": "c", "text": "With petrol and steel wool"}, {"id": "d", "text": "By scratching with a metal scraper"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cool times and soft materials avoid thermal shock and scratching of the glass."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','During routine inspection, the electrolyte level of a flooded lead-acid battery that is low should be:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Topped up with distilled water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Topped up with concentrated acid"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Topped up with petrol"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Left empty"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Only distilled water is added, since water is lost during charging, not acid."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','A regular maintenance check on cable connectors and terminals looks mainly for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Loose, corroded or overheated connections"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The brand of the cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The colour of the roof"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The weight of the panel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Loose or corroded terminals cause heating and power loss and must be corrected."}',0.55,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','Keeping a maintenance logbook of readings and actions is important because it:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Helps track performance trends and plan servicing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increases the panel wattage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cools the batteries"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Replaces the need for an inverter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A logbook records trends so faults and servicing needs can be spotted early."}',0.5,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A solar panel giving normal open-circuit voltage but almost no current under sunlight most likely has:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A shaded, dirty or partially damaged cell circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Too much sunlight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "An oversized inverter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A fully charged battery only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Good voltage but poor current points to shading, soiling or a damaged cell/connection."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','If an off-grid system runs in the day but fails at night, the fault is most likely in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery or its connections"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sunlight intensity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Panel tilt angle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Roof colour"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Night operation depends on the battery, so a weak or faulty battery causes night failure."}',0.65,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','An inverter that repeatedly shuts down on overload is most likely experiencing:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A connected load greater than its rated capacity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Too little load"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Excess sunlight on the panels"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A clean battery terminal"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Overload trips occur when the connected load exceeds the inverter''s rating."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A whole series string producing no output when one module is heavily shaded, with no bypass action, indicates a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Faulty or missing bypass diode"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Oversized cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Correctly working system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fully charged battery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A working bypass diode should route current around a shaded module; failure blocks the string."}',0.7,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS2','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','The safest first step before opening an inverter or combiner box to trace a fault is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Isolate DC and AC supplies and confirm zero voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Touch the terminals to feel for current"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spray water inside the box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the load first"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Isolating both sides and confirming dead terminals prevents electric shock during fault tracing."}',0.6,'{SSS2,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which salon tool is used mainly to remove tangles and detangle wet hair without breaking it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tail comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wide-tooth comb"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Barber''s clipper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Curling tong"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A wide-tooth comb glides through wet, tangled hair with minimal breakage."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','In a Nigerian salon, which electrical equipment is used to dry a client''s hair while she sits under it?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hood (standing) dryer"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sterilizer cabinet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Facial steamer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Manicure table"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A hood or standing dryer dries the hair while the client is seated beneath it."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which tool is most appropriate for creating a straight, clean parting before weaving or braiding?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wide-tooth comb"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tail (rat-tail) comb"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Vent brush"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sponge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The pointed tail of a rat-tail comb sections hair into neat, straight partings."}',0.55,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','The equipment used to press and straighten kinky hair using heat is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "hot comb (pressing comb)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "spray bottle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sectioning clip"}, {"id": "d", "text": "neck brush"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A heated hot comb temporarily straightens kinky hair by pressing it."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O1','Which of the following tools is used specifically to cut and shape fingernails during a manicure?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cuticle pusher"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Nail clipper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Emery board only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buffer"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A nail clipper cuts the free edge of the nail to the desired length."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Which product is applied to hair before relaxing to protect the scalp and hairline from chemical burns?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Base cream (protective petroleum cream)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Setting lotion"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hair spray"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Leave-in conditioner"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A petroleum-based base cream shields the scalp and hairline from the relaxer."}',0.6,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','A neutralizing shampoo is used after chemical relaxing mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add permanent colour to the hair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stop the relaxer action and restore normal pH"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the curl pattern"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dry the hair faster"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Neutralizing shampoo halts relaxer action and returns hair to a normal, mildly acidic pH."}',0.65,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','Which material is most suitable for removing nail polish during a manicure?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hydrogen peroxide"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Acetone (nail polish remover)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Methylated spirit only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Toner"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Acetone-based remover dissolves nail lacquer effectively."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','For a client with dry hair, which product is best selected to restore moisture after washing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Astringent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Moisturizing conditioner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Clarifying shampoo"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bleaching cream"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A moisturizing conditioner adds moisture and softness to dry hair."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T1','BTC-T1-O2','A toner used in facial treatment is applied after cleansing mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "remove the top layer of skin permanently"}, {"id": "b", "text": "close the pores and remove residual dirt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add colour to the face"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bleach the skin"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Toner refreshes the skin, removes leftover cleanser and tightens pores."}',0.6,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','Sterilization of metal salon tools such as scissors is best carried out to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make them shine brighter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "destroy micro-organisms and prevent cross-infection"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sharpen the blades"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase their weight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Sterilization kills germs so infection is not passed between clients."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','Which agent is commonly used to disinfect combs and brushes in a Nigerian salon?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Table salt solution"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Methylated spirit / disinfectant solution"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Palm oil"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Kerosene"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Methylated spirit or a proper disinfectant kills germs on combs and brushes."}',0.55,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','The use of ultraviolet (UV) sterilizer cabinets in a salon is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "warm towels for clients"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sanitize and store sterilized tools free of germs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dry wet hair quickly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "style the hair"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A UV cabinet keeps sterilized instruments germ-free until they are used."}',0.6,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','Why should a beautician wash hands before and after attending to each client?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To keep the hands soft"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To prevent transmission of germs and infections"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To save water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To improve the manicure colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hand washing removes germs and prevents cross-infection between clients."}',0.45,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O1','The process of making tools free of dirt but not necessarily killing all germs is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "sanitation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sterilization"}, {"id": "c", "text": "fumigation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vaccination"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Sanitation reduces dirt and germs but does not destroy all micro-organisms like sterilization does."}',0.65,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','To reduce the risk of electric shock in a salon, a beautician should','[{"id": "a", "text": "operate dryers with wet hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep water away from electrical sockets and equipment"}, {"id": "c", "text": "leave cables lying in water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "overload one socket with many appliances"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Keeping water away from electrical points prevents short circuits and shock."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','The immediate first-aid action when a chemical relaxer enters a client''s eye is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "rub the eye vigorously"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rinse the eye with plenty of clean running water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "apply more relaxer to neutralize it"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cover the eye and continue work"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Flushing the eye with clean water dilutes and removes the chemical quickly."}',0.6,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','A patch (skin) test is carried out before hair colouring or relaxing mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "check the client''s blood group"}, {"id": "b", "text": "detect possible allergic reaction to the chemical"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure the length of the hair"}, {"id": "d", "text": "confirm the client''s age"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A patch test reveals whether the client is allergic before full application."}',0.6,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Which of these is the correct first-aid response to a minor cut from scissors during a haircut?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ignore it and keep working"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clean the wound, apply antiseptic and cover with a plaster"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Apply hair relaxer to the cut"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wash it with kerosene"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning, disinfecting and covering the cut prevents infection."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T2','BTC-T2-O2','Wearing hand gloves while applying chemical relaxer protects the beautician mainly from','[{"id": "a", "text": "the client''s perfume"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chemical burns and skin irritation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loud noise"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bright light"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Gloves shield the hands from the caustic relaxer that can burn skin."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','Before shampooing, the hair should first be','[{"id": "a", "text": "coloured"}, {"id": "b", "text": "thoroughly brushed/combed and wetted"}, {"id": "c", "text": "relaxed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "set with rollers"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Detangling and wetting prepares the hair for even, effective shampooing."}',0.5,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','BTC','BTC-T3','BTC-T3-O1','The main purpose of shampooing the hair is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "permanently straighten it"}, {"id": "b", "text": "clean the hair and scalp of dirt and excess oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add permanent colour"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cut split ends"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Shampoo removes dirt, sweat and excess oil from hair and scalp."}',0.45,'{SSS3,BTC,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
