  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','A newly assembled desktop powers on but shows no display, and gives a repeated beep code. The technician should FIRST:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Replace the entire motherboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reseat the RAM and graphics card"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reinstall the operating system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buy a new monitor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Beep codes with no display commonly indicate loose memory or video, so reseating them is the logical first check."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','To connect a modern SATA hard disk for data transfer you use a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wide 40-wire IDE ribbon cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Flat 7-pin SATA data cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "VGA cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "HDMI cable"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "SATA drives use a slim 7-pin data cable, replacing the old wide IDE ribbon."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T2','CGR-T2-O2','After assembling a PC, the setting used to select the boot device order is found in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "BIOS/UEFI setup"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Recycle Bin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Disk defragmenter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Web browser"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The BIOS/UEFI firmware setup lets the technician set which drive the computer boots from first."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','A desktop is completely dead — no fans, no lights — when the power button is pressed. The MOST likely first suspect is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Operating system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Power supply or mains connection"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Web browser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Printer driver"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "No lights or fans points to a power problem, so the PSU and mains supply are checked first."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','A laptop runs very slowly and its base becomes extremely hot. The MOST probable cause is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A dusty, blocked cooling fan/heat sink causing overheating"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Too many desktop icons"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A wrong screen resolution"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A missing mouse pointer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dust clogging the fan and heat sink raises temperature, causing the CPU to throttle and slow down."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','Which utility software is used to detect and remove malicious programs from a computer?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Antivirus software"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spreadsheet software"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Media player"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Web camera"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Antivirus software scans for and removes viruses, worms and other malware."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','A computer displays ''Operating System not found'' at start-up although it previously worked. A likely cause is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "The keyboard is unplugged"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A failing hard disk or corrupted boot record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The monitor brightness is low"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The speakers are muted"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "That message means the boot files cannot be read, usually from a failing disk or damaged boot sector."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O1','The correct action after installing a new printer that Windows does not recognise is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Replace the motherboard"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Install the appropriate device driver"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Format the hard disk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the RAM"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A device driver lets the operating system communicate with and control the new printer."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','Blowing out dust from a system unit with compressed air is an example of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Corrective maintenance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Preventive maintenance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Data recovery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overclocking"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning to stop future overheating faults is preventive maintenance carried out before failure occurs."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','The main reason for regularly backing up important files is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Make the computer boot faster"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Guard against data loss from failure, theft or virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reduce the screen brightness"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increase the processor speed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Backups keep a spare copy so data can be restored if the original is lost or damaged."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','A device that supplies temporary battery power and protects a computer during a sudden mains outage is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "USB hub"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Router"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Scanner"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A UPS gives battery back-up and surge protection, allowing a safe shutdown during power failure."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','In areas of unstable mains, such as many parts of Nigeria, the BEST device to protect equipment from voltage surges and low voltage is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Automatic voltage stabiliser/regulator"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Extension cable only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Torch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ceiling fan"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stabiliser keeps output voltage within a safe range, protecting equipment from surges and brown-outs."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T3','CGR-T3-O2','Defragmenting a mechanical hard disk helps performance by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Deleting the operating system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reorganising scattered file fragments into contiguous blocks"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increasing the physical size of the disk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Adding more RAM"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Defragmentation places file pieces together so the read head accesses them more quickly."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','In a GSM phone, which section controls all the phone''s operations and processing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Power/charging section"}, {"id": "b", "text": "CPU (application/baseband processor)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ringer/speaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Back cover"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The CPU/processor is the control centre that runs the software and coordinates all phone functions."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','The small card that stores the subscriber''s identity and network details in a GSM phone is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "SIM card"}, {"id": "b", "text": "SD memory card"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Graphics card"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Sound card"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The SIM (Subscriber Identity Module) holds the subscriber identity used to access the mobile network."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','Which component in a GSM handset amplifies the transmit signal so the phone can reach the base station?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Power amplifier (PA)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vibrator motor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "LCD backlight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Earpiece"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The power amplifier boosts the RF transmit signal to a level strong enough to reach the network tower."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','Non-volatile memory chips in a phone that store the operating system and user data are the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flash/EMMC memory ICs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The antenna"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The microphone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The SIM tray"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flash/eMMC ICs retain the firmware and user data even when the phone is switched off."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O1','The IC that manages battery charging and distributes regulated voltages to phone sections is commonly called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Power management IC (PMIC/charging IC)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Camera module"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loudspeaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Touch panel"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The power management/charging IC regulates charging current and supplies the correct voltages to each section."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','GSM stands for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "General Système Mobile only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Global System for Mobile communications"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ground Signal Modulation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "General Storage Memory"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "GSM is the Global System for Mobile communications, the standard for digital cellular networks."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','The part of a phone that converts sound (voice) into an electrical signal during a call is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microphone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Earpiece"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Antenna"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Display"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The microphone transduces the user''s voice into an electrical signal for transmission."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','The crystal oscillator (26 MHz clock) in a GSM phone mainly provides:','[{"id": "a", "text": "The reference frequency/timing needed for the phone to work"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Extra battery power"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Waterproofing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The ringtone melody"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The crystal supplies the stable reference clock that the RF and processor sections depend on."}',0.65,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','The unique 15-digit number that identifies a GSM handset itself (not the SIM) is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "PIN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "IMEI"}, {"id": "c", "text": "PUK"}, {"id": "d", "text": "IP address"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The IMEI (International Mobile Equipment Identity) uniquely identifies the physical handset."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T4','CGR-T4-O2','In the phone''s antenna switch/RF section, the duplexer or antenna switch allows the single antenna to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Charge the battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Handle both transmit and receive signals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Store contacts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Display images"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The antenna switch/duplexer lets one antenna share transmit and receive paths without interference."}',0.65,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A phone will not charge and gets warm at the charging port. The FIRST component to inspect is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Earpiece"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Charging port (connector) and its solder joints"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rear camera"}, {"id": "d", "text": "SIM tray"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A worn or lifted charging connector is the most common cause of charging failure and heating at the port."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A GSM phone powers on but shows ''No Service / No Network'' everywhere. A likely hardware cause is a fault in the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Vibrator motor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Network/RF section (PA or antenna switch)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Torch LED"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Back glass"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Total loss of network points to the RF section such as the power amplifier or antenna switch."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A customer''s phone screen shows the image but does not respond to finger touch. The faulty part is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Digitizer (touch panel)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loudspeaker"}, {"id": "d", "text": "SIM card"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Display working but no touch means the digitizer/touch layer has failed, not the LCD."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','When soldering a new charging connector, the tool used to remove old solder from the pads before fitting is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Desoldering wick (solder braid)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sandpaper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A screwdriver"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Solder braid wicks away excess solder, leaving clean pads for the new connector."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O1','A DC power supply (with current display) is useful in phone repair mainly to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Print the phone''s photos"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Power the board and watch current draw to locate short circuits"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Store phone numbers"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Play music"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Watching the current the board draws helps identify shorts and dead sections during diagnosis."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Reinstalling or updating a phone''s operating firmware using a computer and a box/dongle is commonly called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flashing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Charging"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Soldering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Painting"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Flashing writes new firmware to the phone''s memory to fix software faults or update the OS."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','A phone is stuck on the maker''s logo (boot-loop) and will not start fully, though hardware seems fine. The BEST fix is usually to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Replace the screen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Flash (reload) the firmware"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Change the battery only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Repaint the casing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A boot-loop with healthy hardware indicates corrupted firmware, which reflashing repairs."}',0.6,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','Before flashing or hard-resetting a customer''s phone, the responsible technician should FIRST:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Delete the customer''s contacts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Back up the user''s data where possible"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Remove the camera"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Scratch the screen"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Flashing usually erases data, so backing it up first protects the customer''s information."}',0.5,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','The recovery-mode ''factory reset'' on an Android phone will:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Physically repair a broken screen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Erase user data and restore default software settings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the battery capacity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Add more internal storage"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A factory reset wipes user data and returns the software to its original default state."}',0.55,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','CGR','CGR-T5','CGR-T5-O2','To flash most phones, the handset must be connected to the computer using a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "HDMI cable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "USB data cable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Telephone landline"}, {"id": "d", "text": "VGA cable"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A USB data cable links the phone to the flashing software on the computer."}',0.45,'{SSS3,CGR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','In a relational database, a single row within a table is best described as a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Field"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Query"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Form"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A record (tuple) is one complete row holding the data for a single entity in a table."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','A field that uniquely identifies each record in a database table is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Foreign key"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Composite field"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Primary key"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Index field"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A primary key holds a unique value for every record so no two records can be confused."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','Which of the following is an example of Database Management System software?','[{"id": "a", "text": "CorelDRAW"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Access"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Windows Media Player"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Adobe Reader"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Microsoft Access is a DBMS used to create and manage relational databases."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','A collection of related fields describing one item, such as one student''s details, forms a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Table"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Byte"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Database"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Related fields grouped together to describe one entity constitute a record."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O1','The database model that organises data into tables of rows and columns with relationships between them is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hierarchical model"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Network model"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Relational model"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Flat-file model"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The relational model stores data in linked tables of rows and columns."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','In Microsoft Access, the object used to enter, edit and view records in a user-friendly layout is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Report"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Form"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Macro"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Module"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A form provides a convenient screen interface for entering and viewing records."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','A database object designed mainly to produce a formatted printout of records is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Query"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Table"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Report"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Form"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Reports arrange and format data for printing and presentation."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','To retrieve only the records of students who scored above 50, you would use a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Query"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Form"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Macro"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Template"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A query extracts records that meet a specified condition or criteria."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','In SQL, the clause used to specify a condition that filters which records are returned is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "SELECT"}, {"id": "b", "text": "FROM"}, {"id": "c", "text": "WHERE"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ORDER BY"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The WHERE clause restricts results to rows meeting the stated condition."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T1','DPR-T1-O2','Arranging query results alphabetically by surname is achieved in SQL using the clause:','[{"id": "a", "text": "GROUP BY"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ORDER BY"}, {"id": "c", "text": "WHERE"}, {"id": "d", "text": "HAVING"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "ORDER BY sorts the returned records in ascending or descending order."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','The intersection of a row and a column in a spreadsheet is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Range"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cell"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sheet"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Label"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A cell is the single box formed where a row and column meet."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','In a spreadsheet, the reference $A$1 is an example of a(n):','[{"id": "a", "text": "Relative reference"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mixed reference"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Absolute reference"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Circular reference"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The dollar signs lock both column and row, making it an absolute reference."}',0.65,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','Which of the following is a spreadsheet application package?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Excel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft PowerPoint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Publisher"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Microsoft Outlook"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Microsoft Excel is the spreadsheet package in the Microsoft Office suite."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','A group of adjacent cells selected together, such as A1 to A10, is referred to as a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Range"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Column"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Workbook"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Label"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A range is a rectangular block of neighbouring cells treated as one selection."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O1','Text entered into a spreadsheet cell to describe data, and which is not used in calculations, is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Value"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Formula"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Label"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Function"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A label is descriptive text, unlike values and formulas used in computation."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Every formula entered in a spreadsheet cell must begin with the symbol:','[{"id": "a", "text": "#"}, {"id": "b", "text": "="}, {"id": "c", "text": "@"}, {"id": "d", "text": "&"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The equals sign tells the spreadsheet the entry is a formula to be calculated."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','To add the values in cells B2 through B8 in Excel, the correct function is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "=ADD(B2:B8)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "=TOTAL(B2:B8)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "=SUM(B2:B8)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "=PLUS(B2:B8)"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The SUM function adds all values within the specified range."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','Which function returns the arithmetic mean of a set of values in Excel?','[{"id": "a", "text": "MEDIAN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "AVERAGE"}, {"id": "c", "text": "COUNT"}, {"id": "d", "text": "MODE"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "AVERAGE computes the arithmetic mean of the given numbers."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','A trader uses =IF(C2>=50,"PASS","FAIL") in a cell. If C2 contains 48, the cell displays:','[{"id": "a", "text": "PASS"}, {"id": "b", "text": "FAIL"}, {"id": "c", "text": "48"}, {"id": "d", "text": "50"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Since 48 is not greater than or equal to 50, the IF function returns FAIL."}',0.65,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T2','DPR-T2-O2','The function used to count only the cells within a range that contain numbers is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "COUNTA"}, {"id": "b", "text": "SUM"}, {"id": "c", "text": "COUNT"}, {"id": "d", "text": "COUNTBLANK"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "COUNT tallies only cells containing numeric values within the range."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','A network that connects computers within a single building, such as one school''s computer laboratory, is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "WAN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "LAN"}, {"id": "c", "text": "MAN"}, {"id": "d", "text": "PAN"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A Local Area Network (LAN) covers a limited area like one building."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','The network device that connects two or more different networks and routes data between them is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Router"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scanner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Plotter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Monitor"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A router directs data packets between different networks."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','In which network topology are all computers connected to a single central cable called a backbone?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Star"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bus"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mesh"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "In a bus topology every node shares one central backbone cable."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','A network spanning a very large geographical area, such as across states or countries, is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "LAN"}, {"id": "b", "text": "PAN"}, {"id": "c", "text": "WAN"}, {"id": "d", "text": "CAN"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A Wide Area Network (WAN) covers large distances, like the internet."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O1','The topology in which all nodes connect to a central hub or switch is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Star topology"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bus topology"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Ring topology"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tree topology"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "In a star topology every device links to a single central hub or switch."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The unique address that identifies a particular web page on the internet is called the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "ISP"}, {"id": "b", "text": "URL"}, {"id": "c", "text": "HTTP"}, {"id": "d", "text": "HTML"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A URL (Uniform Resource Locator) is the address of a resource on the web."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','Which of the following is a web browser used to access websites?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Google Chrome"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Word"}, {"id": "c", "text": "WinRAR"}, {"id": "d", "text": "VLC Player"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Google Chrome is a web browser for viewing internet pages."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','A company that provides subscribers with access to the internet, such as MTN or Glo, is known as a(n):','[{"id": "a", "text": "URL"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ISP"}, {"id": "c", "text": "DNS"}, {"id": "d", "text": "FTP"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An Internet Service Provider (ISP) supplies internet access to users."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The internet service used mainly to send and receive electronic messages is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "E-mail"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Telnet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Podcasting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Blogging"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "E-mail (electronic mail) is used to exchange messages over the internet."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T3','DPR-T3-O2','The program that searches the internet to help users find information using keywords is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Search engine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spreadsheet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Compiler"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Firewall"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A search engine such as Google locates information using keyword queries."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','A malicious program that attaches itself to files and spreads from one computer to another is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Compiler"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Driver"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cookie"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A computer virus is malicious code that attaches to files and self-replicates."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Software specifically designed to detect and remove viruses from a computer is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Antivirus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spreadsheet"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Utility scanner"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Browser"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Antivirus software scans for, detects and removes malicious programs."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','The fraudulent practice of sending fake e-mails to trick users into revealing passwords or bank details is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Phishing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Formatting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Buffering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Compiling"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Phishing uses deceptive messages to steal confidential information."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Which of the following is a common way a computer virus can enter a system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Using an infected flash drive"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increasing the screen brightness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Renaming a folder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Adjusting the system clock"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Infected removable media like flash drives commonly transfer viruses."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O1','Gaining unauthorised access to another person''s computer system or data is known as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Debugging"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hacking"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Formatting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Encrypting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hacking is unauthorised intrusion into a computer system or its data."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Converting data into a coded form so that only authorised persons can read it is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Encryption"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Formatting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sorting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Merging"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Encryption encodes data so only authorised users with the key can read it."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Keeping an extra copy of important data on a separate storage medium is known as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Backup"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Deleting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Defragmenting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Renaming"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A backup is a spare copy of data used to recover from loss or damage."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','A secret combination of characters that a user must supply to gain access to a computer system is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Username"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Password"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hyperlink"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Filename"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A password authenticates a user and controls access to the system."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','A hardware or software barrier that controls traffic between a computer network and the internet to block intruders is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Firewall"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Scanner"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Modem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Plotter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A firewall filters network traffic to prevent unauthorised access."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T4','DPR-T4-O2','Which of the following is the best practice for creating a strong password?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Using your first name only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Using ''1234'' for easy recall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Mixing letters, numbers and symbols"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Using the word ''password''"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Combining letters, numbers and symbols makes a password harder to guess."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','The correct order of the basic data processing cycle is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Output, Processing, Input"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Input, Processing, Output"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Processing, Input, Output"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Input, Output, Processing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Data is first input, then processed, and finally produced as output."}',0.5,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','Raw, unprocessed facts and figures fed into a computer are referred to as:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Information"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Data"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Report"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Knowledge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Data are raw facts before processing; processed data becomes information."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','In the data hierarchy, the smallest unit, represented by a 0 or 1, is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Byte"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Field"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Record"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A bit is the smallest data unit and holds a single binary value, 0 or 1."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','Arrange the data hierarchy correctly from smallest to largest:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Bit, Byte, Field, Record, File"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Byte, Bit, Record, Field, File"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Field, Record, Byte, Bit, File"}, {"id": "d", "text": "File, Record, Field, Byte, Bit"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The hierarchy rises from bit to byte to field to record to file."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O1','Processed data that is meaningful and useful for decision making is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Data"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Information"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Signal"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Information is the meaningful result obtained after processing data."}',0.45,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','A file organisation method in which records are stored and read one after another in sequence is called:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Random access"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sequential access"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Direct access"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Indexed access"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In sequential organisation records are stored and retrieved one after another."}',0.55,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','The storage medium that only supports sequential access to stored data is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Magnetic tape"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hard disk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Flash drive"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Compact disc"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Magnetic tape must be read in order, allowing only sequential access."}',0.65,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','A file that holds relatively permanent data, such as a customer''s name and account number, is called a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Transaction file"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Temporary file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Master file"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Backup file"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A master file stores permanent, standing data about entities."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','A file containing day-to-day changes used to update a master file is a:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Master file"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Transaction file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reference file"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Program file"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A transaction file records recent activity used to update the master file."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','DPR','DPR-T5','DPR-T5-O2','The method of access that allows a record to be retrieved directly without reading preceding records is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sequential access"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Serial access"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Direct (random) access"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Batch access"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Direct or random access reaches any record immediately without scanning others."}',0.6,'{SSS3,DPR,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','The main reason an electrician switches off and locks the mains before working on a circuit is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "save electricity while working"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent electric shock from live conductors"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reduce the load on the transformer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "improve the power factor of the circuit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isolating and locking off the supply ensures conductors are dead, preventing shock during work."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Which of the following is the correct first action when a person is found still in contact with a live conductor?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pull the victim away with your bare hands"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pour water on the victim to cool the burn"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Switch off the supply at the source"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Give the victim food and drink immediately"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The supply must be switched off first so the rescuer is not electrocuted while helping."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','A fire caused by burning electrical equipment that is still energised should be put out with a','[{"id": "a", "text": "bucket of water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "carbon dioxide (CO2) extinguisher"}, {"id": "c", "text": "foam extinguisher"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wet sand"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "CO2 is non-conductive and safe on live electrical fires, unlike water or foam."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Rubber mats are placed in front of a switchboard mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "keep the floor clean and dust-free"}, {"id": "b", "text": "insulate the operator from earth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "prevent the board from vibrating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce noise from the switches"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Insulating rubber mats break the path to earth, protecting the operator from shock."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O1','Which colour of the modern IEE/NEC wiring code identifies the protective earth conductor?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Brown"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Blue"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Green-and-yellow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Black"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Green-and-yellow striped insulation is reserved for the protective earth conductor."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The hand tool used to remove the insulation from the end of a cable without cutting the conductor is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "combination pliers"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wire stripper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hacksaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bradawl"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A wire stripper is designed to cut and remove insulation while leaving the conductor intact."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','A neon test screwdriver is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "measure the exact voltage of a circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "indicate the presence of voltage on a conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "measure the current flowing in a cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "test the continuity of a fuse"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The neon lamp glows when voltage is present, showing whether a point is live."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','Which tool is most suitable for making a hole in a wooden board to receive a wood screw?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cold chisel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bradawl"}, {"id": "c", "text": "File"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Center punch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A bradawl makes a starting hole in wood for screws, unlike a cold chisel used on metal."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The best practice for keeping the workshop floor safe during installation work is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "leave tools and offcuts where they fall for quick reach"}, {"id": "b", "text": "keep the floor clear of trailing cables and scrap"}, {"id": "c", "text": "polish the floor to a high shine daily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "store flammable liquids near the entrance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A clear floor free of trailing cables and scrap prevents trips and other accidents."}',0.45,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T1','ELE-T1-O2','The correct file to use for smoothing and finishing a metal surface after rough filing is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "bastard file"}, {"id": "b", "text": "rough file"}, {"id": "c", "text": "smooth file"}, {"id": "d", "text": "rasp file"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A smooth file has fine teeth and gives the final finish after coarser files."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','Copper is preferred to aluminium for most domestic wiring because copper has','[{"id": "a", "text": "lower resistivity and better conductivity"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lower cost per metre"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lighter weight for the same length"}, {"id": "d", "text": "higher melting point only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Copper''s low resistivity gives it high conductivity, making it ideal for domestic wiring."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The letters PVC on a cable stand for','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plastic Voltage Conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Polyvinyl Chloride"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Protected Voltage Cable"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Power Volt Cable"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "PVC stands for Polyvinyl Chloride, a common cable insulation material."}',0.45,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','A cable made up of several thin strands of wire twisted together is preferred to a single solid conductor because it is','[{"id": "a", "text": "cheaper to manufacture"}, {"id": "b", "text": "more flexible"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a better insulator"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lighter in weight"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Stranded conductors bend easily, giving greater flexibility than solid conductors."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The cross-sectional area of a cable is measured in','[{"id": "a", "text": "amperes"}, {"id": "b", "text": "square millimetres"}, {"id": "c", "text": "ohms per metre"}, {"id": "d", "text": "volts"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cable size is stated as its conductor cross-sectional area in square millimetres."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O1','The rating of a cable that states the maximum current it can carry continuously without overheating is called its','[{"id": "a", "text": "voltage rating"}, {"id": "b", "text": "current-carrying capacity"}, {"id": "c", "text": "power factor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "insulation resistance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Current-carrying capacity is the safe maximum continuous current for a cable."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A ceiling rose is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "provide a fixing point and connection for a pendant lamp"}, {"id": "b", "text": "control the speed of a ceiling fan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "protect a circuit against overload"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure the energy used by a lamp"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A ceiling rose connects the supply to a pendant lampholder and fixes it to the ceiling."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','The accessory used to join and terminate cables inside a lighting or power point is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "junction (connector) block"}, {"id": "b", "text": "conduit bend"}, {"id": "c", "text": "saddle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "grommet"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A connector block joins and terminates conductors securely at a point."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','The type of cable joint used to connect a branch line to a continuous main run without cutting the main is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "married joint"}, {"id": "b", "text": "britannia joint"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tee (tap) joint"}, {"id": "d", "text": "western union joint"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "A tee or tap joint branches a wire off a continuous main conductor."}',0.65,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','A saddle is used in surface conduit wiring to','[{"id": "a", "text": "join two lengths of conduit together"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fix and support the conduit to the wall"}, {"id": "c", "text": "protect the cable where it enters a box"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bend the conduit around a corner"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Saddles clamp and support conduit against the surface at intervals."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T2','ELE-T2-O2','Before soldering a cable joint, the conductors should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "painted to prevent rust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cleaned and fluxed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wrapped with insulation tape"}, {"id": "d", "text": "coated with grease"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Clean, fluxed conductors allow solder to flow and make a sound electrical joint."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','In a domestic lighting circuit, the switch controlling a lamp must be connected in the','[{"id": "a", "text": "neutral conductor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "earth conductor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "live (phase) conductor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "any conductor of the circuit"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Switching the live conductor makes the lampholder dead when off, which is safe."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','The wiring arrangement used to control one lamp from two different positions, such as at the top and bottom of a staircase, uses','[{"id": "a", "text": "two one-way switches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "two two-way switches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "one intermediate switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "one dimmer switch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Two two-way switches allow a single lamp to be controlled from two positions."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','Concealed conduit wiring is preferred to surface wiring in modern buildings mainly because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "is cheaper and faster to install"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gives better appearance and mechanical protection"}, {"id": "c", "text": "does not require an earth conductor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "allows the use of thinner cables"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Concealed conduit hides cables and protects them mechanically, improving appearance."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','A wiring system in which the cable is enclosed in a flexible or rigid tube run on or in the wall is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "cleat wiring"}, {"id": "b", "text": "conduit wiring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "batten wiring"}, {"id": "d", "text": "casing and capping wiring"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In conduit wiring, conductors are drawn through protective tubing."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O1','The number of lighting points that may be connected to a lighting sub-circuit in a domestic installation is usually limited to a maximum of','[{"id": "a", "text": "2 points"}, {"id": "b", "text": "10 points"}, {"id": "c", "text": "30 points"}, {"id": "d", "text": "50 points"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A lighting sub-circuit is commonly limited to about 10 points to avoid overloading."}',0.65,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','The main purpose of earthing the metal casing of an appliance is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduce the electricity bill"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect the user from shock if a fault makes the casing live"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the current drawn by the appliance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "improve the brightness of the appliance"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Earthing gives fault current a safe path and blows the fuse, protecting the user."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','The instrument used to measure the insulation resistance of a completed installation is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ammeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "megger (insulation tester)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "wattmeter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frequency meter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A megger applies a high test voltage to measure insulation resistance in megohms."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','In a house installation, the consumer unit (distribution board) is fed directly from the','[{"id": "a", "text": "lighting points"}, {"id": "b", "text": "socket outlets"}, {"id": "c", "text": "energy meter through the main switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "earth electrode"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Supply passes from the meter through the main switch to the consumer unit."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','A good earth connection for a domestic installation can be obtained using an','[{"id": "a", "text": "earth electrode (rod) driven into moist soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "wooden peg buried in dry sand"}, {"id": "c", "text": "plastic pipe laid on the surface"}, {"id": "d", "text": "painted steel plate hung on the wall"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A metal earth electrode in moist soil gives a low-resistance path to earth."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T3','ELE-T3-O2','A continuity test on a lighting circuit is carried out to confirm that the circuit','[{"id": "a", "text": "has an unbroken path from end to end"}, {"id": "b", "text": "draws the correct power factor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "operates at the right frequency"}, {"id": "d", "text": "consumes the least energy"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A continuity test checks that the conductor forms a complete, unbroken path."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','The main function of a fuse in an electrical circuit is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the voltage of the circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protect the circuit against excessive current"}, {"id": "c", "text": "improve the power factor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "store electrical energy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A fuse melts and breaks the circuit when current exceeds a safe value."}',0.45,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','An advantage of a miniature circuit breaker (MCB) over a rewirable fuse is that the MCB','[{"id": "a", "text": "is cheaper to buy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "can be reset after tripping without replacing a wire"}, {"id": "c", "text": "does not need a live supply"}, {"id": "d", "text": "carries more current than any fuse"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An MCB simply resets after tripping, whereas a rewirable fuse must be rewired."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','A device that quickly disconnects the supply when it detects a small leakage current to earth is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "residual current device (RCD)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "isolator switch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dimmer switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "changeover switch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An RCD trips on earth-leakage current, giving protection against shock."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','The fuse rating chosen for a circuit should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "much lower than the normal working current"}, {"id": "b", "text": "slightly above the normal working current of the circuit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "equal to the supply voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "as high as possible for safety"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The fuse should carry normal current but blow on overload, so it is set just above working current."}',0.65,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O1','An isolator (isolating switch) is fitted in an installation so that a section can be','[{"id": "a", "text": "made brighter during use"}, {"id": "b", "text": "safely disconnected for maintenance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "supplied at a higher voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "connected to two supplies at once"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An isolator lets a part of the installation be cut off safely for servicing."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','A transformer is a machine that changes the','[{"id": "a", "text": "frequency of an a.c. supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "level of an alternating voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "direction of current flow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a.c. supply into d.c. supply"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A transformer steps an alternating voltage up or down at the same frequency."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','The device used to convert alternating current (a.c.) to direct current (d.c.) is a','[{"id": "a", "text": "rectifier"}, {"id": "b", "text": "transformer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "capacitor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "relay"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rectifier converts a.c. to d.c. using diodes."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','Compared with an incandescent filament lamp, a fluorescent tube of the same light output is','[{"id": "a", "text": "less efficient and uses more power"}, {"id": "b", "text": "more efficient and uses less power"}, {"id": "c", "text": "unable to work on a.c. supply"}, {"id": "d", "text": "always brighter but hotter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Fluorescent lamps give more light per watt, so they are more efficient."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','In a fluorescent lamp fitting, the component that provides the high voltage to start the tube and then limits the current is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "starter and choke (ballast)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "capacitor only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lampholder"}, {"id": "d", "text": "earth wire"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The starter initiates the discharge and the choke limits running current."}',0.65,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T4','ELE-T4-O2','The single-phase motor commonly used in domestic electric fans and small pumps is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "three-phase induction motor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "single-phase induction motor"}, {"id": "c", "text": "d.c. series motor"}, {"id": "d", "text": "synchronous generator"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Small domestic appliances typically use single-phase induction motors."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','According to Ohm''s law, the current through a resistor of 20 ohms connected across a 240 V supply is','[{"id": "a", "text": "4 A"}, {"id": "b", "text": "12 A"}, {"id": "c", "text": "20 A"}, {"id": "d", "text": "4800 A"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "I = V/R = 240/20 = 12 A."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','The power consumed by a 240 V heater drawing 5 A of current is','[{"id": "a", "text": "48 W"}, {"id": "b", "text": "245 W"}, {"id": "c", "text": "1200 W"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1200 kW"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "P = V x I = 240 x 5 = 1200 W."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','Three resistors of 2 ohms, 3 ohms and 5 ohms connected in series have a total resistance of','[{"id": "a", "text": "0.97 ohms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "10 ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "30 ohms"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1.5 ohms"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Series resistances add: 2 + 3 + 5 = 10 ohms."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','The unit of electrical energy for which consumers are billed by the electricity company is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "ampere-hour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kilowatt-hour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "volt-ampere"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ohm-metre"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Energy is billed in kilowatt-hours (units) as measured by the energy meter."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O1','A 1000 W electric iron used for 3 hours consumes electrical energy of','[{"id": "a", "text": "3 kWh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "0.33 kWh"}, {"id": "c", "text": "300 kWh"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1003 kWh"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Energy = 1 kW x 3 h = 3 kWh."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','To measure the current flowing in a circuit, an ammeter must be connected in','[{"id": "a", "text": "parallel with the load"}, {"id": "b", "text": "series with the load"}, {"id": "c", "text": "series with a voltmeter"}, {"id": "d", "text": "parallel with the supply only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An ammeter is connected in series so the full circuit current passes through it."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','A voltmeter is always connected across (in parallel with) the component because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "has a very low resistance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "has a very high resistance and reads potential difference"}, {"id": "c", "text": "must carry the full load current"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measures the frequency of the supply"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A high-resistance voltmeter in parallel reads potential difference without diverting much current."}',0.6,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','The instrument that can measure voltage, current and resistance in one device is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "multimeter (AVO meter)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "energy meter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tachometer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "hydrometer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A multimeter combines voltmeter, ammeter and ohmmeter functions."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','When preparing a bill of quantities for an installation, an electrician estimates the number of','[{"id": "a", "text": "workers living in the town"}, {"id": "b", "text": "materials and accessories needed for the job"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vehicles passing the site"}, {"id": "d", "text": "trees around the building"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A bill of quantities lists the materials and accessories required for the installation."}',0.55,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','ELE','ELE-T5','ELE-T5-O2','An electric energy (kilowatt-hour) meter installed in a consumer''s premises records the','[{"id": "a", "text": "instantaneous voltage of the supply"}, {"id": "b", "text": "total electrical energy consumed over time"}, {"id": "c", "text": "resistance of the wiring"}, {"id": "d", "text": "frequency of the mains"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The kWh meter totals the electrical energy consumed for billing."}',0.5,'{SSS3,ELE,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which tool is best suited for marking a hemline evenly from the floor on a made-up garment?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tracing wheel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Skirt marker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bodkin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stiletto"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A skirt marker measures and marks a level hemline at a set distance from the floor."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','A tailor uses pinking shears mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "cut buttonholes open neatly"}, {"id": "b", "text": "produce a zig-zag edge that reduces fraying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "trim thread ends close to fabric"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cut thick leather and vinyl"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pinking shears leave a serrated edge that limits fraying on woven fabrics."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','Which of these tools is used to turn out corners of collars and to make eyelet holes?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Stiletto"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Thimble"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Seam ripper"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tape measure"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A stiletto (awl) pushes out collar corners and pierces eyelet holes without cutting threads."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','The tool worn on the middle finger to protect it while hand sewing is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "bodkin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "thimble"}, {"id": "c", "text": "emery bag"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pin cushion"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A thimble shields the finger when pushing a needle through firm fabric."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O1','For transferring pattern markings onto fabric using dressmaker''s carbon, a dressmaker uses a','[{"id": "a", "text": "tracing wheel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tailor''s chalk sharpener"}, {"id": "c", "text": "loop turner"}, {"id": "d", "text": "seam gauge"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The tracing wheel presses carbon onto fabric to transfer construction lines."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Before threading or oiling an electric sewing machine, the safest first step is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "raise the presser foot"}, {"id": "b", "text": "switch off and unplug the machine"}, {"id": "c", "text": "remove the bobbin case"}, {"id": "d", "text": "loosen the top tension"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Disconnecting power prevents accidental needle movement and electric shock during maintenance."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Pins and needles dropped on the workroom floor should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "left until the day''s work is finished"}, {"id": "b", "text": "picked up immediately to prevent injury"}, {"id": "c", "text": "swept toward the machine table"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kicked under the cutting table"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Prompt removal of sharp objects prevents foot injuries and accidents."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','A pressing iron that leaves a shiny mark on wool fabric was most likely used','[{"id": "a", "text": "with a damp pressing cloth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "at too high a temperature without a pressing cloth"}, {"id": "c", "text": "on the wrong grain line"}, {"id": "d", "text": "with the steam function off"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Excess heat and direct contact flatten and glaze wool fibres, causing shine."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','To keep sewing scissors sharp and rust-free, they should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "used to cut paper and card as well as fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "reserved for fabric only and wiped dry after use"}, {"id": "c", "text": "soaked in water overnight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stored open on a damp cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cutting only fabric preserves the edge, and wiping prevents rust."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T1','FGM-T1-O2','Which practice best reduces eye strain in a garment-making workroom?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Sewing under dim, coloured light"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Providing adequate natural or bright even lighting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Facing the machine away from windows"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Using dark thread on dark fabric only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good, even lighting reduces strain when working with fine stitches."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which of the following is a natural fibre obtained from an animal source?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Silk"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rayon"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Silk is a protein fibre produced by the silkworm, an animal source."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','A fabric that scorches and forms a hard bead when burned, giving off a plastic smell, is most likely','[{"id": "a", "text": "pure cotton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "linen"}, {"id": "c", "text": "polyester"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wool"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Synthetic polyester melts into a hard bead and smells of burning plastic."}',0.65,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Which fibre is most absorbent and cool, making it suitable for Nigerian tropical wear?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cotton"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Acrylic"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Nylon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Polyester"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cotton is highly absorbent and breathable, keeping the wearer cool in hot climates."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Ankara and other African prints sold in Nigerian markets are most commonly made from','[{"id": "a", "text": "wool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cotton"}, {"id": "c", "text": "silk"}, {"id": "d", "text": "linen"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ankara wax prints are typically woven from cotton, valued for its absorbency and comfort."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O1','Rayon is best classified as','[{"id": "a", "text": "a natural protein fibre"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a regenerated (man-made) cellulose fibre"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a fully synthetic petroleum fibre"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a mineral fibre"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Rayon is made from regenerated cellulose, so it is man-made but not fully synthetic."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','A garment label showing a crossed-out iron symbol means the garment should','[{"id": "a", "text": "be ironed only on the reverse side"}, {"id": "b", "text": "not be ironed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "be ironed at high heat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "be steam-pressed only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A crossed-out iron symbol instructs that the item must not be ironed."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Woollen garments should be washed in cool water and not wrung mainly because heat and agitation cause the fibres to','[{"id": "a", "text": "fade in colour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "felt and shrink"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stretch permanently"}, {"id": "d", "text": "become stiff and glossy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Wool fibres mat together (felting) and shrink under heat and rubbing."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','The best way to remove a fresh blood stain from cotton fabric is to soak it in','[{"id": "a", "text": "hot water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cold salt water"}, {"id": "c", "text": "boiling starch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "warm cooking oil"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cold salt water dissolves fresh blood, while hot water sets the protein stain."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Starching a cotton shirt during laundry is done mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "remove stubborn stains"}, {"id": "b", "text": "give the fabric body and a crisp finish"}, {"id": "c", "text": "prevent colour running"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kill germs on the fabric"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Starch stiffens fabric, giving a smart, crisp appearance after pressing."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T2','FGM-T2-O2','Coloured fabrics that are likely to bleed should first be tested for','[{"id": "a", "text": "shrinkage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "colour fastness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "thread count"}, {"id": "d", "text": "grain direction"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A colour-fastness test shows whether a dye will run during washing."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','When taking the bust measurement, the tape should be passed','[{"id": "a", "text": "around the fullest part of the bust, level all round"}, {"id": "b", "text": "tightly under the arms only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "over the shoulder tips"}, {"id": "d", "text": "around the natural waistline"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bust measurement is taken round the fullest part, kept level for accuracy."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The measurement taken from the nape of the neck to the required hem is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "back width"}, {"id": "b", "text": "full length"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shoulder to waist"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sleeve length"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Full (garment) length runs from the neck nape down to the hem level."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','To allow the finished garment to fit comfortably and permit movement, the dressmaker adds','[{"id": "a", "text": "seam allowance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ease allowance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "hem allowance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dart intake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ease allowance is the extra measurement added for comfort and movement."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','Which of the following is essential for taking accurate body measurements?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Measuring over a heavy coat"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tying a string round the natural waistline as a guide"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stretching the tape as tightly as possible"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Letting the client sit throughout"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A string at the natural waist gives a fixed reference for length measurements."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O1','The hip measurement is normally taken about','[{"id": "a", "text": "at the natural waistline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "20 cm below the waist, round the fullest part of the hip"}, {"id": "c", "text": "at the knee level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "just under the bust"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Hip girth is taken round the fullest part, roughly 18-20 cm below the waist."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','On a paper pattern, the arrow line printed along the piece indicates the','[{"id": "a", "text": "fold line"}, {"id": "b", "text": "straight grain to align with the fabric selvage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "buttonhole position"}, {"id": "d", "text": "seam line"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The grain-line arrow must run parallel to the selvage so the garment hangs correctly."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','A dart is introduced in pattern drafting mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add decoration to the garment"}, {"id": "b", "text": "shape flat fabric to fit body curves"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reinforce the seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark the centre front"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Darts control fullness so flat cloth contours to the bust, waist or hip."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','The basic pattern block without seam allowance or style features is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "toile"}, {"id": "b", "text": "sloper (basic block)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "notch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "facing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The sloper or basic block is the foundation pattern used to develop styles."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','Small triangular marks cut into the seam allowance to match pattern pieces during joining are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "notches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pleats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "gussets"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vents"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Notches are balance marks used to align and match adjoining pattern pieces."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T3','FGM-T3-O2','When laying out patterns to cut a striped or one-way print fabric, the tailor should','[{"id": "a", "text": "place all pieces in any direction to save fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lay all pieces in the same direction to match the print"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cut on the cross grain only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ignore the pattern arrows"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "One-way designs require pieces laid in one direction so the print matches throughout."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Which temporary stitch is used to hold two layers of fabric together before permanent stitching?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Tacking (basting) stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Back stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Blanket stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Overcasting stitch"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Tacking or basting temporarily joins layers and is removed after final stitching."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','The seam most suitable for joining seams on sheer or unlined garments so raw edges are enclosed is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "plain seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "French seam"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lapped seam"}, {"id": "d", "text": "top-stitched seam"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A French seam encloses raw edges within it, giving a neat finish on sheer fabric."}',0.65,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Overcasting is a stitch worked mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "gather fabric fullness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "neaten raw edges and prevent fraying"}, {"id": "c", "text": "attach buttons"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make decorative smocking"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Overcasting works over a raw edge to stop the threads from fraying."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','Which hand stitch gives a strong, unbroken line resembling machine stitching and is used to repair seams by hand?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Running stitch"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Back stitch"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hemming stitch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chain stitch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Back stitch produces a firm continuous line like machine stitching, ideal for strong seams."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O1','A run-and-fell (flat fell) seam is commonly used on','[{"id": "a", "text": "evening gowns"}, {"id": "b", "text": "jeans and men''s shirts for strength"}, {"id": "c", "text": "chiffon scarves"}, {"id": "d", "text": "lace blouses"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The flat fell seam is strong and hard-wearing, so it suits jeans and shirts."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Interfacing is applied to collars, cuffs and facings mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "add colour contrast"}, {"id": "b", "text": "give shape, body and firmness"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reduce the garment weight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "allow the garment to stretch"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Interfacing stiffens and supports areas like collars and cuffs so they hold shape."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Gathering is worked in garment construction to','[{"id": "a", "text": "strengthen a seam"}, {"id": "b", "text": "control fullness by drawing up fabric evenly"}, {"id": "c", "text": "neaten a hem"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mark darts"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Gathering draws fabric along a thread to distribute fullness, as at a waistband or cuff."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','Which finish is most appropriate for the lower edge of a flared skirt to reduce bulk?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A deep 8 cm turned hem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A narrow rolled hem"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A wide facing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A bound buttonhole"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A narrow rolled hem removes bulk that a deep hem would create on a curved, flared edge."}',0.65,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','A placket is constructed in a garment to','[{"id": "a", "text": "decorate the neckline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "provide a neat opening for putting on and removing the garment"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add fullness to sleeves"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reinforce the hem"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A placket finishes an opening (at cuff, neck or skirt) so the garment can be worn easily."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T4','FGM-T4-O2','To set in a sleeve smoothly without puckers at the armhole, the sleeve head is first','[{"id": "a", "text": "clipped at the notches"}, {"id": "b", "text": "eased with a gathering thread to fit the armhole"}, {"id": "c", "text": "interfaced heavily"}, {"id": "d", "text": "top-stitched flat"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Easing the sleeve cap with a gathering thread lets the extra fabric fit the armhole smoothly."}',0.65,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Vertical lines in a garment design are used mainly to make the wearer appear','[{"id": "a", "text": "shorter and wider"}, {"id": "b", "text": "taller and slimmer"}, {"id": "c", "text": "broader across the shoulders"}, {"id": "d", "text": "younger in the face"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Vertical lines lead the eye up and down, giving an impression of height and slimness."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Colour, line, texture and shape are collectively referred to as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "principles of design"}, {"id": "b", "text": "elements of design"}, {"id": "c", "text": "rules of drafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stages of construction"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Line, colour, texture and shape are the basic elements of design."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','Which colour scheme uses different tints and shades of a single colour?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Complementary"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monochromatic"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Triadic"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Analogous"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A monochromatic scheme is built from the tints and shades of one hue."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','In design, the principle that gives a feeling of equal visual weight on both sides of a garment is','[{"id": "a", "text": "rhythm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "balance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "emphasis"}, {"id": "d", "text": "proportion"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Balance distributes visual weight evenly so the design looks stable."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O1','A full-figured client is best advised to choose a dress with','[{"id": "a", "text": "large, bold horizontal prints"}, {"id": "b", "text": "small prints and dark, plain colours"}, {"id": "c", "text": "shiny satin with big frills"}, {"id": "d", "text": "wide horizontal stripes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Small prints and dark plain colours have a slimming, less-widening effect on a full figure."}',0.6,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','When costing a garment for sale, the tailor''s selling price should cover materials, labour and','[{"id": "a", "text": "only the cost of thread"}, {"id": "b", "text": "overheads plus a reasonable profit margin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the client''s transport fare"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the cost of the sewing machine in full"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A sound price covers materials, labour, overheads and a profit margin."}',0.55,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','Keeping a record of orders, measurements and delivery dates in a tailoring business helps mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the price of fabric"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ensure customer satisfaction and timely delivery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid paying tax"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the need for measurements"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good records help meet deadlines and keep clients satisfied, building the business."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','A wise consumer buying ready-made clothing should first check the','[{"id": "a", "text": "colour of the packaging"}, {"id": "b", "text": "fabric quality, fit, finishing and price"}, {"id": "c", "text": "name of the delivery rider"}, {"id": "d", "text": "brand of the sewing machine used"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Quality, fit, finishing and value for money are the key checks when buying clothing."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','Which quality shows good workmanship in a finished garment?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Uneven hems and puckered seams"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Even stitches, well-pressed seams and matched patterns"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Loose threads left hanging"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Buttonholes of different sizes"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Even stitching, neat pressing and matched patterns are signs of good workmanship."}',0.5,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','FGM','FGM-T5','FGM-T5-O2','For a small tailoring enterprise in Nigeria, the most important reason for advertising services is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduce the quality of the work"}, {"id": "b", "text": "attract more customers and increase sales"}, {"id": "c", "text": "avoid keeping business records"}, {"id": "d", "text": "increase the cost of materials"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Advertising makes the business known, attracting customers and boosting sales."}',0.45,'{SSS3,FGM,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Which hand tool is most suitable for trimming the edges of a lawn to give it a neat finish?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutlass"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Edging shears"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hoe"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rake"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Edging shears are designed to cut and neaten grass along lawn borders."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','A secateur is used in the nursery mainly for which operation?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watering seedlings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pruning small stems and branches"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Levelling seed beds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mixing potting soil"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A secateur is a hand pruner used to cut small twigs and branches cleanly."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','Which tool is most appropriate for transplanting seedlings from a nursery bed into polythene pots?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hand trowel"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spade"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wheelbarrow"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Watering can"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The hand trowel lifts seedlings with minimal root disturbance during transplanting."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','The garden fork is best used for which of the following operations?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cutting tall grasses"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Loosening and aerating the soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Applying foliar fertiliser"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Marking out flower beds"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A garden fork breaks up and aerates compacted soil without turning it fully."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O1','A rose can (rose of a watering can) is fitted to a watering can mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the volume of water held"}, {"id": "b", "text": "break water into a fine gentle spray"}, {"id": "c", "text": "prevent the can from rusting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "measure the exact litres applied"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The rose spreads water into a fine spray that does not wash away young seedlings."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Before spraying a garden with insecticide, the operator should FIRST','[{"id": "a", "text": "eat a heavy meal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "put on protective clothing and a nose mask"}, {"id": "c", "text": "spray against the direction of the wind"}, {"id": "d", "text": "remove the gloves for a firm grip"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Protective clothing and a mask prevent inhalation and skin contact with the chemical."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','To keep cutting tools such as secateurs and cutlasses effective, they should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "left in water overnight"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cleaned, sharpened and oiled after use"}, {"id": "c", "text": "stored while still wet with sap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "painted over the cutting edge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Cleaning, sharpening and oiling prevent rust and keep the blades sharp."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Which practice best reduces the risk of accidents when using a lawn mower?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Clearing stones and debris from the lawn before mowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mowing barefoot for better balance"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Refuelling while the engine is running"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Removing the blade guard for speed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Removing stones prevents them from being thrown out and causing injury."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','Horticultural chemicals should be stored in','[{"id": "a", "text": "an open shelf in the kitchen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a locked store away from food and children"}, {"id": "c", "text": "used drinking bottles for easy pouring"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the same box as harvested vegetables"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Locked storage away from food and children prevents accidental poisoning."}',0.45,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T1','HRT-T1-O2','The main reason for washing hands and changing clothes after applying pesticides is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "save water on the farm"}, {"id": "b", "text": "avoid chemical absorption and poisoning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the clothes last longer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "reduce the cost of the chemical"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Washing removes chemical residue that could otherwise be absorbed through the skin."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Propagation of hibiscus using a piece of stem placed in moist soil is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "seed propagation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "stem cutting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "layering"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A cut stem section rooted in soil is propagation by stem cutting."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','In which propagation method is a rooted branch of a plant bent down and covered with soil while still attached to the parent?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Budding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Layering"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Seed sowing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Layering roots a branch while it is still attached to the parent plant."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','The joining of a scion of one plant onto the rootstock of another is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "grafting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cutting"}, {"id": "c", "text": "division"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sowing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Grafting unites a scion with a rootstock so they grow as one plant."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Which of the following is an advantage of propagating fruit trees by grafting rather than by seed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The plant takes much longer to fruit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It preserves the exact qualities of the parent variety"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It always produces a taller tree"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It requires no rootstock"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Grafting is vegetative, so the offspring keeps the parent''s desirable traits."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O1','Ornamental plants such as canna and ginger lily are commonly propagated by','[{"id": "a", "text": "rhizome or division"}, {"id": "b", "text": "budding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "air layering"}, {"id": "d", "text": "seed only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Canna and ginger lily produce rhizomes that are divided to raise new plants."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','The main purpose of providing shade over a nursery bed of young seedlings is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduce excessive heat and water loss"}, {"id": "b", "text": "prevent the seeds from germinating"}, {"id": "c", "text": "attract more insect pests"}, {"id": "d", "text": "make the seedlings grow taller quickly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Shade lowers temperature and transpiration, protecting delicate seedlings."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Pricking out in nursery management refers to','[{"id": "a", "text": "spraying seedlings against pests"}, {"id": "b", "text": "transferring crowded seedlings to give more space"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cutting the roots of seedlings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "removing weeds from the bed"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pricking out spaces out overcrowded seedlings so each develops well."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Hardening off of nursery seedlings is done mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make the seedlings resistant to field conditions before transplanting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase the size of the nursery bed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reduce the number of leaves"}, {"id": "d", "text": "speed up flowering in the nursery"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hardening off gradually exposes seedlings to sun and less water to survive the field."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Which soil medium is most suitable for filling nursery bags for raising seedlings?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pure river sand only"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A mixture of topsoil, sand and well-decomposed manure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fresh sawdust only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clay subsoil only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A balanced mix gives good drainage, aeration and nutrients for seedlings."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T2','HRT-T2-O2','Damping-off disease, common in nurseries, is best controlled by','[{"id": "a", "text": "over-watering the seedlings"}, {"id": "b", "text": "avoiding overcrowding and using sterilised soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "removing all shade from the bed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "adding fresh manure to the medium"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good spacing and sterilised medium reduce the fungi that cause damping-off."}',0.65,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','A flowering plant that completes its life cycle within one growing season is described as','[{"id": "a", "text": "an annual"}, {"id": "b", "text": "a perennial"}, {"id": "c", "text": "a shrub"}, {"id": "d", "text": "a climber"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Annuals germinate, flower and die within a single season."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Which of the following is commonly grown as a hedge plant in Nigerian compounds?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Ixora (flame of the woods)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cassava"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Yam"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Ixora is a popular ornamental shrub used for hedges and borders."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Ornamental plants grown mainly for the beauty of their coloured leaves rather than flowers are called','[{"id": "a", "text": "foliage plants"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cover crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cereals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "legumes"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Foliage plants like croton are valued for their attractive leaves."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','The practice of removing dead flowers from ornamental plants to encourage more blooming is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "deadheading"}, {"id": "b", "text": "mulching"}, {"id": "c", "text": "staking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "ridging"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Deadheading removes spent flowers so the plant produces new blooms."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O1','Bougainvillea is best described as a','[{"id": "a", "text": "climbing ornamental shrub"}, {"id": "b", "text": "root tuber crop"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grass species"}, {"id": "d", "text": "aquatic weed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Bougainvillea is a woody climber grown for its colourful bracts."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','The quickest method of establishing a lawn on a prepared site is by','[{"id": "a", "text": "turfing (laying grass sods)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "broadcasting seeds only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "planting tree seedlings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "spreading dry leaves"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Laying ready-grown sods gives an almost immediate lawn cover."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Regular mowing of a lawn is important because it','[{"id": "a", "text": "encourages dense, even grass growth"}, {"id": "b", "text": "kills the grass roots"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increases weed seeds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "removes the topsoil"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Frequent mowing promotes tillering, giving a thick, even lawn."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Which grass is commonly used for establishing lawns in Nigeria?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Carpet grass (Axonopus compressus)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Elephant grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Guinea corn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Spear grass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Carpet grass forms a low, dense turf ideal for Nigerian lawns."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','Rolling a newly turfed lawn is done to','[{"id": "a", "text": "firm the sods and ensure good contact with the soil"}, {"id": "b", "text": "raise the grass higher"}, {"id": "c", "text": "encourage weed growth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "remove the grass colour"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rolling presses the sods onto the soil so roots establish quickly."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T3','HRT-T3-O2','A common maintenance operation that supplies nutrients to keep a lawn green is','[{"id": "a", "text": "top dressing with fertiliser or manure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pouring petrol on the grass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "covering the lawn with polythene"}, {"id": "d", "text": "uprooting the grass yearly"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Top dressing adds nutrients that keep the lawn vigorous and green."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','In landscaping, the arrangement of plants and features so that both sides of a garden look similar is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "balance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "irrigation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "grafting"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pruning"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Balance in design creates visual equilibrium between parts of the landscape."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','A landscape feature made of stone, concrete or brick, such as a walkway or wall, is referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "hardscape"}, {"id": "b", "text": "softscape"}, {"id": "c", "text": "mulch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "compost"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hardscape refers to the non-living, constructed elements of a landscape."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','The first step in preparing a good landscape plan for a site is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "carry out a site survey and analysis"}, {"id": "b", "text": "buy all the plants immediately"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pour concrete over the whole site"}, {"id": "d", "text": "plant a lawn without measuring"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A site survey and analysis guides an appropriate and functional design."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','Which of the following is a softscape element in landscaping?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Flower beds and shrubs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Concrete pavement"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Brick fence"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stone fountain basin"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Softscape covers the living plant materials used in a landscape."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O1','A focal point in a garden design is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "draw and hold the viewer''s attention"}, {"id": "b", "text": "block all sunlight from the garden"}, {"id": "c", "text": "prevent water drainage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kill unwanted plants"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A focal point such as a fountain or specimen tree directs the eye."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','When constructing a garden path, providing a slight slope (gradient) is important to','[{"id": "a", "text": "allow rainwater to drain off the surface"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the path more slippery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the cost of construction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "prevent people from walking on it"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A gradient lets water run off so the path does not flood or become soggy."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','A rockery (rock garden) in landscaping is mainly established to','[{"id": "a", "text": "display plants among decorative rocks"}, {"id": "b", "text": "store harvested crops"}, {"id": "c", "text": "park vehicles"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dispose of refuse"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A rockery combines rocks and small plants for ornamental effect."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Which feature is commonly constructed to provide shade and support climbing plants in a garden?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pergola"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Compost pit"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Drainage ditch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Seed bed"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A pergola is an overhead structure that shades and supports climbers."}',0.65,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','Before laying paving slabs for a patio, the ground should be','[{"id": "a", "text": "levelled and compacted with a firm base"}, {"id": "b", "text": "left loose and uneven"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flooded with water"}, {"id": "d", "text": "covered with fresh grass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A level, compacted base keeps the slabs firm and prevents sinking."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T4','HRT-T4-O2','An artificial pool of water constructed as an ornamental feature in a landscape is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "water garden or pond"}, {"id": "b", "text": "nursery bed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "compost heap"}, {"id": "d", "text": "greenhouse"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A water garden or pond is an ornamental water feature in landscaping."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','The addition of well-decomposed organic matter to garden soil helps mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "improve soil structure and fertility"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the soil more acidic only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "reduce the soil water-holding capacity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kill all soil organisms"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Organic matter improves structure, fertility and water retention of soil."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Which nutrient element is mainly responsible for the healthy green colour of ornamental foliage?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Nitrogen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Phosphorus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Calcium"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Chlorine"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Nitrogen promotes chlorophyll formation and lush green leaves."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','Mulching around ornamental plants helps to','[{"id": "a", "text": "conserve soil moisture and suppress weeds"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase evaporation from the soil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "attract termites to the roots"}, {"id": "d", "text": "raise the soil temperature sharply"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Mulch reduces water loss and smothers weeds around plants."}',0.5,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','A soil that is too acidic for many horticultural crops can be corrected by adding','[{"id": "a", "text": "lime"}, {"id": "b", "text": "common salt"}, {"id": "c", "text": "kerosene"}, {"id": "d", "text": "sawdust only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Liming raises soil pH, reducing excessive acidity."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O1','The best time to apply foliar fertiliser to garden plants is','[{"id": "a", "text": "early morning or late evening when it is cool"}, {"id": "b", "text": "at midday under hot sun"}, {"id": "c", "text": "during heavy rainfall"}, {"id": "d", "text": "at midnight in total darkness"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Cool periods reduce leaf scorch and allow better nutrient absorption."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Aphids attack ornamental plants mainly by','[{"id": "a", "text": "sucking sap from the leaves and shoots"}, {"id": "b", "text": "boring holes in the stem"}, {"id": "c", "text": "eating the roots underground"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pollinating the flowers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Aphids are sap-sucking insects that weaken shoots and spread viruses."}',0.55,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','The use of natural enemies such as ladybirds to control aphids is an example of','[{"id": "a", "text": "biological control"}, {"id": "b", "text": "chemical control"}, {"id": "c", "text": "mechanical control"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cultural control"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Using living organisms to control pests is biological control."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','Which of the following is a cultural method of weed control in a garden?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Hand hoeing and mulching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Spraying a systemic herbicide"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Releasing predatory insects"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Using a knapsack sprayer"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Hoeing and mulching are cultural practices that suppress weeds."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','A fungal disease that shows as a white powdery coating on the leaves of ornamental plants is','[{"id": "a", "text": "powdery mildew"}, {"id": "b", "text": "leaf curl virus"}, {"id": "c", "text": "root-knot nematode"}, {"id": "d", "text": "bacterial wilt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Powdery mildew is a fungus that coats leaves with a white powder."}',0.65,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','HRT','HRT-T5','HRT-T5-O2','The main reason for practising crop rotation and field sanitation in a horticultural garden is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduce the build-up of pests and diseases"}, {"id": "b", "text": "increase the number of weeds"}, {"id": "c", "text": "make the soil permanently barren"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stop plants from flowering"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Rotation and sanitation break pest and disease cycles in the soil."}',0.6,'{SSS3,HRT,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','A poultry farmer in Ibadan keeps 500 layers in individual wire cages arranged in tiers inside a building. Which housing system is this?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Deep litter system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Battery cage system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Free range system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fold unit system"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Birds kept in tiers of individual wire cages define the battery cage system."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which housing system allows birds to roam freely on the ground and forage for part of their feed?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Battery cage system"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Deep litter system"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Free range system"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Slatted floor system"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "The free range system lets birds roam and forage naturally outdoors."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','In the deep litter system for poultry, which material is most commonly spread on the floor to absorb droppings?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Fine river sand"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Wood shavings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Broken bottles"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Plastic sheeting"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Wood shavings are a common litter material that absorbs moisture from droppings."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','A pig house floor is best made of concrete mainly because concrete floors','[{"id": "a", "text": "keep the pigs permanently cool at night"}, {"id": "b", "text": "are easy to clean and disinfect"}, {"id": "c", "text": "supply extra minerals to the pigs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "prevent the pigs from feeding"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Concrete floors resist rooting and are easily washed and disinfected."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O1','Which housing arrangement is most appropriate for a dairy cow being milked and fed indoors while tied in a stall?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Loose housing barn"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Stanchion (tie) barn"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Battery cage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fold unit"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A stanchion or tie barn restrains each cow in a stall for feeding and milking."}',0.6,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Why is proper ventilation important in a poultry house in Nigeria''s humid climate?','[{"id": "a", "text": "It increases the price of eggs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "It removes ammonia and excess heat and moisture"}, {"id": "c", "text": "It makes the birds lay double-yolk eggs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "It prevents the birds from drinking water"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Good ventilation clears ammonia, heat and moisture, keeping birds healthy."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','In the tropics, a livestock house is best oriented with its long axis running','[{"id": "a", "text": "north to south"}, {"id": "b", "text": "east to west"}, {"id": "c", "text": "along the nearest road"}, {"id": "d", "text": "in any random direction"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "An east-west long axis reduces direct sunlight entering the house, keeping it cool."}',0.65,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','The regular removal of manure and washing of pens in a livestock house is mainly done to','[{"id": "a", "text": "reduce build-up of disease-causing organisms"}, {"id": "b", "text": "make the animals grow horns faster"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the number of flies"}, {"id": "d", "text": "change the colour of the animals"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Regular cleaning lowers the population of pathogens and parasites."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','A footbath containing disinfectant placed at the entrance of a poultry house is used to','[{"id": "a", "text": "wash the eggs before sale"}, {"id": "b", "text": "disinfect footwear and prevent disease entry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cool the feet of the birds"}, {"id": "d", "text": "provide drinking water for visitors"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A disinfectant footbath kills pathogens on footwear, part of biosecurity."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T1','LVF-T1-O2','Overcrowding of birds in a poultry house most directly leads to','[{"id": "a", "text": "faster egg production per bird"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cannibalism, stress and rapid spread of disease"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lower feed consumption and larger eggs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "improved feather colour"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Overcrowding raises stress, encourages pecking, and spreads disease quickly."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Which of the following is the best example of an energy-giving feedstuff for poultry?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Groundnut cake"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Maize"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Bone meal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fish meal"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Maize is rich in carbohydrate and serves mainly as an energy feed."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Soya bean meal and fish meal are added to livestock rations chiefly to supply','[{"id": "a", "text": "protein"}, {"id": "b", "text": "carbohydrate"}, {"id": "c", "text": "roughage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "water"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "These feedstuffs are protein concentrates supplying amino acids for growth."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','A feed ingredient added in small quantities to supply calcium and phosphorus for strong bones and eggshells is','[{"id": "a", "text": "wheat offal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "palm oil"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bone meal"}, {"id": "d", "text": "cassava peel"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Bone meal is a mineral supplement rich in calcium and phosphorus."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Roughages such as guinea grass and elephant grass are especially important in the ration of','[{"id": "a", "text": "day-old chicks"}, {"id": "b", "text": "ruminants like cattle and goats"}, {"id": "c", "text": "laying hens in cages"}, {"id": "d", "text": "weaner rabbits only"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ruminants use their rumen microbes to digest fibrous roughages."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O1','Oyster shell is included in the diet of laying hens mainly to','[{"id": "a", "text": "provide energy for movement"}, {"id": "b", "text": "supply calcium for strong eggshells"}, {"id": "c", "text": "add protein for feather growth"}, {"id": "d", "text": "act as a source of vitamin C"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oyster shell is a calcium source that hardens eggshells."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','A balanced ration is best described as a feed that','[{"id": "a", "text": "contains only maize and water"}, {"id": "b", "text": "supplies all nutrients in the right proportion for the animal"}, {"id": "c", "text": "is the cheapest feed available in the market"}, {"id": "d", "text": "contains only protein sources"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A balanced ration provides all required nutrients in correct proportions."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','The method commonly used to compute the proportions of two feedstuffs to obtain a desired protein level is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "Pearson square method"}, {"id": "b", "text": "randomised block method"}, {"id": "c", "text": "line transect method"}, {"id": "d", "text": "quadrat method"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The Pearson square balances two ingredients to a target crude protein level."}',0.65,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','Which type of ration has the highest crude protein content and is fed to young growing chicks?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Layers'' mash"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Chick starter mash"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Grower''s mash"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Maintenance ration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Chick starter mash carries the highest protein for rapid early growth."}',0.6,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','Feeding a portion of ration just enough to keep an idle animal alive without gain or loss in weight is called a','[{"id": "a", "text": "production ration"}, {"id": "b", "text": "maintenance ration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "starter ration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "finisher ration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A maintenance ration meets only basic needs with no weight change."}',0.6,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T2','LVF-T2-O2','Clean drinking water should always be available to livestock because water','[{"id": "a", "text": "is a source of dietary protein"}, {"id": "b", "text": "aids digestion, transport of nutrients and temperature control"}, {"id": "c", "text": "provides most of the animal''s energy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "replaces the need for minerals"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Water is essential for digestion, nutrient transport and body temperature regulation."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','The period during which a female farm animal is sexually receptive and can be successfully mated is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "gestation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "oestrus (heat)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "lactation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "parturition"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oestrus, or heat, is when the female is receptive and can conceive."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','The act of giving birth in cattle is technically referred to as','[{"id": "a", "text": "farrowing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "lambing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "calving"}, {"id": "d", "text": "kidding"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Parturition in cattle is called calving."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','A common visible sign that a cow is on heat is that it','[{"id": "a", "text": "refuses to move at all for days"}, {"id": "b", "text": "becomes restless and allows other cows to mount it"}, {"id": "c", "text": "suddenly grows longer horns"}, {"id": "d", "text": "stops breathing intermittently"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Standing to be mounted and restlessness are typical heat signs in cows."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','The length of time from conception to birth in an animal is known as the','[{"id": "a", "text": "incubation period"}, {"id": "b", "text": "gestation period"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weaning period"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dry period"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The gestation period is the duration of pregnancy from conception to birth."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O1','In poultry, the process of applying heat to fertile eggs so that chicks develop and hatch is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "brooding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "incubation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "debeaking"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Incubation supplies the warmth needed for embryos to develop and hatch."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','The mating of animals that are closely related, such as a sire to its daughter, is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "outbreeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "cross breeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "inbreeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "upgrading"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Inbreeding is mating of closely related individuals."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','The introduction of semen into the reproductive tract of a female without natural mating is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "artificial insemination"}, {"id": "b", "text": "natural service"}, {"id": "c", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "steaming up"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Artificial insemination places semen mechanically into the female tract."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','One major advantage of artificial insemination over natural mating is that it','[{"id": "a", "text": "removes the need to feed the animals"}, {"id": "b", "text": "allows one superior sire to serve many females"}, {"id": "c", "text": "makes all offspring identical twins"}, {"id": "d", "text": "prevents the females from ever conceiving"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "AI lets semen from one outstanding sire breed many females widely."}',0.6,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','Mating two different breeds to combine their desirable qualities in the offspring is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "inbreeding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "line breeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "cross breeding"}, {"id": "d", "text": "self-fertilisation"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Cross breeding mates different breeds to blend their good traits."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T3','LVF-T3-O2','Removing poor-performing or unproductive animals from a herd or flock to improve overall quality is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "b", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dipping"}, {"id": "d", "text": "drenching"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Culling removes inferior animals so productive ones remain."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Newcastle disease, which causes twisting of the neck and high mortality, mainly affects','[{"id": "a", "text": "cattle"}, {"id": "b", "text": "poultry"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pigs"}, {"id": "d", "text": "goats"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Newcastle disease is a serious viral disease of poultry."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Ticks found attached to the skin of cattle are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "internal parasites"}, {"id": "b", "text": "external parasites"}, {"id": "c", "text": "bacteria"}, {"id": "d", "text": "protozoa"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Ticks live on the body surface, so they are external parasites (ectoparasites)."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Which of the following is a viral disease of cattle characterised by fever, mouth sores and lameness from foot blisters?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Foot and mouth disease"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Coccidiosis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fowl pox"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mastitis"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Foot and mouth disease is a viral cattle disease with mouth and foot lesions."}',0.6,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Coccidiosis in poultry, which causes bloody droppings in chicks, is caused by a','[{"id": "a", "text": "virus"}, {"id": "b", "text": "protozoan"}, {"id": "c", "text": "tapeworm"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mineral deficiency"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Coccidiosis is caused by protozoa of the genus Eimeria."}',0.65,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O1','Roundworms and tapeworms living in the digestive tract of livestock are examples of','[{"id": "a", "text": "ectoparasites"}, {"id": "b", "text": "endoparasites"}, {"id": "c", "text": "vectors"}, {"id": "d", "text": "predators"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Worms living inside the body are internal parasites, or endoparasites."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','The most reliable way to protect a poultry flock against Newcastle disease is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "increase the lighting in the pen"}, {"id": "b", "text": "vaccinate the birds on schedule"}, {"id": "c", "text": "feed them extra maize only"}, {"id": "d", "text": "paint the pen walls white"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Routine vaccination is the main defence against Newcastle disease."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Passing cattle through a bath of acaricide solution to kill ticks and mites is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "drenching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dipping"}, {"id": "c", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "castration"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dipping immerses animals in acaricide to control external parasites."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Giving a liquid dewormer to a goat by mouth using a drenching gun is done mainly to control','[{"id": "a", "text": "ticks on the skin"}, {"id": "b", "text": "internal worms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "viral infections"}, {"id": "d", "text": "mineral deficiency"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Oral drenching with an anthelmintic controls internal worms."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Keeping newly bought animals separate from the main herd for a period before mixing them is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "quarantine"}, {"id": "b", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "flushing"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Quarantine isolates new stock to prevent introducing disease."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T4','LVF-T4-O2','Which of the following practices best helps to prevent the spread of disease on a livestock farm?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Allowing visitors free access to all pens"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prompt isolation and treatment of sick animals"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Leaving dead animals in the pen"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reusing dirty needles between animals"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Isolating and treating sick animals early limits disease spread."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','Cutting or trimming the upper beak of chicks to prevent cannibalism and feed wastage is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "debeaking"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "castration"}, {"id": "d", "text": "docking"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Debeaking trims the beak to reduce pecking and feather picking."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The removal of the testes of a male animal to make it docile and improve meat quality is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "culling"}, {"id": "b", "text": "castration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "branding"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Castration removes the testes, making males calmer and improving carcass quality."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','Gradually changing a young animal''s feed from its mother''s milk to solid feed is known as','[{"id": "a", "text": "flushing"}, {"id": "b", "text": "steaming up"}, {"id": "c", "text": "weaning"}, {"id": "d", "text": "dipping"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Weaning transitions the young from milk to solid feed."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','The provision of extra warmth for day-old chicks using a source such as a charcoal stove or bulb is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "incubation"}, {"id": "b", "text": "brooding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "candling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "vaccination"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Brooding supplies warmth to chicks that cannot yet regulate body heat."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O1','Removing the horn buds of a young calf to prevent injuries in the herd is called','[{"id": "a", "text": "docking"}, {"id": "b", "text": "dehorning"}, {"id": "c", "text": "debeaking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "shearing"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Dehorning removes horn growth to reduce injuries among animals."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','A record that shows the parents and ancestors of an animal, used in breeding decisions, is the','[{"id": "a", "text": "feeding record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "pedigree record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "sales record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "health record"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A pedigree record traces an animal''s ancestry for breeding choices."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','Which record would a farmer check to know the quantity and cost of feed used over a month?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Feeding record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Breeding record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Vaccination record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pedigree record"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The feeding record captures feed quantities and costs."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','The main reason a livestock farmer keeps accurate records is to','[{"id": "a", "text": "make the farm look busy to visitors"}, {"id": "b", "text": "monitor performance and make sound management decisions"}, {"id": "c", "text": "increase the weight of the animals directly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "avoid feeding the animals"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Records reveal performance and guide profitable management decisions."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','A record showing dates of vaccination, disease outbreaks and treatments given is called the','[{"id": "a", "text": "financial record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "health record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "egg production record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "pedigree record"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "The health record documents vaccinations, illnesses and treatments."}',0.5,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','LVF','LVF-T5','LVF-T5-O2','To determine whether a poultry enterprise made a profit or loss over the year, the farmer should examine the','[{"id": "a", "text": "financial (income and expenditure) record"}, {"id": "b", "text": "brooding record"}, {"id": "c", "text": "pedigree record"}, {"id": "d", "text": "housing plan"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "The financial record compares income and expenditure to show profit or loss."}',0.55,'{SSS3,LVF,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','The photovoltaic effect describes the direct conversion of sunlight into which form of energy?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Heat energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Electrical energy"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Chemical energy"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Mechanical energy"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "In the photovoltaic effect, solar cells convert sunlight directly into electrical energy."}',0.45,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','Most solar cells used in PV modules installed in Nigeria are made primarily from which material?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Copper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Aluminium"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Silicon"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Carbon"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Silicon is the semiconductor material used to manufacture most solar cells."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','A single crystalline solar cell typically produces an open-circuit voltage of about how much under standard test conditions?','[{"id": "a", "text": "0.5 to 0.6 volts"}, {"id": "b", "text": "1.5 volts"}, {"id": "c", "text": "12 volts"}, {"id": "d", "text": "24 volts"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "One silicon solar cell produces roughly 0.5 to 0.6 volts under standard conditions."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','Why do solar module manufacturers connect many cells in series inside one panel?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To reduce the panel weight"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To increase the output voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To change AC into DC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To store the electricity"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Connecting cells in series adds their voltages to reach a usable module voltage."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O1','Which region of Nigeria generally receives the highest annual solar irradiation, making it most favourable for PV systems?','[{"id": "a", "text": "The southern coastal zone"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The northern savanna zone"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The Niger Delta swamp zone"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The rainforest belt"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Northern Nigeria receives higher solar irradiation due to less cloud cover and lower humidity."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Which type of solar module is generally recognised by its uniform dark black cells and highest efficiency?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Polycrystalline"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monocrystalline"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Amorphous thin-film"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cadmium telluride"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Monocrystalline modules have uniform dark cells and the highest efficiency among common types."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Polycrystalline solar panels can usually be identified by which visual feature?','[{"id": "a", "text": "A blue speckled or fragmented appearance"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A completely transparent surface"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A flexible rubbery texture"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A bright red colour"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Polycrystalline cells show a blue, grainy, multi-crystal appearance."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','Which technology allows solar cells to be made flexible and lightweight but with lower efficiency?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Monocrystalline silicon"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Polycrystalline silicon"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Thin-film"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Concentrated PV"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Thin-film modules are flexible and lightweight but have lower efficiency than crystalline types."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','The power rating of a solar module printed on its nameplate is measured under Standard Test Conditions, which assume an irradiance of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "500 W/m²"}, {"id": "b", "text": "1000 W/m²"}, {"id": "c", "text": "1500 W/m²"}, {"id": "d", "text": "2000 W/m²"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Standard Test Conditions use 1000 W/m² irradiance at 25°C cell temperature."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T1','SPV-T1-O2','A protective transparent layer on the front of a crystalline PV module is usually made of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Plywood"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tempered glass"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Cardboard"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ordinary cloth"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Tempered glass protects the cells while allowing sunlight to pass through."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','What is the main function of a charge controller in a battery-based solar system?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To convert DC to AC"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To regulate charging and prevent battery overcharge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To increase panel voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To cool the inverter"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A charge controller regulates current to the battery and prevents overcharging."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','Which type of charge controller harvests more energy by adjusting to the panel''s optimum operating point?','[{"id": "a", "text": "PWM controller"}, {"id": "b", "text": "MPPT controller"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Manual switch"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Shunt resistor"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "MPPT (Maximum Power Point Tracking) controllers extract more energy than PWM types."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','In a solar home system, the inverter is used to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Convert DC electricity to AC for appliances"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Store energy for the night"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Generate sunlight"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Measure battery temperature"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An inverter converts DC from panels or batteries into AC used by household appliances."}',0.45,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','Which battery type is commonly recommended for deep, repeated discharge in solar installations?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Car starter battery"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Deep-cycle battery"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Dry cell torch battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Button cell"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Deep-cycle batteries are designed for repeated deep discharge in solar systems."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O1','A pure sine wave inverter is preferred over a modified sine wave inverter mainly because it:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Is always cheaper"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Runs sensitive appliances cleanly with less interference"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Needs no battery"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Produces DC output"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Pure sine wave output runs sensitive electronics cleanly with minimal interference."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','The ''Isc'' value on a solar module nameplate refers to the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Short-circuit current"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Open-circuit voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Maximum power point"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cell temperature"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Isc is the short-circuit current, the current when output terminals are shorted."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','The purpose of a blocking diode in a solar array is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Increase panel voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prevent battery current from flowing back into the panels at night"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Convert AC to DC"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Store extra charge"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A blocking diode stops reverse current draining the battery through the panels at night."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','A bypass diode fitted in a PV module helps to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Add more voltage to the array"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Allow current to flow around a shaded or faulty cell string"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charge the battery faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cool the panel surface"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Bypass diodes route current around shaded cells, reducing hot spots and losses."}',0.7,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','Which special connector is the industry standard for joining PV module cables outdoors?','[{"id": "a", "text": "MC4 connector"}, {"id": "b", "text": "RJ45 connector"}, {"id": "c", "text": "USB connector"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Banana plug"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "MC4 connectors are the weatherproof standard for PV module wiring."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T2','SPV-T2-O2','Why should PV cables used outdoors on rooftops be UV-resistant?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To increase their voltage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To prevent insulation breakdown from prolonged sunlight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To make them conduct better"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To reduce their length"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "UV-resistant insulation prevents cracking and failure from constant sun exposure."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Which instrument is used to measure the DC voltage output of a solar panel during testing?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Multimeter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Vernier caliper"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Spirit level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Micrometer screw gauge"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A multimeter measures voltage, current and resistance during PV testing."}',0.45,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','A crimping tool is used during PV installation to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cut metal roofing sheets"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Attach connectors firmly onto cable ends"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Measure sunlight intensity"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tighten roof bolts"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A crimping tool secures terminals and connectors onto cable conductors."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Which instrument is used to check that a mounting rail or panel is perfectly horizontal?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Spirit level"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Clamp meter"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hydrometer"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Soldering iron"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A spirit level checks whether a surface is level or horizontal."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','A hydrometer is used in solar battery maintenance to measure the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cable thickness"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Specific gravity of the electrolyte"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Panel wattage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Roof angle"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "A hydrometer measures electrolyte specific gravity to check a battery''s state of charge."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O1','Which tool is most suitable for accurately setting the tilt angle of a solar array?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Inclinometer or protractor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Screwdriver"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hacksaw"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Pliers"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An inclinometer or protractor measures the tilt angle of the array."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','Before working on a solar array''s DC wiring, the installer should first:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cover the panels or isolate the DC circuit"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Pour water on the panels"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the tilt angle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Remove the roof sheets"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Covering panels or isolating the DC circuit stops current flow before working safely."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','Which personal protective equipment is essential when handling flooded lead-acid batteries?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Acid-resistant gloves and eye goggles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Sunglasses only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A raincoat"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Ear plugs only"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Acid-resistant gloves and goggles protect skin and eyes from battery acid."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','Why must a battery bank room be well ventilated?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To keep the battery colourful"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To disperse explosive hydrogen gas released during charging"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To increase panel output"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To dry the roof"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Charging batteries release hydrogen, which must be ventilated to avoid explosion risk."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','When working on a rooftop PV installation, the most important fall-protection measure is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Wear a safety harness secured to an anchor"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Work barefoot for better grip"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Remove all tools from the roof"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Install only at night"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A safety harness anchored to the roof prevents falls during rooftop work."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T3','SPV-T3-O2','A short circuit at a battery terminal is dangerous mainly because it can cause:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A very large current, sparks and possible fire"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The panel to lose colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The inverter to speed up"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The sun to dim"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A shorted battery delivers a huge current that can cause burns, sparks and fire."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','The daily energy consumption of an appliance is best expressed in:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Watt-hours"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Ohms"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Farads"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Newtons"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Energy use per day equals power times hours, measured in watt-hours."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','A 100 W bulb runs for 5 hours a day. What is its daily energy consumption?','[{"id": "a", "text": "20 Wh"}, {"id": "b", "text": "105 Wh"}, {"id": "c", "text": "500 Wh"}, {"id": "d", "text": "5000 Wh"}]','{"correct": ["c"], "explanation": "Energy equals power times time: 100 W multiplied by 5 h gives 500 Wh."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','To supply a total load of 600 W using 150 W panels, how many panels are needed at minimum?','[{"id": "a", "text": "2"}, {"id": "b", "text": "4"}, {"id": "c", "text": "6"}, {"id": "d", "text": "8"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "600 W divided by 150 W per panel equals 4 panels."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','The term ''peak sun hours'' used in system sizing represents:','[{"id": "a", "text": "The number of hours of equivalent full 1000 W/m² sunlight per day"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The hottest hour of the day only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The total daylight hours including dawn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The number of panels on a roof"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Peak sun hours express daily solar energy as equivalent hours of full 1000 W/m² sunlight."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O1','Increasing the battery bank capacity in a solar system mainly provides:','[{"id": "a", "text": "More days of backup (autonomy)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Higher panel voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Faster inverter cooling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Reduced cable length"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A larger battery bank stores more energy, giving more days of autonomy."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','For a fixed solar array in Nigeria, panels are generally tilted and oriented to face which direction for best year-round output?','[{"id": "a", "text": "North"}, {"id": "b", "text": "South"}, {"id": "c", "text": "West"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Straight down"}]','{"correct": ["b"], "explanation": "Being north of the equator, Nigerian fixed arrays face south for best annual output."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','Connecting two identical panels in series will:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Double the voltage while current stays the same"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Double the current while voltage stays the same"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Halve both voltage and current"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Change DC to AC"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Series connection adds voltages while the current remains the same."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','Connecting two identical panels in parallel will:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Add their currents while voltage stays the same"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Add their voltages while current stays the same"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reduce the total power to zero"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Convert the output to AC"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Parallel connection adds currents while the voltage stays the same."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','A slight tilt is given to roof-mounted panels partly so that:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Rainwater can run off and self-clean dust"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The panels weigh less"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The voltage increases automatically"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The battery charges at night"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A tilt lets rain drain and wash away dust, keeping the panels clean."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T4','SPV-T4-O2','Why should a gap be left between roof-mounted panels and the roof surface?','[{"id": "a", "text": "To allow air flow that cools the panels"}, {"id": "b", "text": "To store rainwater"}, {"id": "c", "text": "To reduce the panel voltage"}, {"id": "d", "text": "To hide the cables from the sun"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "An air gap cools the panels, since high temperature lowers PV efficiency."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','The most common routine maintenance task that keeps PV output high in dusty Nigerian environments is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Cleaning dust from the panel surface"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Repainting the roof"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Replacing the inverter monthly"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Increasing the battery voltage"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Dust and dirt block sunlight, so regular cleaning maintains output."}',0.45,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','Routine maintenance of a flooded lead-acid battery includes:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Topping up with distilled water to the correct level"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Adding petrol to the cells"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Painting the terminals"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wrapping it in cloth"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Distilled water is added to keep the electrolyte at the correct level."}',0.5,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','White or greenish powdery deposits on battery terminals are a sign of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Terminal corrosion"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Full charge"}, {"id": "c", "text": "High efficiency"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Correct wiring"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Powdery deposits indicate terminal corrosion that increases resistance."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','During periodic inspection, PV connectors and terminals should be checked mainly for:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Looseness and overheating signs"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Correct colour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Their brand name"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The date of manufacture"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Loose or hot connections cause power loss and fire risk, so they are checked."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O1','Partial shading of even one panel in a series string is a maintenance concern because it can:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Reduce the output of the whole string"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increase the string voltage"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charge the battery faster"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cool the inverter"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A shaded panel limits the current for the whole series string, cutting output."}',0.65,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A solar system stops powering AC appliances although the panels and battery are good. The most likely faulty component is the:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Inverter"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Mounting rail"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Panel glass"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Roof bolt"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "AC appliances rely on the inverter, so a faulty inverter stops AC supply."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A panel reads normal open-circuit voltage but delivers almost no current on load. This suggests:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A poor or high-resistance connection or damaged cell string"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The battery is fully charged"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The inverter is oversized"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The tilt angle is perfect"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Normal voltage but no current points to high-resistance connections or cell damage."}',0.7,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','If a battery no longer holds charge and discharges very quickly, the correct action is usually to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Test it and replace it if it has failed"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Add more panels only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increase the tilt angle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Paint the terminals"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A battery that will not hold charge should be tested and replaced if failed."}',0.55,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','A charge controller shows the battery as full during the day but appliances fail at night. A likely cause is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "A weak battery that cannot store enough energy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Too much sunlight"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The panel facing south"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Clean panel glass"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "A weak battery may read full yet fail to store real energy for night use."}',0.7,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}'),
  ('SSS3','SPV','SPV-T5','SPV-T5-O2','When diagnosing a dead PV system, the safest logical first step is to:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Systematically check connections and measure voltages stage by stage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Replace every component at once"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pour water on the panels"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Remove the roof"}]','{"correct": ["a"], "explanation": "Systematic stage-by-stage checking isolates the fault safely and cheaply."}',0.6,'{SSS3,SPV,WASSCE,NECO,nerdc-quiz-seed-v3}')
) AS v(class_code, subj_code, topic_code, obj_code, stem, options, answer, difficulty, tags)
JOIN public.academy_curriculum_versions ver ON ver.code='NERDC-2025'
JOIN public.academy_classes c ON c.version_id=ver.id AND c.code=v.class_code
JOIN public.academy_subjects s ON s.class_id=c.id AND s.code=v.subj_code
JOIN public.academy_topics t ON t.subject_id=s.id AND t.code=v.topic_code
JOIN public.academy_learning_objectives o ON o.topic_id=t.id AND o.code=v.obj_code
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.academy_question_items q WHERE q.tags @> ARRAY['nerdc-quiz-seed-v3']);

COMMIT;
